ticipating more actively than in the training their companies provide."}, {"name": "~때문이다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Causal expression meaning ''because of; due to''. Follows noun (with 의 if needed) to indicate reason/cause.", "ex_ko": "전문가들은 이런 현상이 취업 시장의 변화 때문이라고 분석했어요.", "ex_en": "Experts analyzed that this phenomenon was due to changes in the job market."}, {"name": "~라고 분석하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Quotative particle ~라고 with verb of saying/analysis. Reports indirect speech or analysis results.", "ex_ko": "전문가들은 이런 현상이 취업 시장의 변화 때문이라고 분석했어요.", "ex_en": "Experts analyzed that this phenomenon was due to changes in the job market."}, {"name": "~기 위해", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Purpose/intention marker. Follows verb stem to indicate goal or objective of the main action.", "ex_ko": "직장인들은 미래를 준비하기 위해 스스로 공부하고 있어요.", "ex_en": "Office workers are studying by themselves in order to prepare for the future."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mogepo38afq2' and md5(translation) = '21911074af2c558713941cbe83769ee8';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["There was a peaceful walk in an apartment complex in Seoul. The weather was really nice today.", "The blue sky and tall buildings create a wonderful sight. Seoul''s apartments are built very high, reaching toward the sky.", "Many people like this view of Seoul. It is a landscape where the city and nature blend together nicely.", "In Seoul, you can often see such peaceful afternoons. It''s also nice to spend the day walking through the apartment complex."], "sentences": [{"text": "서울의 한 아파트 단지에서 평화로운 산책이 있었어요.", "translation": "There was a peaceful walk in an apartment complex in Seoul.", "vocab": [{"ko": "아파트", "en": "apartment"}, {"ko": "단지", "en": "complex; site"}, {"ko": "평화롭다", "en": "to be peaceful"}, {"ko": "산책", "en": "walk; stroll"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서 (location of action)", "exp": "Particle marking where an action or event takes place. Attaches to location nouns.", "example_in_sentence": "아파트 단지에서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past tense)", "exp": "Past tense marker for regular past events. 있다 (to exist/be) → 있었어요 (was/existed).", "example_in_sentence": "있었어요"}]}, {"text": "오늘은 날씨가 정말 좋았어요.", "translation": "The weather was really nice today.", "vocab": [{"ko": "오늘", "en": "today"}, {"ko": "날씨", "en": "weather"}, {"ko": "정말", "en": "really; very"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "exp": "Particle marking the topic of the sentence. 오늘 (today) + 은 → 오늘은.", "example_in_sentence": "오늘은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 (subject marker)", "exp": "Particle marking the subject. 날씨 (weather) + 가 → 날씨가.", "example_in_sentence": "날씨가"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past tense)", "exp": "Past tense marker. 좋다 (to be good) → 좋았어요 (was good).", "example_in_sentence": "좋았어요"}]}, {"text": "파란 하늘과 높은 건물들이 멋진 모습을 만들어요.", "translation": "The blue sky and tall buildings make a wonderful scene.", "vocab": [{"ko": "파랗다", "en": "to be blue"}, {"ko": "하늘", "en": "sky"}, {"ko": "높다", "en": "to be tall; high"}, {"ko": "건물", "en": "building"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~과/와 (conjunction)", "exp": "Particle joining two nouns. 하늘 (sky) + 과 → 하늘과.", "example_in_sentence": "하늘과"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 (subject marker)", "exp": "Particle marking the subject. 건물들 (buildings) + 이 → 건물들이.", "example_in_sentence": "건물들이"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 (object marker)", "exp": "Particle marking the direct object. 모습 (appearance) + 을 → 모습을.", "example_in_sentence": "모습을"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "멋진 모습을 만들다", "exp": "Collocation meaning ''to create/make a wonderful appearance.'' 만들다 pairs with 모습 as the object.", "example_in_sentence": "멋진 모습을 만들어요"}]}, {"text": "서울의 아파트들은 하늘까지 높게 지어져 있어요.", "translation": "Apartments in Seoul are built as high as the sky.", "vocab": [{"ko": "지어지다", "en": "to be built"}, {"ko": "높다", "en": "to be high; tall"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~까지 (up to; as far as)", "exp": "Particle marking extent or limit. 하늘 (sky) + 까지 → 하늘까지 (up to the sky).", "example_in_sentence": "하늘까지"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어지다 (passive/state change)", "exp": "Auxiliary verb forming passive or stative meaning. 짓다 (to build) → 지어지다 (to be built).", "example_in_sentence": "지어져"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~어 있다 (resultant state)", "exp": "Structure expressing a state resulting from a prior action. 지어져 (built) + 있어요 (is/exists) = are in a built state.", "example_in_sentence": "지어져 있어요"}]}, {"text": "많은 사람들이 이런 서울의 모습을 좋아해요.", "translation": "Many people like this appearance of Seoul.", "vocab": [{"ko": "많다", "en": "to be many; a lot"}, {"ko": "사람", "en": "person; people"}, {"ko": "이런", "en": "this kind of; such"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 (subject marker)", "exp": "Particle marking the subject. 사람들 (people) + 이 → 사람들이.", "example_in_sentence": "사람들이"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 (object marker)", "exp": "Particle marking the direct object. 모습 (appearance) + 을 → 모습을.", "example_in_sentence": "모습을"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~을/를 좋아하다", "exp": "Collocation meaning ''to like/prefer.'' 좋아하다 takes the object with ~을/를.", "example_in_sentence": "모습을 좋아해요"}]}, {"text": "도시와 자연이 함께 어우러진 풍경이에요.", "translation": "It is a landscape where city and nature blend together.", "vocab": [{"ko": "도시", "en": "city"}, {"ko": "자연", "en": "nature"}, {"ko": "어우러지다", "en": "to blend; to harmonize"}, {"ko": "풍경", "en": "landscape; scenery"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~과/와 (conjunction)", "exp": "Particle joining two nouns. 도시 (city) + 와 → 도시와.", "example_in_sentence": "도시와"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "exp": "describes a noun with a completed action. 어우러지다 → 어우러진 풍경 = \"a scene where (things) blend together\".", "example_in_sentence": "어우러진 풍경"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이에요 (is)", "exp": "polite \"to be\" after a noun ending in a consonant. 풍경 → 풍경이에요 = \"it is a scene\".", "example_in_sentence": "풍경이에요"}]}, {"text": "서울에서는 이런 평온한 오후를 자주 볼 수 있어요.", "translation": "In Seoul, one can often see such peaceful afternoons.", "vocab": [{"ko": "평온하다", "en": "to be peaceful; calm"}, {"ko": "오후", "en": "afternoon"}, {"ko": "자주", "en": "often; frequently"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서는 (in; at; from)", "exp": "Location particle with topic marker. 서울 (Seoul) + 에서는 (in Seoul, as for Seoul).", "example_in_sentence": "서울에서는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 (object marker)", "exp": "Particle marking the direct object. 오후 (afternoon) + 를 → 오후를.", "example_in_sentence": "오후를"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다 (can)", "exp": "ability or possibility. 보다 → 볼 수 있어요 = \"can see\".", "example_in_sentence": "볼 수 있어요"}]}, {"text": "아파트 단지를 걸으며 하루를 보내는 것도 좋아요.", "translation": "It is also nice to spend a day walking through the apartment complex.", "vocab": [{"ko": "걷다", "en": "to walk"}, {"ko": "하루", "en": "one day; a day"}, {"ko": "보내다", "en": "to spend (time)"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 (object marker)", "exp": "Particle marking the direct object. 단지 (complex) + 를 → 단지를.", "example_in_sentence": "단지를"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)며 (while)", "exp": "doing two things at once. 걷다 → 걸으며 (ㄷ changes to ㄹ) = \"while walking\".", "example_in_sentence": "걸으며"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 것 (nominalization)", "exp": "Nominalizing a clause into a noun phrase. 보내다 → 보내는 것 (the act of spending).", "example_in_sentence": "보내는 것"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~도 (also; too)", "exp": "Particle adding an additional item or fact. 것 (thing) + 도 → 것도 (also/too).", "example_in_sentence": "것도"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "아파트", "en": "apartment", "note": ""}, {"ko": "단지", "en": "complex; site", "note": ""}, {"ko": "평화롭다", "en": "to be peaceful", "note": ""}, {"ko": "산책", "en": "walk; stroll", "note": ""}, {"ko": "오늘", "en": "today", "note": ""}, {"ko": "날씨", "en": "weather", "note": ""}, {"ko": "정말", "en": "really; very", "note": ""}, {"ko": "파랗다", "en": "to be blue", "note": ""}, {"ko": "하늘", "en": "sky", "note": ""}, {"ko": "높다", "en": "to be tall; high", "note": ""}, {"ko": "건물", "en": "building", "note": ""}, {"ko": "지어지다", "en": "to be built", "note": ""}, {"ko": "많다", "en": "to be many; a lot", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사람", "en": "person; people", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이런", "en": "this kind of; such", "note": ""}, {"ko": "도시", "en": "city", "note": ""}, {"ko": "자연", "en": "nature", "note": ""}, {"ko": "어우러지다", "en": "to blend; to harmonize", "note": ""}, {"ko": "풍경", "en": "landscape; scenery", "note": ""}, {"ko": "평온하다", "en": "to be peaceful; calm", "note": ""}, {"ko": "오후", "en": "afternoon", "note": ""}, {"ko": "자주", "en": "often; frequently", "note": ""}, {"ko": "걷다", "en": "to walk", "note": ""}, {"ko": "하루", "en": "one day; a day", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보내다", "en": "to spend (time)", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~에서 (location of action)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Particle marking where an action or event takes place. Attaches to location nouns.", "ex_ko": "서울의 한 아파트 단지에서 평화로운 산책이 있었어요.", "ex_en": "There was a peaceful walk in an apartment complex in Seoul."}, {"name": "~았/었어요 (past tense)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Past tense marker for regular past events. 있다 (to exist/be) → 있었어요 (was/existed).", "ex_ko": "서울의 한 아파트 단지에서 평화로운 산책이 있었어요.", "ex_en": "There was a peaceful walk in an apartment complex in Seoul."}, {"name": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Particle marking the topic of the sentence. 오늘 (today) + 은 → 오늘은.", "ex_ko": "오늘은 날씨가 정말 좋았어요.", "ex_en": "The weather was really nice today."}, {"name": "~이/가 (subject marker)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Particle marking the subject. 건물들 (buildings) + 이 → 건물들이.", "ex_ko": "오늘은 날씨가 정말 좋았어요.", "ex_en": "The weather was really nice today."}, {"name": "~과/와 (conjunction)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Particle joining two nouns. 도시 (city) + 와 → 도시와.", "ex_ko": "파란 하늘과 높은 건물들이 멋진 모습을 만들어요.", "ex_en": "The blue sky and tall buildings make a wonderful scene."}, {"name": "~을/를 (object marker)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Particle marking the direct object. 모습 (appearance) + 을 → 모습을.", "ex_ko": "파란 하늘과 높은 건물들이 멋진 모습을 만들어요.", "ex_en": "The blue sky and tall buildings make a wonderful scene."}, {"name": "~까지 (up to; as far as)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Particle marking extent or limit. 하늘 (sky) + 까지 → 하늘까지 (up to the sky).", "ex_ko": "서울의 아파트들은 하늘까지 높게 지어져 있어요.", "ex_en": "Apartments in Seoul are built as high as the sky."}, {"name": "~아/어지다 (passive/state change)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Auxiliary verb forming passive or stative meaning. 짓다 (to build) → 지어지다 (to be built).", "ex_ko": "서울의 아파트들은 하늘까지 높게 지어져 있어요.", "ex_en": "Apartments in Seoul are built as high as the sky."}, {"name": "~어 있다 (resultant state)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Structure expressing a state resulting from a prior action. 지어져 (built) + 있어요 (is/exists) = are in a built state.", "ex_ko": "서울의 아파트들은 하늘까지 높게 지어져 있어요.", "ex_en": "Apartments in Seoul are built as high as the sky."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "describes a noun with a completed action. 어우러지다 → 어우러진 풍경 = \"a scene where (things) blend together\".", "ex_ko": "도시와 자연이 함께 어우러진 풍경이에요.", "ex_en": "It is a landscape where city and nature blend together."}, {"name": "~이에요 (is)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "polite \"to be\" after a noun ending in a consonant. 풍경 → 풍경이에요 = \"it is a scene\".", "ex_ko": "도시와 자연이 함께 어우러진 풍경이에요.", "ex_en": "It is a landscape where city and nature blend together."}, {"name": "~에서는 (in; at; from)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Location particle with topic marker. 서울 (Seoul) + 에서는 (in Seoul, as for Seoul).", "ex_ko": "서울에서는 이런 평온한 오후를 자주 볼 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "In Seoul, one can often see such peaceful afternoons."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다 (can)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "ability or possibility. 보다 → 볼 수 있어요 = \"can see\".", "ex_ko": "서울에서는 이런 평온한 오후를 자주 볼 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "In Seoul, one can often see such peaceful afternoons."}, {"name": "~(으)며 (while)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "doing two things at once. 걷다 → 걸으며 (ㄷ changes to ㄹ) = \"while walking\".", "ex_ko": "아파트 단지를 걸으며 하루를 보내는 것도 좋아요.", "ex_en": "It is also nice to spend a day walking through the apartment complex."}, {"name": "~는 것 (nominalization)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Nominalizing a clause into a noun phrase. 보내다 → 보내는 것 (the act of spending).", "ex_ko": "아파트 단지를 걸으며 하루를 보내는 것도 좋아요.", "ex_en": "It is also nice to spend a day walking through the apartment complex."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mogeqcdktbco' and md5(translation) = '6be2fcf5c24dca89dfbc05af51dd9bb5';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["An Iranian court sentenced 3 women to death for participating in protests in January this year. They were arrested after participating in protest activities against government policies.", "The Iranian government announced that the protest participants are ''criminals who threaten national security.'' However, international human rights organizations are strongly criticizing this ruling.", "The United Nations (UN) and several countries have demanded that the Iranian government stop the execution. In particular, they emphasized that women''s freedom of expression (the right to speak opinions freely) should be guaranteed.", "The Korean government also expressed its concern about the human rights situation in Iran. It is expected that the international community will continue to pressure the Iranian government."], "sentences": [{"text": "이란 법원이 올해 1월 시위에 참여한 여성 3명에게 사형을 선고했어요.", "translation": "Iran''s court sentenced three women who participated in a protest in January this year to death.", "vocab": [{"ko": "법원", "en": "court"}, {"ko": "시위", "en": "protest"}, {"ko": "사형", "en": "death sentence"}, {"ko": "선고하다", "en": "to sentence"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past noun modifier)", "exp": "Describes the noun with a completed action. 참여하다 → 참여한 여성 = women who took part.", "example_in_sentence": "시위에 참여한 여성"}]}, {"text": "이들은 정부 정책에 반대하는 시위 활동에 참여했다가 체포되었습니다.", "translation": "They participated in protest activities opposing government policies and were then arrested.", "vocab": [{"ko": "정책", "en": "policy"}, {"ko": "반대하다", "en": "to oppose"}, {"ko": "체포되다", "en": "to be arrested"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (present noun modifier)", "exp": "Describes the noun with an action or ongoing fact. 반대하다 → 반대하는 시위 활동 = protest activities opposing (policies).", "example_in_sentence": "반대하는 시위 활동"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었다가 (did ~ and then)", "exp": "Shows that one action was followed by a different, often unexpected one. 참여했다가 체포되었다 = took part and then were arrested.", "example_in_sentence": "참여했다가 체포되었습니다"}]}, {"text": "이란 정부는 시위 참여자들을 ''국가 안보를 위협하는 범죄자''라고 발표했어요.", "translation": "The Iranian government announced that protest participants are ''criminals threatening national security.''", "vocab": [{"ko": "안보", "en": "security"}, {"ko": "위협하다", "en": "to threaten"}, {"ko": "범죄자", "en": "criminal"}, {"ko": "발표하다", "en": "to announce"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (present relative clause modifier)", "exp": "Modifies the noun 범죄자. 위협하다 → 위협하는.", "example_in_sentence": "국가 안보를 위협하는 범죄자"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(이)라고 (quoting: ''as / that'')", "exp": "Quotes a description or label someone gives. 범죄자라고 발표했어요 = announced (them) as criminals.", "example_in_sentence": "''국가 안보를 위협하는 범죄자''라고 발표했어요"}]}, {"text": "하지만 국제 인권 단체들은 이번 판결을 강하게 비판하고 있습니다.", "translation": "However, international human rights organizations are strongly criticizing this verdict.", "vocab": [{"ko": "인권", "en": "human rights"}, {"ko": "단체", "en": "organization"}, {"ko": "판결", "en": "verdict / judgment"}, {"ko": "비판하다", "en": "to criticize"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다 (progressive aspect)", "exp": "Indicates an ongoing or continuous action. 비판하다 → 비판하고 있습니다.", "example_in_sentence": "비판하고 있습니다"}]}, {"text": "유엔(UN)과 여러 나라들이 이란 정부에 사형 집행을 중단하라고 요구했어요.", "translation": "The UN and several countries demanded that the Iranian government stop carrying out the executions.", "vocab": [{"ko": "유엔", "en": "UN / United Nations"}, {"ko": "여러", "en": "several / various"}, {"ko": "사형", "en": "death sentence"}, {"ko": "집행하다", "en": "to execute / to carry out"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에 (to — with groups and institutions)", "exp": "Marks who a demand is made to. With organizations like a government, 에 is used instead of 에게. 정부에 요구하다 = to demand of the government.", "example_in_sentence": "정부에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)라고 (quoting a command)", "exp": "Quotes an order or demand. 중단하다 → 중단하라고 요구하다 = to demand that (they) stop.", "example_in_sentence": "중단하라고 요구했어요"}]}, {"text": "특히 여성의 표현의 자유(의견을 자유롭게 말할 권리)를 보장해야 한다고 강조했습니다.", "translation": "They especially emphasized that the freedom of expression for women (the right to speak opinions freely) must be guaranteed.", "vocab": [{"ko": "표현", "en": "expression"}, {"ko": "자유", "en": "freedom"}, {"ko": "권리", "en": "right"}, {"ko": "보장하다", "en": "to guarantee"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어야 하다 (must)", "exp": "Expresses necessity or obligation. 보장하다 → 보장해야 한다 = must guarantee.", "example_in_sentence": "보장해야 한다"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~다고 (quotative: reported speech/content)", "exp": "Marks the content of speech or emphasis. 보장해야 한다고 강조 = emphasized that [it] must be guaranteed.", "example_in_sentence": "보장해야 한다고 강조했습니다"}]}, {"text": "한국 정부도 이란의 인권 상황을 우려한다는 입장을 밝혔어요.", "translation": "The Korean government also expressed its position of concern about Iran''s human rights situation.", "vocab": [{"ko": "인권", "en": "human rights"}, {"ko": "상황", "en": "situation"}, {"ko": "우려하다", "en": "to be concerned / to worry"}, {"ko": "입장", "en": "position / stance"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/는다는 + noun (the ~ that ...)", "exp": "Turns a statement into a description of the noun that follows. 우려한다 → 우려한다는 입장 = a position that it is concerned.", "example_in_sentence": "우려한다는 입장"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~에 대해 우려하다 / ~을/를 우려하다 (to express concern about ~)", "exp": "Collocational expression indicating worry or concern about a matter.", "example_in_sentence": "인권 상황을 우려한다"}]}, {"text": "국제사회가 이란 정부에 지속적으로 압력을 가할 것으로 예상됩니다.", "translation": "It is expected that the international community will continuously apply pressure to the Iranian government.", "vocab": [{"ko": "국제사회", "en": "international community"}, {"ko": "지속적", "en": "continuous / sustained"}, {"ko": "압력", "en": "pressure"}, {"ko": "예상되다", "en": "to be expected"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 것으로 예상되다 (is expected to ~)", "exp": "A formal way to state a prediction. 가하다 → 가할 것으로 예상됩니다 = (it) is expected to apply.", "example_in_sentence": "가할 것으로 예상됩니다"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~에 압력을 가하다 (to put pressure on ~)", "exp": "Collocational expression meaning to exert pressure or influence on someone/something.", "example_in_sentence": "정부에 지속적으로 압력을 가할"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "법원", "en": "court", "note": ""}, {"ko": "시위", "en": "protest", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사형", "en": "death sentence", "note": ""}, {"ko": "선고하다", "en": "to sentence", "note": ""}, {"ko": "정책", "en": "policy", "note": ""}, {"ko": "반대하다", "en": "to oppose", "note": ""}, {"ko": "체포되다", "en": "to be arrested", "note": ""}, {"ko": "안보", "en": "security", "note": ""}, {"ko": "위협하다", "en": "to threaten", "note": ""}, {"ko": "범죄자", "en": "criminal", "note": ""}, {"ko": "발표하다", "en": "to announce", "note": ""}, {"ko": "인권", "en": "human rights", "note": ""}, {"ko": "단체", "en": "organization", "note": ""}, {"ko": "판결", "en": "verdict / judgment", "note": ""}, {"ko": "비판하다", "en": "to criticize", "note": ""}, {"ko": "유엔", "en": "UN / United Nations", "note": ""}, {"ko": "여러", "en": "several / various", "note": ""}, {"ko": "집행하다", "en": "to execute / to carry out", "note": ""}, {"ko": "표현", "en": "expression", "note": ""}, {"ko": "자유", "en": "freedom", "note": ""}, {"ko": "권리", "en": "right", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보장하다", "en": "to guarantee", "note": ""}, {"ko": "상황", "en": "situation", "note": ""}, {"ko": "우려하다", "en": "to be concerned / to worry", "note": ""}, {"ko": "입장", "en": "position / stance", "note": ""}, {"ko": "국제사회", "en": "international community", "note": ""}, {"ko": "지속적", "en": "continuous / sustained", "note": ""}, {"ko": "압력", "en": "pressure", "note": ""}, {"ko": "예상되다", "en": "to be expected", "note": ""}, {"word": "지속적으로", "reading": "jisok-jeog-euro", "meaning": "continuously; persistently", "context": "지속적으로 압력을 가할 것으로 예상"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~(으)ㄴ (past noun modifier)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Describes the noun with a completed action. 참여하다 → 참여한 여성 = women who took part.", "ex_ko": "이란 법원이 올해 1월 시위에 참여한 여성 3명에게 사형을 선고했어요.", "ex_en": "Iran''s court sentenced three women who participated in a protest in January this year to death."}, {"name": "~는 (present relative clause modifier)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Describes the noun with an action or ongoing fact. 반대하다 → 반대하는 시위 활동 = protest activities opposing (policies).", "ex_ko": "이들은 정부 정책에 반대하는 시위 활동에 참여했다가 체포되었습니다.", "ex_en": "They participated in protest activities opposing government policies and were then arrested."}, {"name": "~았/었다가 (did ~ and then)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Shows that one action was followed by a different, often unexpected one. 참여했다가 체포되었다 = took part and then were arrested.", "ex_ko": "이들은 정부 정책에 반대하는 시위 활동에 참여했다가 체포되었습니다.", "ex_en": "They participated in protest activities opposing government policies and were then arrested."}, {"name": "~(이)라고 (quoting: ''as / that'')", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Quotes a description or label someone gives. 범죄자라고 발표했어요 = announced (them) as criminals.", "ex_ko": "이란 정부는 시위 참여자들을 ''국가 안보를 위협하는 범죄자''라고 발표했어요.", "ex_en": "The Iranian government announced that protest participants are ''criminals threatening national security.''"}, {"name": "~고 있다 (progressive aspect)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Indicates an ongoing or continuous action. 비판하다 → 비판하고 있습니다.", "ex_ko": "하지만 국제 인권 단체들은 이번 판결을 강하게 비판하고 있습니다.", "ex_en": "However, international human rights organizations are strongly criticizing this verdict."}, {"name": "~에 (to — with groups and institutions)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Marks who a demand is made to. With organizations like a government, 에 is used instead of 에게. 정부에 요구하다 = to demand of the government.", "ex_ko": "유엔(UN)과 여러 나라들이 이란 정부에 사형 집행을 중단하라고 요구했어요.", "ex_en": "The UN and several countries demanded that the Iranian government stop carrying out the executions."}, {"name": "~(으)라고 (quoting a command)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Quotes an order or demand. 중단하다 → 중단하라고 요구하다 = to demand that (they) stop.", "ex_ko": "유엔(UN)과 여러 나라들이 이란 정부에 사형 집행을 중단하라고 요구했어요.", "ex_en": "The UN and several countries demanded that the Iranian government stop carrying out the executions."}, {"name": "~아/어야 하다 (must)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Expresses necessity or obligation. 보장하다 → 보장해야 한다 = must guarantee.", "ex_ko": "특히 여성의 표현의 자유(의견을 자유롭게 말할 권리)를 보장해야 한다고 강조했습니다.", "ex_en": "They especially emphasized that the freedom of expression for women (the right to speak opinions freely) must be guaranteed."}, {"name": "~다고 (quotative: reported speech/content)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Marks the content of speech or emphasis. 보장해야 한다고 강조 = emphasized that [it] must be guaranteed.", "ex_ko": "특히 여성의 표현의 자유(의견을 자유롭게 말할 권리)를 보장해야 한다고 강조했습니다.", "ex_en": "They especially emphasized that the freedom of expression for women (the right to speak opinions freely) must be guaranteed."}, {"name": "~ㄴ/는다는 + noun (the ~ that ...)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Turns a statement into a description of the noun that follows. 우려한다 → 우려한다는 입장 = a position that it is concerned.", "ex_ko": "한국 정부도 이란의 인권 상황을 우려한다는 입장을 밝혔어요.", "ex_en": "The Korean government also expressed its position of concern about Iran''s human rights situation."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 것으로 예상되다 (is expected to ~)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "A formal way to state a prediction. 가하다 → 가할 것으로 예상됩니다 = (it) is expected to apply.", "ex_ko": "국제사회가 이란 정부에 지속적으로 압력을 가할 것으로 예상됩니다.", "ex_en": "It is expected that the international community will continuously apply pressure to the Iranian government."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'moh0g4bsfk23' and md5(translation) = 'c47ba0538804d3cdd513b86a5644da2f';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["Research has shown that the period during which people in the UK live healthily has become shorter than it was 10 years ago. This is becoming an important issue for the UK''s health system and society as a whole.", "According to the research, while the overall life expectancy of British people has increased, the period of living healthily without disease has actually decreased. This means that more people are suffering from illness for longer periods of time.", "Experts are pointing to worsening lifestyle habits and environmental changes as the causes of this phenomenon. In particular, increased stress, lack of exercise, and poor eating habits are being analyzed as major causes.", "South Korea is also receiving attention as it may face similar problems. Maintaining healthy living habits has become more important than ever."], "sentences": [{"text": "영국에서 사람들이 건강하게 사는 기간이 10년 전보다 짧아졌다는 연구 결과가 나왔어요.", "translation": "Research results have come out showing that the period during which people in Britain live healthily has become shorter than 10 years ago.", "vocab": [{"ko": "기간", "en": "period; duration"}, {"ko": "짧아지다", "en": "become short; shorten"}, {"ko": "연구 결과", "en": "research result; finding"}, {"ko": "나오다", "en": "come out; emerge"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었다는 + noun (the ~ that ...)", "exp": "Turns a statement into the content of the noun that follows. 짧아지다 → 짧아졌다는 연구 결과 = a study finding that (it) has become shorter.", "example_in_sentence": "짧아졌다는 연구 결과"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~보다 (than)", "exp": "Marks what something is compared with. 10년 전보다 짧아졌다 = became shorter than 10 years ago.", "example_in_sentence": "10년 전보다 짧아졌다"}]}, {"text": "이는 영국 보건 시스템과 사회 전반에 중요한 문제가 되고 있습니다.", "translation": "This is becoming an important issue for the British healthcare system and society as a whole.", "vocab": [{"ko": "보건 시스템", "en": "healthcare system"}, {"ko": "사회 전반", "en": "society as a whole; overall society"}, {"ko": "중요하다", "en": "to be important"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다", "exp": "Progressive aspect marker. Indicates ongoing or current state. 되다 (become) + -고 있다 = ''is becoming''.", "example_in_sentence": "되고 있습니다"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~이/가 되다 (to become ~)", "exp": "Noun + 이/가 되다 means to become something. 문제가 되다 = to become a problem.", "example_in_sentence": "중요한 문제가 되고"}]}, {"text": "연구에 따르면 영국인들의 전체 수명(기대수명)은 늘어났지만, 질병 없이 건강하게 지내는 기간은 오히려 줄어들었어요.", "translation": "According to research, while the overall lifespan (life expectancy) of British people has increased, the period during which they live healthily without disease has rather decreased.", "vocab": [{"ko": "수명", "en": "lifespan; life expectancy"}, {"ko": "늘어나다", "en": "increase; grow"}, {"ko": "줄어들다", "en": "decrease; diminish"}, {"ko": "오히려", "en": "on the contrary; rather"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~지만", "exp": "Contrastive connective joining two clauses. Indicates opposition or concession between 늘어났다 (increased) and 줄어들었다 (decreased).", "example_in_sentence": "늘어났지만"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~에 따르면", "exp": "According to; based on. Indicates source of information (연구 = research). Source + 에 따르면.", "example_in_sentence": "연구에 따르면"}]}, {"text": "이것은 더 오랜 기간 동안 질병으로 고생하는 사람들이 많아졌다는 의미입니다.", "translation": "This means that more people have come to suffer from disease over longer periods.", "vocab": [{"ko": "오랜", "en": "long; lengthy"}, {"ko": "기간", "en": "period; duration"}, {"ko": "질병", "en": "disease; illness"}, {"ko": "고생하다", "en": "suffer; have difficulty"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~다는 의미이다 (it means that ~)", "exp": "Explains what a fact means. 많아지다 → 많아졌다는 의미입니다 = it means that (people) have increased.", "example_in_sentence": "많아졌다는 의미"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~(으)로 고생하다 (to suffer from ~)", "exp": "(으)로 marks the cause of the hardship. 질병으로 고생하다 = to suffer from illness.", "example_in_sentence": "질병으로 고생하는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ 동안 (for, during)", "exp": "Follows a length of time to mean ''for'' or ''during''. 오랜 기간 동안 = for a long period.", "example_in_sentence": "더 오랜 기간 동안"}]}, {"text": "전문가들은 이런 현상의 원인으로 생활 습관 악화와 환경 변화를 꼽고 있어요.", "translation": "Experts point to lifestyle deterioration and environmental change as the causes of such phenomena.", "vocab": [{"ko": "전문가", "en": "expert; specialist"}, {"ko": "현상", "en": "phenomenon; occurrence"}, {"ko": "습관", "en": "habit; custom"}, {"ko": "악화", "en": "deterioration; worsening"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다", "exp": "Progressive aspect. Marks ongoing action or habitual state. 꼽다 (point to) + -고 있다 = ''are pointing''.", "example_in_sentence": "꼽고 있어요"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~을/를 ~(으)로 꼽다 (to name A as B)", "exp": "To single something out as a main example. ...를 원인으로 꼽다 = to name ... as the cause.", "example_in_sentence": "원인으로 생활 습관 악화와 환경 변화를 꼽고"}]}, {"text": "특히 스트레스 증가와 운동 부족, 잘못된 식습관이 주요 원인으로 분석되고 있습니다.", "translation": "In particular, increased stress, lack of exercise, and poor dietary habits are being analyzed as major causes.", "vocab": [{"ko": "특히", "en": "especially; in particular"}, {"ko": "스트레스", "en": "stress"}, {"ko": "운동 부족", "en": "lack of exercise"}, {"ko": "식습관", "en": "eating habit; dietary habit"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다", "exp": "Progressive aspect in passive voice. 분석되다 (be analyzed) + -고 있다 = ''are being analyzed'' (ongoing process).", "example_in_sentence": "분석되고 있습니다"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로 (as)", "exp": "Marks the role or status something is given. 주요 원인으로 분석되다 = to be analyzed as a major cause.", "example_in_sentence": "주요 원인으로"}]}, {"text": "한국도 비슷한 문제에 직면할 가능성이 있어 주목받고 있어요.", "translation": "Korea too is receiving attention as it has the possibility of facing similar problems.", "vocab": [{"ko": "비슷하다", "en": "to be similar"}, {"ko": "직면하다", "en": "face; confront"}, {"ko": "가능성", "en": "possibility; potential"}, {"ko": "주목받다", "en": "receive attention; attract notice"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 가능성이 있다 (there is a chance of ~)", "exp": "Says something may happen. 직면하다 → 직면할 가능성이 있다 = there is a chance of facing (it).", "example_in_sentence": "직면할 가능성이 있어"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다 (ongoing action)", "exp": "Shows an action or state that is ongoing now. 주목받다 → 주목받고 있어요 = is drawing attention.", "example_in_sentence": "주목받고 있어요"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~에 직면하다", "exp": "Face; confront; encounter. Problem/difficulty + 에 + 직면하다.", "example_in_sentence": "비슷한 문제에 직면할"}]}, {"text": "건강한 생활 습관을 유지하는 것이 그 어느 때보다 중요해졌습니다.", "translation": "Maintaining healthy living habits has become more important than ever.", "vocab": [{"ko": "생활 습관", "en": "living habit; lifestyle"}, {"ko": "유지하다", "en": "maintain; keep"}, {"ko": "중요하다", "en": "be important"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 것", "exp": "Nominalized clause. 유지하다 (maintain) + ~는 것 converts predicate into object noun (thing). Functions as subject of 중요해졌다.", "example_in_sentence": "유지하는 것이"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어지다", "exp": "Become; turn into. State-change auxiliary. 중요하다 (important) + -아/어지다 = ''has become/turned important''.", "example_in_sentence": "중요해졌습니다"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~보다 (그 어느 때보다)", "exp": "More than ~; compared to ~. Temporal comparative: ''more important than any other time''.", "example_in_sentence": "그 어느 때보다 중요해졌습니다"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "기간", "en": "period; duration", "note": ""}, {"ko": "짧아지다", "en": "become short; shorten", "note": ""}, {"ko": "연구 결과", "en": "research result; finding", "note": ""}, {"ko": "나오다", "en": "come out; emerge", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보건 시스템", "en": "healthcare system", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사회 전반", "en": "society as a whole; overall society", "note": ""}, {"ko": "중요하다", "en": "to be important", "note": ""}, {"ko": "수명", "en": "lifespan; life expectancy", "note": ""}, {"ko": "늘어나다", "en": "increase; grow", "note": ""}, {"ko": "줄어들다", "en": "decrease; diminish", "note": ""}, {"ko": "오히려", "en": "on the contrary; rather", "note": ""}, {"ko": "오랜", "en": "long; lengthy", "note": ""}, {"ko": "질병", "en": "disease; illness", "note": ""}, {"ko": "고생하다", "en": "suffer; have difficulty", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전문가", "en": "expert; specialist", "note": ""}, {"ko": "현상", "en": "phenomenon; occurrence", "note": ""}, {"ko": "습관", "en": "habit; custom", "note": ""}, {"ko": "악화", "en": "deterioration; worsening", "note": ""}, {"ko": "특히", "en": "especially; in particular", "note": ""}, {"ko": "스트레스", "en": "stress", "note": ""}, {"ko": "운동 부족", "en": "lack of exercise", "note": ""}, {"ko": "식습관", "en": "eating habit; dietary habit", "note": ""}, {"ko": "비슷하다", "en": "to be similar", "note": ""}, {"ko": "직면하다", "en": "face; confront", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가능성", "en": "possibility; potential", "note": ""}, {"ko": "주목받다", "en": "receive attention; attract notice", "note": ""}, {"ko": "생활 습관", "en": "living habit; lifestyle", "note": ""}, {"ko": "유지하다", "en": "maintain; keep", "note": ""}, {"word": "기대수명", "reading": "gidae-sumyeong", "meaning": "life expectancy", "context": "영국인들의 전체 수명(기대수명)은 늘어났지만"}, {"word": "원인", "reading": "won-in", "meaning": "cause; reason", "context": "전문가들은 이런 현상의 원인으로 생활 습관"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~았/었다는 + noun (the ~ that ...)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Turns a statement into the content of the noun that follows. 짧아지다 → 짧아졌다는 연구 결과 = a study finding that (it) has become shorter.", "ex_ko": "영국에서 사람들이 건강하게 사는 기간이 10년 전보다 짧아졌다는 연구 결과가 나왔어요.", "ex_en": "Research results have come out showing that the period during which people in Britain live healthily has become shorter than 10 years ago."}, {"name": "~고 있다 (ongoing action)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Progressive aspect in passive voice. 분석되다 (be analyzed) + -고 있다 = ''are being analyzed'' (ongoing process).", "ex_ko": "이는 영국 보건 시스템과 사회 전반에 중요한 문제가 되고 있습니다.", "ex_en": "This is becoming an important issue for the British healthcare system and society as a whole."}, {"name": "~지만", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Contrastive connective joining two clauses. Indicates opposition or concession between 늘어났다 (increased) and 줄어들었다 (decreased).", "ex_ko": "연구에 따르면 영국인들의 전체 수명(기대수명)은 늘어났지만, 질병 없이 건강하게 지내는 기간은 오히려 줄어들었어요.", "ex_en": "According to research, while the overall lifespan (life expectancy) of British people has increased, the period during which they live healthily without disease has rather decreased."}, {"name": "~다는 의미이다 (it means that ~)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Explains what a fact means. 많아지다 → 많아졌다는 의미입니다 = it means that (people) have increased.", "ex_ko": "이것은 더 오랜 기간 동안 질병으로 고생하는 사람들이 많아졌다는 의미입니다.", "ex_en": "This means that more people have come to suffer from disease over longer periods."}, {"name": "~ 동안 (for, during)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Follows a length of time to mean ''for'' or ''during''. 오랜 기간 동안 = for a long period.", "ex_ko": "이것은 더 오랜 기간 동안 질병으로 고생하는 사람들이 많아졌다는 의미입니다.", "ex_en": "This means that more people have come to suffer from disease over longer periods."}, {"name": "~(으)로 (as)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Marks the role or status something is given. 주요 원인으로 분석되다 = to be analyzed as a major cause.", "ex_ko": "특히 스트레스 증가와 운동 부족, 잘못된 식습관이 주요 원인으로 분석되고 있습니다.", "ex_en": "In particular, increased stress, lack of exercise, and poor dietary habits are being analyzed as major causes."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 가능성이 있다 (there is a chance of ~)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Says something may happen. 직면하다 → 직면할 가능성이 있다 = there is a chance of facing (it).", "ex_ko": "한국도 비슷한 문제에 직면할 가능성이 있어 주목받고 있어요.", "ex_en": "Korea too is receiving attention as it has the possibility of facing similar problems."}, {"name": "~는 것", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Nominalized clause. 유지하다 (maintain) + ~는 것 converts predicate into object noun (thing). Functions as subject of 중요해졌다.", "ex_ko": "건강한 생활 습관을 유지하는 것이 그 어느 때보다 중요해졌습니다.", "ex_en": "Maintaining healthy living habits has become more important than ever."}, {"name": "~아/어지다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Become; turn into. State-change auxiliary. 중요하다 (important) + -아/어지다 = ''has become/turned important''.", "ex_ko": "건강한 생활 습관을 유지하는 것이 그 어느 때보다 중요해졌습니다.", "ex_en": "Maintaining healthy living habits has become more important than ever."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'moh0gvildai3' and md5(translation) = '39ad1f8ff58ed00e10238cd1d6293f4f';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["A car bomb exploded outside a police station in Northern Ireland. This incident caused a significant shock to the surrounding area.", "Northern Ireland is a region where religious conflicts and political disputes have continued for a long time. The confrontation between Catholics and Protestants has lasted for decades. Peace has been maintained since the Good Friday Agreement in 1998.", "This bombing attack could negatively impact Northern Ireland''s peace process. Police and government authorities are investigating the perpetrators of the incident. Local residents are currently feeling anxiety again.", "The Korean government also takes a strong stance in condemning such terrorist attacks. The international community hopes that peace and stability in Northern Ireland will continue."], "sentences": [{"text": "북아일랜드의 한 경찰서 밖에서 차량 폭탄이 터지는 사건이 발생했습니다.", "translation": "An incident occurred in which a car bomb exploded outside a police station in Northern Ireland.", "vocab": [{"ko": "차량", "en": "vehicle"}, {"ko": "폭탄", "en": "bomb"}, {"ko": "터지다", "en": "to explode; to go off"}, {"ko": "발생하다", "en": "to occur; to happen"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 + noun (noun modifier)", "exp": "The clause describes the noun that follows. 터지다 → 터지는 사건 = an incident in which (a bomb) explodes.", "example_in_sentence": "터지는 사건"}]}, {"text": "이 사건으로 인해 주변 지역에 큰 충격이 일어났어요.", "translation": "Due to this incident, a major shock occurred in the surrounding area.", "vocab": [{"ko": "충격", "en": "shock; impact"}, {"ko": "일어나다", "en": "to occur; to arise"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~(으)로 인해 (due to)", "exp": "A formal way to give a cause. 이 사건으로 인해 = because of this incident.", "example_in_sentence": "이 사건으로 인해"}]}, {"text": "북아일랜드는 오랫동안 종교적 갈등과 정치적 분쟁이 계속된 지역입니다.", "translation": "Northern Ireland is a region where religious conflict and political dispute have persisted for a long time.", "vocab": [{"ko": "종교적", "en": "religious"}, {"ko": "갈등", "en": "conflict; discord"}, {"ko": "분쟁", "en": "dispute; strife"}, {"ko": "계속되다", "en": "to continue; to persist"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past noun modifier)", "exp": "Describes the noun with something that has happened. 계속되다 → 계속된 지역 = a region where (conflict) has continued.", "example_in_sentence": "계속된 지역"}]}, {"text": "가톨릭계와 개신교계 사이의 대립이 수십 년간 이어져 왔어요.", "translation": "The confrontation between Catholics and Protestants has continued for decades.", "vocab": [{"ko": "가톨릭계", "en": "Catholic community/side"}, {"ko": "개신교계", "en": "Protestant community/side"}, {"ko": "대립", "en": "confrontation; opposition"}, {"ko": "이어지다", "en": "to continue; to be connected"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "A와 B 사이의 (between A and B)", "exp": "사이 + 의 links ''between A and B'' to the noun that follows. 가톨릭계와 개신교계 사이의 대립 = the confrontation between Catholics and Protestants.", "example_in_sentence": "가톨릭계와 개신교계 사이의 대립"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어 왔다", "exp": "Continuous aspect auxiliary. Combines past participle 이어져 (이어지다→이어져) with 왔어요 to express action continuing from past to present.", "example_in_sentence": "이어져 왔어요"}]}, {"text": "1998년 성금요일 협정(굿 프라이데이 협정) 이후 평화가 유지되고 있었습니다.", "translation": "After the 1998 Good Friday Agreement, peace had been maintained.", "vocab": [{"ko": "협정", "en": "agreement; accord"}, {"ko": "유지되다", "en": "to be maintained"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~ 이후 (after, since)", "exp": "Marks the point in time from which something continues. 1998년 ... 협정 이후 = since the 1998 agreement.", "example_in_sentence": "협정(굿 프라이데이 협정) 이후"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있었다 (had been ~ing)", "exp": "An ongoing state in the past. 유지되다 → 유지되고 있었습니다 = had been maintained.", "example_in_sentence": "유지되고 있었습니다"}]}, {"text": "이번 폭탄 테러는 북아일랜드의 평화 과정에 악영향을 미칠 수 있습니다.", "translation": "This bomb attack could have a negative impact on Northern Ireland''s peace process.", "vocab": [{"ko": "악영향", "en": "negative impact; adverse effect"}, {"ko": "미치다", "en": "to have (an effect); to affect"}, {"ko": "과정", "en": "process; course"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~에 (악)영향을 미치다 (to have an effect on ~)", "exp": "미치다 here means to exert or have (an effect); 악영향 is a negative effect. 평화 과정에 악영향을 미치다 = to harm the peace process.", "example_in_sentence": "평화 과정에 악영향을 미칠"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다 (can, could)", "exp": "Expresses possibility. 미치다 → 미칠 수 있습니다 = could have (an effect).", "example_in_sentence": "미칠 수 있습니다"}]}, {"text": "경찰과 정부 당국은 사건의 배후를 조사하고 있어요.", "translation": "Police and government authorities are investigating who was behind the incident.", "vocab": [{"ko": "당국", "en": "authorities; officials"}, {"ko": "배후", "en": "those behind (it); mastermind"}, {"ko": "조사하다", "en": "to investigate; to examine"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다", "exp": "Progressive aspect. Indicates ongoing action in present. 조사하다 → 조사하고 + 있어요.", "example_in_sentence": "조사하고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "지역 주민들은 다시 불안감을 느끼고 있는 상황입니다.", "translation": "Local residents are in a situation where they are feeling anxiety again.", "vocab": [{"ko": "주민", "en": "resident; inhabitant"}, {"ko": "불안감", "en": "sense of anxiety; unease"}, {"ko": "느끼다", "en": "to feel; to sense"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있는", "exp": "Present participle with progressive aspect. Modifies the noun 상황, describing an ongoing state or condition.", "example_in_sentence": "느끼고 있는 상황"}]}, {"text": "한국 정부도 이런 테러 사건을 강력히 규탄하는 입장입니다.", "translation": "The Korean government also takes a stance of strongly condemning such terrorist attacks.", "vocab": [{"ko": "규탄하다", "en": "to condemn; to denounce"}, {"ko": "입장", "en": "stance; position"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 입장", "exp": "Nominal form expressing ''one''s position/stance is such that''. Present participle (규탄하는) modifies 입장.", "example_in_sentence": "규탄하는 입장"}]}, {"text": "국제 사회는 북아일랜드의 평화와 안정이 지속되기를 바라고 있어요.", "translation": "The international community is wishing that Northern Ireland''s peace and stability will continue.", "vocab": [{"ko": "국제", "en": "international"}, {"ko": "안정", "en": "stability; order"}, {"ko": "지속되다", "en": "to continue; to last"}, {"ko": "바라다", "en": "to wish; to hope for"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~기를 바라다 (to hope that ~)", "exp": "Expresses a wish about something happening. 지속되다 → 지속되기를 바라다 = to hope that (it) continues.", "example_in_sentence": "지속되기를 바라고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다", "exp": "Progressive aspect. Indicates the ongoing state of wishing/hoping. 바라다 → 바라고 + 있어요.", "example_in_sentence": "바라고 있어요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "차량", "en": "vehicle", "note": ""}, {"ko": "폭탄", "en": "bomb", "note": ""}, {"ko": "터지다", "en": "to explode; to go off", "note": ""}, {"ko": "발생하다", "en": "to occur; to happen", "note": ""}, {"ko": "충격", "en": "shock; impact", "note": ""}, {"ko": "일어나다", "en": "to occur; to arise", "note": ""}, {"ko": "종교적", "en": "religious", "note": ""}, {"ko": "갈등", "en": "conflict; discord", "note": ""}, {"ko": "분쟁", "en": "dispute; strife", "note": ""}, {"ko": "계속되다", "en": "to continue; to persist", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가톨릭계", "en": "Catholic community/side", "note": ""}, {"ko": "개신교계", "en": "Protestant community/side", "note": ""}, {"ko": "대립", "en": "confrontation; opposition", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이어지다", "en": "to continue; to be connected", "note": ""}, {"ko": "협정", "en": "agreement; accord", "note": ""}, {"ko": "유지되다", "en": "to be maintained", "note": ""}, {"ko": "악영향", "en": "negative impact; adverse effect", "note": ""}, {"ko": "미치다", "en": "to have (an effect); to affect", "note": ""}, {"ko": "과정", "en": "process; course", "note": ""}, {"ko": "당국", "en": "authorities; officials", "note": ""}, {"ko": "배후", "en": "those behind (it); mastermind", "note": ""}, {"ko": "조사하다", "en": "to investigate; to examine", "note": ""}, {"ko": "주민", "en": "resident; inhabitant", "note": ""}, {"ko": "불안감", "en": "sense of anxiety; unease", "note": ""}, {"ko": "느끼다", "en": "to feel; to sense", "note": ""}, {"ko": "규탄하다", "en": "to condemn; to denounce", "note": ""}, {"ko": "입장", "en": "stance; position", "note": ""}, {"ko": "국제", "en": "international", "note": ""}, {"ko": "안정", "en": "stability; order", "note": ""}, {"ko": "지속되다", "en": "to continue; to last", "note": ""}, {"ko": "바라다", "en": "to wish; to hope for", "note": ""}, {"word": "테러", "reading": "tereo", "meaning": "terrorism; terrorist attack", "context": "이번 폭탄 테러는 북아일랜드의"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~는 + noun (noun modifier)", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "The clause describes the noun that follows. 터지다 → 터지는 사건 = an incident in which (a bomb) explodes.", "ex_ko": "북아일랜드의 한 경찰서 밖에서 차량 폭탄이 터지는 사건이 발생했습니다.", "ex_en": "An incident occurred in which a car bomb exploded outside a police station in Northern Ireland."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ (past noun modifier)", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "Describes the noun with something that has happened. 계속되다 → 계속된 지역 = a region where (conflict) has continued.", "ex_ko": "북아일랜드는 오랫동안 종교적 갈등과 정치적 분쟁이 계속된 지역입니다.", "ex_en": "Northern Ireland is a region where religious conflict and political dispute have persisted for a long time."}, {"name": "~아/어 왔다", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "Continuous aspect auxiliary. Combines past participle 이어져 (이어지다→이어져) with 왔어요 to express action continuing from past to present.", "ex_ko": "가톨릭계와 개신교계 사이의 대립이 수십 년간 이어져 왔어요.", "ex_en": "The confrontation between Catholics and Protestants has continued for decades."}, {"name": "~고 있었다 (had been ~ing)", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "An ongoing state in the past. 유지되다 → 유지되고 있었습니다 = had been maintained.", "ex_ko": "1998년 성금요일 협정(굿 프라이데이 협정) 이후 평화가 유지되고 있었습니다.", "ex_en": "After the 1998 Good Friday Agreement, peace had been maintained."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다 (can, could)", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "Expresses possibility. 미치다 → 미칠 수 있습니다 = could have (an effect).", "ex_ko": "이번 폭탄 테러는 북아일랜드의 평화 과정에 악영향을 미칠 수 있습니다.", "ex_en": "This bomb attack could have a negative impact on Northern Ireland''s peace process."}, {"name": "~고 있다", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "Progressive aspect. Indicates the ongoing state of wishing/hoping. 바라다 → 바라고 + 있어요.", "ex_ko": "경찰과 정부 당국은 사건의 배후를 조사하고 있어요.", "ex_en": "Police and government authorities are investigating who was behind the incident."}, {"name": "~고 있는", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "Present participle with progressive aspect. Modifies the noun 상황, describing an ongoing state or condition.", "ex_ko": "지역 주민들은 다시 불안감을 느끼고 있는 상황입니다.", "ex_en": "Local residents are in a situation where they are feeling anxiety again."}, {"name": "~는 입장", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "Nominal form expressing ''one''s position/stance is such that''. Present participle (규탄하는) modifies 입장.", "ex_ko": "한국 정부도 이런 테러 사건을 강력히 규탄하는 입장입니다.", "ex_en": "The Korean government also takes a stance of strongly condemning such terrorist attacks."}, {"name": "~기를 바라다 (to hope that ~)", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "Expresses a wish about something happening. 지속되다 → 지속되기를 바라다 = to hope that (it) continues.", "ex_ko": "국제 사회는 북아일랜드의 평화와 안정이 지속되기를 바라고 있어요.", "ex_en": "The international community is wishing that Northern Ireland''s peace and stability will continue."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'moh0hkwl7713' and md5(translation) = 'dc986f522a949516776beb6a3f004a94';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["An interesting incident happened in the United States. A frog fell into hardening concrete at a construction site. It appears the frog entered the concrete before it completely hardened.", "This photo became a big topic on the internet. Many people said they had never seen such an unusual situation before. It looks even more remarkable because the frog''s appearance remained clearly visible in the concrete.", "Experts explained that this kind of thing can happen occasionally. Small animals sometimes mistake wet concrete for soil and enter it. However, it is rare for the appearance to remain so clearly visible like this.", "This incident shows an interesting moment where nature and human construction activities meet. Many netizens found this photo amusing but also felt sympathetic toward the frog."], "sentences": [{"text": "미국에서 흥미로운 일이 일어났어요.", "translation": "An interesting incident occurred in the United States.", "vocab": [{"ko": "흥미롭다", "en": "to be interesting"}, {"ko": "일어나다", "en": "to occur, to happen"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense ending expressing completed action. 일어나다 (present) → 일어났어요 (past).", "example_in_sentence": "일어났어요"}]}, {"text": "한 건설 현장에서 개구리 한 마리가 굳어가는 콘크리트 안에 빠졌어요.", "translation": "At a construction site, a single frog fell into concrete that was hardening.", "vocab": [{"ko": "건설 현장", "en": "construction site"}, {"ko": "개구리", "en": "frog"}, {"ko": "굳다", "en": "to harden, to solidify"}, {"ko": "빠지다", "en": "to fall into, to sink"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어 가다 (change in progress)", "exp": "Shows a gradual change that is still going on. 굳다 → 굳어가는 콘크리트 = concrete that is hardening.", "example_in_sentence": "굳어가는"}]}, {"text": "개구리는 콘크리트가 완전히 굳기 전에 그 안에 들어간 것 같아요.", "translation": "It seems the frog entered inside before the concrete completely hardened.", "vocab": [{"ko": "완전히", "en": "completely"}, {"ko": "들어가다", "en": "to go in, to enter"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~기 전에", "exp": "Temporal clause marking ''before'' an action. Noun form ~기 + 전에 (before). 굳다 → 굳기 전에 (before hardening).", "example_in_sentence": "굳기 전에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ 것 같다 (seems to have ~)", "exp": "A guess about something that already happened. 들어가다 → 들어간 것 같아요 = it seems (it) went in.", "example_in_sentence": "들어간 것 같아요"}]}, {"text": "이 사진은 인터넷에서 큰 화제가 되었어요.", "translation": "This photo became a major topic on the internet.", "vocab": [{"ko": "사진", "en": "photo"}, {"ko": "화제", "en": "topic, subject of discussion"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "화제가 되다", "exp": "Idiomatic expression meaning ''to become a topic/subject of discussion.'' 화제 (topic) + 되다 (become).", "example_in_sentence": "화제가 되었어요"}]}, {"text": "많은 사람들이 이런 특이한 상황을 처음 본다고 말했어요.", "translation": "Many people said it was the first time they had seen such an unusual situation.", "vocab": [{"ko": "특이한", "en": "unusual, unique"}, {"ko": "처음", "en": "first time"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/는다고 말하다 (to say that ~)", "exp": "Reports what someone said. 보다 → 본다 → 본다고 말했어요 = said that (they) see.", "example_in_sentence": "본다고 말했어요"}]}, {"text": "개구리의 모습이 콘크리트에 그대로 남아 있어서 더욱 신기해 보여요.", "translation": "Because the frog''s shape remained intact on the concrete, it looks even more remarkable.", "vocab": [{"ko": "모습", "en": "appearance, shape"}, {"ko": "그대로", "en": "as it is, intact"}, {"ko": "남다", "en": "to remain, to be left"}, {"ko": "신기하다", "en": "to be amazing, to be remarkable"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어 있다", "exp": "Stative auxiliary indicating resultant state. 남다 → 남아 있다 (remains/is left in a state).", "example_in_sentence": "남아 있어서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~어서", "exp": "Causal/connective ending. Cause or reason for following clause. 있다 → 있어서 (because it is/remains).", "example_in_sentence": "있어서"}]}, {"text": "전문가들은 이런 일이 가끔 일어날 수 있다고 설명했어요.", "translation": "Experts explained that such incidents can sometimes occur.", "vocab": [{"ko": "전문가", "en": "expert"}, {"ko": "가끔", "en": "sometimes, occasionally"}, {"ko": "설명하다", "en": "to explain"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄹ 수 있다", "exp": "Possibility modal. Future/potential modifier ~ㄹ + 수 (measure/way) + 있다 (exist/can). 일어나다 → 일어날 수 있다 (can occur).", "example_in_sentence": "일어날 수 있다"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~다고 설명하다", "exp": "Reported speech with declarative. ~다고 (quotative) + 설명하다 (explain). 있다 → 있다고 설명했어요 (explained that [something] is possible).", "example_in_sentence": "있다고 설명했어요"}]}, {"text": "작은 동물들이 젖은 콘크리트를 흙으로 착각하고 들어가는 경우가 있다고 해요.", "translation": "It is said that there are cases where small animals mistake wet concrete for soil and enter it.", "vocab": [{"ko": "젖다", "en": "to be wet"}, {"ko": "착각하다", "en": "to mistake, to misunderstand"}, {"ko": "경우", "en": "case, instance"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고", "exp": "Coordinative connective joining two actions. 착각하다 → 착각하고 (mistake and...). Indicates sequential actions.", "example_in_sentence": "착각하고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~다고 하다", "exp": "Hearsay/reportative. ~다고 (quotative) + 하다 (do/say). 있다 → 있다고 해요 (it is said that there are...).", "example_in_sentence": "있다고 해요"}]}, {"text": "하지만 이렇게 선명하게 모습이 남는 것은 드문 일이에요.", "translation": "However, it is rare for the shape to remain so clearly like this.", "vocab": [{"ko": "선명하다", "en": "to be clear, to be vivid"}, {"ko": "드물다", "en": "to be rare"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 것 (turning a verb into a noun)", "exp": "Turns a verb phrase into a noun. 남다 → 남는 것 = (the fact of) remaining.", "example_in_sentence": "남는 것"}]}, {"text": "이 사건은 자연과 인간의 건설 활동이 만나는 흥미로운 순간을 보여줘요.", "translation": "This incident shows an interesting moment where nature and human construction activity meet.", "vocab": [{"ko": "사건", "en": "incident, event"}, {"ko": "자연", "en": "nature"}, {"ko": "건설 활동", "en": "construction activity"}, {"ko": "만나다", "en": "to meet, to encounter"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (present noun modifier)", "exp": "Describes the noun that follows. 만나다 → 만나는 순간 = the moment when (they) meet.", "example_in_sentence": "만나는"}]}, {"text": "많은 네티즌들이 이 사진을 보고 재미있어하면서도 개구리를 안쓰럽게 생각한다고 말했어요.", "translation": "Many netizens said that while they found this photo amusing, they also felt sorry for the frog.", "vocab": [{"ko": "네티즌", "en": "netizen, internet user"}, {"ko": "재미있어하다", "en": "to find amusing, to enjoy"}, {"ko": "안쓰럽다", "en": "to feel sorry for, to pity"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면서도 (while ~, also)", "exp": "Joins two feelings or actions that happen together but contrast. 재미있어하다 → 재미있어하면서도 = while finding it funny, (they) also ...", "example_in_sentence": "재미있어하면서도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ다고 말하다", "exp": "Reported speech with present declarative. ~ㄴ다 + 고 (quotative) + 말하다 (say). 생각하다 → 생각한다 → 생각한다고 말했어요 (said they think).", "example_in_sentence": "생각한다고 말했어요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "흥미롭다", "en": "to be interesting", "note": ""}, {"ko": "일어나다", "en": "to occur, to happen", "note": ""}, {"ko": "건설 현장", "en": "construction site", "note": ""}, {"ko": "개구리", "en": "frog", "note": ""}, {"ko": "굳다", "en": "to harden, to solidify", "note": ""}, {"ko": "빠지다", "en": "to fall into, to sink", "note": ""}, {"ko": "완전히", "en": "completely", "note": ""}, {"ko": "들어가다", "en": "to go in, to enter", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사진", "en": "photo", "note": ""}, {"ko": "화제", "en": "topic, subject of discussion", "note": ""}, {"ko": "특이한", "en": "unusual, unique", "note": ""}, {"ko": "처음", "en": "first time", "note": ""}, {"ko": "모습", "en": "appearance, shape", "note": ""}, {"ko": "그대로", "en": "as it is, intact", "note": ""}, {"ko": "남다", "en": "to remain, to be left", "note": ""}, {"ko": "신기하다", "en": "to be amazing, to be remarkable", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전문가", "en": "expert", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가끔", "en": "sometimes, occasionally", "note": ""}, {"ko": "설명하다", "en": "to explain", "note": ""}, {"ko": "젖다", "en": "to be wet", "note": ""}, {"ko": "착각하다", "en": "to mistake, to misunderstand", "note": ""}, {"ko": "경우", "en": "case, instance", "note": ""}, {"ko": "선명하다", "en": "to be clear, to be vivid", "note": ""}, {"ko": "드물다", "en": "to be rare", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사건", "en": "incident, event", "note": ""}, {"ko": "자연", "en": "nature", "note": ""}, {"ko": "건설 활동", "en": "construction activity", "note": ""}, {"ko": "만나다", "en": "to meet, to encounter", "note": ""}, {"ko": "네티즌", "en": "netizen, internet user", "note": ""}, {"ko": "재미있어하다", "en": "to find amusing, to enjoy", "note": ""}, {"ko": "안쓰럽다", "en": "to feel sorry for, to pity", "note": ""}, {"word": "굳어가다", "reading": "gudeogyada", "meaning": "to harden / solidify gradually", "context": "굳어가는 콘크리트 안에 빠졌어요"}, {"word": "콘크리트", "reading": "konkeuriteu", "meaning": "concrete", "context": "콘크리트가 완전히 굳기 전에"}, {"word": "화제가 되다", "reading": "hwajega doeda", "meaning": "to become a topic of conversation / attract attention", "context": "이 사진은 인터넷에서 큰 화제가 되었어요"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~았/었어요", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Past tense ending expressing completed action. 일어나다 (present) → 일어났어요 (past).", "ex_ko": "미국에서 흥미로운 일이 일어났어요.", "ex_en": "An interesting incident occurred in the United States."}, {"name": "~아/어 가다 (change in progress)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Shows a gradual change that is still going on. 굳다 → 굳어가는 콘크리트 = concrete that is hardening.", "ex_ko": "한 건설 현장에서 개구리 한 마리가 굳어가는 콘크리트 안에 빠졌어요.", "ex_en": "At a construction site, a single frog fell into concrete that was hardening."}, {"name": "~기 전에", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Temporal clause marking ''before'' an action. Noun form ~기 + 전에 (before). 굳다 → 굳기 전에 (before hardening).", "ex_ko": "개구리는 콘크리트가 완전히 굳기 전에 그 안에 들어간 것 같아요.", "ex_en": "It seems the frog entered inside before the concrete completely hardened."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ 것 같다 (seems to have ~)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "A guess about something that already happened. 들어가다 → 들어간 것 같아요 = it seems (it) went in.", "ex_ko": "개구리는 콘크리트가 완전히 굳기 전에 그 안에 들어간 것 같아요.", "ex_en": "It seems the frog entered inside before the concrete completely hardened."}, {"name": "~ㄴ/는다고 말하다 (to say that ~)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Reports what someone said. 보다 → 본다 → 본다고 말했어요 = said that (they) see.", "ex_ko": "많은 사람들이 이런 특이한 상황을 처음 본다고 말했어요.", "ex_en": "Many people said it was the first time they had seen such an unusual situation."}, {"name": "~아/어 있다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Stative auxiliary indicating resultant state. 남다 → 남아 있다 (remains/is left in a state).", "ex_ko": "개구리의 모습이 콘크리트에 그대로 남아 있어서 더욱 신기해 보여요.", "ex_en": "Because the frog''s shape remained intact on the concrete, it looks even more remarkable."}, {"name": "~어서", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Causal/connective ending. Cause or reason for following clause. 있다 → 있어서 (because it is/remains).", "ex_ko": "개구리의 모습이 콘크리트에 그대로 남아 있어서 더욱 신기해 보여요.", "ex_en": "Because the frog''s shape remained intact on the concrete, it looks even more remarkable."}, {"name": "~ㄹ 수 있다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Possibility modal. Future/potential modifier ~ㄹ + 수 (measure/way) + 있다 (exist/can). 일어나다 → 일어날 수 있다 (can occur).", "ex_ko": "전문가들은 이런 일이 가끔 일어날 수 있다고 설명했어요.", "ex_en": "Experts explained that such incidents can sometimes occur."}, {"name": "~다고 설명하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Reported speech with declarative. ~다고 (quotative) + 설명하다 (explain). 있다 → 있다고 설명했어요 (explained that [something] is possible).", "ex_ko": "전문가들은 이런 일이 가끔 일어날 수 있다고 설명했어요.", "ex_en": "Experts explained that such incidents can sometimes occur."}, {"name": "~고", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Coordinative connective joining two actions. 착각하다 → 착각하고 (mistake and...). Indicates sequential actions.", "ex_ko": "작은 동물들이 젖은 콘크리트를 흙으로 착각하고 들어가는 경우가 있다고 해요.", "ex_en": "It is said that there are cases where small animals mistake wet concrete for soil and enter it."}, {"name": "~다고 하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Hearsay/reportative. ~다고 (quotative) + 하다 (do/say). 있다 → 있다고 해요 (it is said that there are...).", "ex_ko": "작은 동물들이 젖은 콘크리트를 흙으로 착각하고 들어가는 경우가 있다고 해요.", "ex_en": "It is said that there are cases where small animals mistake wet concrete for soil and enter it."}, {"name": "~는 것 (turning a verb into a noun)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Turns a verb phrase into a noun. 남다 → 남는 것 = (the fact of) remaining.", "ex_ko": "하지만 이렇게 선명하게 모습이 남는 것은 드문 일이에요.", "ex_en": "However, it is rare for the shape to remain so clearly like this."}, {"name": "~는 (present noun modifier)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Describes the noun that follows. 만나다 → 만나는 순간 = the moment when (they) meet.", "ex_ko": "이 사건은 자연과 인간의 건설 활동이 만나는 흥미로운 순간을 보여줘요.", "ex_en": "This incident shows an interesting moment where nature and human construction activity meet."}, {"name": "~(으)면서도 (while ~, also)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Joins two feelings or actions that happen together but contrast. 재미있어하다 → 재미있어하면서도 = while finding it funny, (they) also ...", "ex_ko": "많은 네티즌들이 이 사진을 보고 재미있어하면서도 개구리를 안쓰럽게 생각한다고 말했어요.", "ex_en": "Many netizens said that while they found this photo amusing, they also felt sorry for the frog."}, {"name": "~ㄴ다고 말하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Reported speech with present declarative. ~ㄴ다 + 고 (quotative) + 말하다 (say). 생각하다 → 생각한다 → 생각한다고 말했어요 (said they think).", "ex_ko": "많은 네티즌들이 이 사진을 보고 재미있어하면서도 개구리를 안쓰럽게 생각한다고 말했어요.", "ex_en": "Many netizens said that while they found this photo amusing, they also felt sorry for the frog."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'moi5is6egtkl' and md5(translation) = 'a6188860bc199b25ec70c1ba4acf8231';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["Historians have confirmed 2 real pirate flags that are the only ones remaining in the world. Pirate flags are banners that pirates who were active at sea used.", "The first pirate flag is estimated to have been used by the 18th-century pirate Black Sam. It has a white skull and bones drawn on a black background. The second is a flag used by the pirate Stede Bonnet.", "Unlike pirate flags seen in movies or novels, actual pirate flags are very simple. Pirates used these flags to threaten their opponents. When this flag was seen at sea, all ships were said to be afraid.", "These two pirate flags are currently kept in a museum. They are very important materials for researching pirate history. Many tourists are visiting the museum to see these real pirate flags."], "sentences": [{"text": "역사학자들이 세계에서 유일하게 남은 진짜 해적기(海賊旗) 2개를 확인했어요.", "translation": "Historians have confirmed the only two genuine pirate flags left in the world.", "vocab": [{"ko": "역사학자", "en": "historian"}, {"ko": "유일하게", "en": "as the only one; uniquely"}, {"ko": "확인하다", "en": "to confirm; to verify"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past noun modifier)", "exp": "Describes the noun with a resulting state. 남다 → 남은 해적기 = pirate flags that remain.", "example_in_sentence": "유일하게 남은 진짜 해적기"}]}, {"text": "해적기는 바다에서 활동한 해적들이 사용한 깃발이에요.", "translation": "A pirate flag is a flag used by pirates who operated on the sea.", "vocab": [{"ko": "해적기", "en": "pirate flag"}, {"ko": "활동하다", "en": "to operate; to be active"}, {"ko": "깃발", "en": "flag"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past noun modifier)", "exp": "Two past modifiers in a row: 활동하다 → 활동한 해적들 (pirates who were active), 사용하다 → 사용한 깃발 (a flag that was used).", "example_in_sentence": "바다에서 활동한 해적들이 사용한 깃발"}]}, {"text": "첫 번째 해적기는 18세기 해적 블랙 샘(Black Sam)이 사용한 것으로 추정돼요.", "translation": "The first pirate flag is presumed to be one used by 18th-century pirate Black Sam.", "vocab": [{"ko": "추정되다", "en": "to be presumed; to be estimated"}, {"ko": "18세기", "en": "18th century"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ 것으로 추정되다 (is presumed to have ~)", "exp": "A formal way to state a guess about the past. 사용하다 → 사용한 것으로 추정돼요 = (it) is presumed to have been used.", "example_in_sentence": "사용한 것으로 추정돼요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~되다 (passive of ~하다 verbs)", "exp": "Many 하다 verbs become passive by changing 하다 to 되다. 추정하다 (to presume) → 추정되다 (to be presumed) → 추정돼요.", "example_in_sentence": "추정돼요"}]}, {"text": "검은 바탕에 하얀 해골과 뼈가 그려져 있어요.", "translation": "A white skull and bones are drawn on a black background.", "vocab": [{"ko": "바탕", "en": "background; base"}, {"ko": "해골", "en": "skull"}, {"ko": "그리다", "en": "to draw; to paint"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어지다 (passive auxiliary) + ~아/어 있다 (resultant state)", "exp": "''그려지다'' is passive of ''그리다''. Combined with ''있어요'', it expresses resultant state—the skull and bones exist in a drawn state (i.e., have been drawn and remain so).", "example_in_sentence": "그려져 있어요"}]}, {"text": "두 번째는 스테드 보넷(Stede Bonnet) 해적이 쓴 깃발이에요.", "translation": "The second is a flag used by pirate Stede Bonnet.", "vocab": [{"ko": "두 번째", "en": "second"}, {"ko": "쓰다", "en": "to use"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past noun modifier)", "exp": "Describes the noun with a past action. 쓰다 → 쓴 깃발 = the flag that (he) used.", "example_in_sentence": "쓴 깃발"}]}, {"text": "영화나 소설에서 본 해적기와 달리 실제 해적기는 매우 단순해요.", "translation": "Unlike pirate flags seen in movies or novels, actual pirate flags are very simple.", "vocab": [{"ko": "소설", "en": "novel"}, {"ko": "달리", "en": "differently; contrary to"}, {"ko": "실제", "en": "actual; reality"}, {"ko": "단순하다", "en": "to be simple"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~와/과 달리 (unlike ~)", "exp": "Contrasts something with what comes before. 영화나 소설에서 본 해적기와 달리 = unlike the pirate flags seen in movies or novels.", "example_in_sentence": "영화나 소설에서 본 해적기와 달리"}]}, {"text": "해적들은 상대방을 위협하기 위해 이런 깃발을 사용했어요.", "translation": "Pirates used such flags in order to threaten the other party.", "vocab": [{"ko": "상대방", "en": "the other party; opponent"}, {"ko": "위협하다", "en": "to threaten"}, {"ko": "사용하다", "en": "to use"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~기 위해 (in order to)", "exp": "Shows purpose. 위협하다 → 위협하기 위해 = in order to threaten.", "example_in_sentence": "위협하기 위해"}]}, {"text": "바다에서 이 깃발을 보면 모든 배가 두려워했다고 해요.", "translation": "It is said that whenever this flag was seen on the sea, all ships became afraid.", "vocab": [{"ko": "두려워하다", "en": "to fear; to be afraid of"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면 (when, if)", "exp": "Sets up a condition or a time when something happens. 보다 → 보면 = when (they) saw (it).", "example_in_sentence": "이 깃발을 보면"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었다고 하다 (it is said that ~ did)", "exp": "Reports a past event you heard about. 두려워하다 → 두려워했다 → 두려워했다고 해요 = it is said (they) were afraid.", "example_in_sentence": "두려워했다고 해요"}]}, {"text": "이 두 해적기는 현재 박물관에 보관되어 있어요.", "translation": "These two pirate flags are currently stored in a museum.", "vocab": [{"ko": "보관되다", "en": "to be kept; to be stored"}, {"ko": "현재", "en": "currently; at present"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어 있다 (resulting state)", "exp": "Shows a state that continues after an action. 보관되다 → 보관되어 있어요 = are kept (there).", "example_in_sentence": "보관되어 있어요"}]}, {"text": "해적 역사를 연구하는 데 매우 중요한 자료예요.", "translation": "It is very important material for researching pirate history.", "vocab": [{"ko": "연구하다", "en": "to research; to study"}, {"ko": "중요하다", "en": "to be important"}, {"ko": "자료", "en": "material; data; resource"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~는 데 (for ~ing, in ~ing)", "exp": "Means ''for doing'' or ''in doing'' something. 연구하다 → 연구하는 데 중요하다 = important for researching.", "example_in_sentence": "해적 역사를 연구하는 데"}]}, {"text": "많은 관광객들이 이 진짜 해적기를 보기 위해 박물관을 찾고 있어요.", "translation": "Many tourists are visiting the museum in order to see these authentic pirate flags.", "vocab": [{"ko": "관광객", "en": "tourist"}, {"ko": "찾다", "en": "to visit"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~기 위해 (in order to)", "exp": "Shows purpose. 보다 → 보기 위해 = in order to see.", "example_in_sentence": "보기 위해"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다 (ongoing action)", "exp": "Shows an action happening over the current period. 찾다 → 찾고 있어요 = are visiting.", "example_in_sentence": "찾고 있어요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "역사학자", "en": "historian", "note": ""}, {"ko": "유일하게", "en": "as the only one; uniquely", "note": ""}, {"ko": "확인하다", "en": "to confirm; to verify", "note": ""}, {"ko": "해적기", "en": "pirate flag", "note": ""}, {"ko": "활동하다", "en": "to operate; to be active", "note": ""}, {"ko": "깃발", "en": "flag", "note": ""}, {"ko": "추정되다", "en": "to be presumed; to be estimated", "note": ""}, {"ko": "18세기", "en": "18th century", "note": ""}, {"ko": "바탕", "en": "background; base", "note": ""}, {"ko": "해골", "en": "skull", "note": ""}, {"ko": "그리다", "en": "to draw; to paint", "note": ""}, {"ko": "두 번째", "en": "second", "note": ""}, {"ko": "쓰다", "en": "to use", "note": ""}, {"ko": "소설", "en": "novel", "note": ""}, {"ko": "달리", "en": "differently; contrary to", "note": ""}, {"ko": "실제", "en": "actual; reality", "note": ""}, {"ko": "단순하다", "en": "to be simple", "note": ""}, {"ko": "상대방", "en": "the other party; opponent", "note": ""}, {"ko": "위협하다", "en": "to threaten", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사용하다", "en": "to use", "note": ""}, {"ko": "두려워하다", "en": "to fear; to be afraid of", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보관되다", "en": "to be kept; to be stored", "note": ""}, {"ko": "현재", "en": "currently; at present", "note": ""}, {"ko": "연구하다", "en": "to research; to study", "note": ""}, {"ko": "중요하다", "en": "to be important", "note": ""}, {"ko": "자료", "en": "material; data; resource", "note": ""}, {"ko": "관광객", "en": "tourist", "note": ""}, {"ko": "찾다", "en": "to visit", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~(으)ㄴ (past noun modifier)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Two past modifiers in a row: 활동하다 → 활동한 해적들 (pirates who were active), 사용하다 → 사용한 깃발 (a flag that was used).", "ex_ko": "역사학자들이 세계에서 유일하게 남은 진짜 해적기(海賊旗) 2개를 확인했어요.", "ex_en": "Historians have confirmed the only two genuine pirate flags left in the world."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ 것으로 추정되다 (is presumed to have ~)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "A formal way to state a guess about the past. 사용하다 → 사용한 것으로 추정돼요 = (it) is presumed to have been used.", "ex_ko": "첫 번째 해적기는 18세기 해적 블랙 샘(Black Sam)이 사용한 것으로 추정돼요.", "ex_en": "The first pirate flag is presumed to be one used by 18th-century pirate Black Sam."}, {"name": "~되다 (passive of ~하다 verbs)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Many 하다 verbs become passive by changing 하다 to 되다. 추정하다 (to presume) → 추정되다 (to be presumed) → 추정돼요.", "ex_ko": "첫 번째 해적기는 18세기 해적 블랙 샘(Black Sam)이 사용한 것으로 추정돼요.", "ex_en": "The first pirate flag is presumed to be one used by 18th-century pirate Black Sam."}, {"name": "~아/어지다 (passive auxiliary) + ~아/어 있다 (resultant state)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "''그려지다'' is passive of ''그리다''. Combined with ''있어요'', it expresses resultant state—the skull and bones exist in a drawn state (i.e., have been drawn and remain so).", "ex_ko": "검은 바탕에 하얀 해골과 뼈가 그려져 있어요.", "ex_en": "A white skull and bones are drawn on a black background."}, {"name": "~기 위해 (in order to)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Shows purpose. 위협하다 → 위협하기 위해 = in order to threaten.", "ex_ko": "해적들은 상대방을 위협하기 위해 이런 깃발을 사용했어요.", "ex_en": "Pirates used such flags in order to threaten the other party."}, {"name": "~(으)면 (when, if)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Sets up a condition or a time when something happens. 보다 → 보면 = when (they) saw (it).", "ex_ko": "바다에서 이 깃발을 보면 모든 배가 두려워했다고 해요.", "ex_en": "It is said that whenever this flag was seen on the sea, all ships became afraid."}, {"name": "~았/었다고 하다 (it is said that ~ did)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Reports a past event you heard about. 두려워하다 → 두려워했다 → 두려워했다고 해요 = it is said (they) were afraid.", "ex_ko": "바다에서 이 깃발을 보면 모든 배가 두려워했다고 해요.", "ex_en": "It is said that whenever this flag was seen on the sea, all ships became afraid."}, {"name": "~아/어 있다 (resulting state)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Shows a state that continues after an action. 보관되다 → 보관되어 있어요 = are kept (there).", "ex_ko": "이 두 해적기는 현재 박물관에 보관되어 있어요.", "ex_en": "These two pirate flags are currently stored in a museum."}, {"name": "~고 있다 (ongoing action)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Shows an action happening over the current period. 찾다 → 찾고 있어요 = are visiting.", "ex_ko": "많은 관광객들이 이 진짜 해적기를 보기 위해 박물관을 찾고 있어요.", "ex_en": "Many tourists are visiting the museum in order to see these authentic pirate flags."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'moi5jl1iakkq' and md5(translation) = '9ee03bb6ca9a35336b4510030ac924a8';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["On January 25, 1966, Bill Weaver, an American test pilot, experienced something unbelievable. He survived falling from the edge of space.", "At that time, Weaver was piloting a special aircraft called the SR-71. This reconnaissance aircraft could fly at three times the speed of sound (Mach 3). However, the aircraft suddenly shattered in mid-air.", "Weaver fell from the edge of space to the ground without the aircraft. Normally, it would have been a situation where he could only die. However, he miraculously survived.", "This incident is one of the most remarkable survival records in aviation history. Weaver''s survival is still talked about by many people to this day."], "sentences": [{"text": "1966년 1월 25일, 미국의 시험 조종사 빌 위버는 믿을 수 없는 일을 겪었어요.", "translation": "On January 25, 1966, Bill Weaver, an American test pilot, experienced something unbelievable.", "vocab": [{"ko": "시험 조종사", "en": "test pilot"}, {"ko": "겪다", "en": "to experience; to go through"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 없다 (cannot)", "exp": "Says something is impossible. 믿다 → 믿을 수 없는 일 = something (you) cannot believe.", "example_in_sentence": "믿을 수 없는"}]}, {"text": "그는 우주 가장자리에서 떨어져도 살아남았습니다.", "translation": "He survived despite falling from the edge of space.", "vocab": [{"ko": "가장자리", "en": "edge; margin"}, {"ko": "떨어지다", "en": "to fall; to drop"}, {"ko": "살아남다", "en": "to survive"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어도 (even though, even if)", "exp": "Shows that the result happens despite the first part. 떨어지다 → 떨어져도 = even though (he) fell.", "example_in_sentence": "떨어져도"}]}, {"text": "당시 위버는 SR-71이라는 특수 비행기를 조종하고 있었어요.", "translation": "At that time, Weaver was piloting a special aircraft called the SR-71.", "vocab": [{"ko": "당시", "en": "at that time; then"}, {"ko": "조종하다", "en": "to pilot; to operate"}, {"ko": "특수", "en": "special; specific"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(이)라는 (called ~)", "exp": "Comes after a name to describe the noun that follows. SR-71이라는 특수 비행기 = a special aircraft called the SR-71.", "example_in_sentence": "SR-71이라는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다", "exp": "Progressive aspect. 조종하다 + 고 있었어요 (was in the process of piloting). Indicates ongoing action in the past.", "example_in_sentence": "조종하고 있었어요"}]}, {"text": "이 비행기는 음속의 3배(마하 3) 속도로 날아갈 수 있는 정찰기입니다.", "translation": "This aircraft is a reconnaissance jet that can fly at three times the speed of sound (Mach 3).", "vocab": [{"ko": "음속", "en": "speed of sound"}, {"ko": "배", "en": "times; fold (multiplier)"}, {"ko": "정찰기", "en": "reconnaissance aircraft"}, {"ko": "날아가다", "en": "to fly"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다", "exp": "Capability/possibility pattern. 날아가다 + ㄹ 수 있는 (can; is able to). Modifies the noun 정찰기.", "example_in_sentence": "날아갈 수 있는"}]}, {"text": "하지만 갑자기 비행기가 공중에서 산산조각이 났어요.", "translation": "However, suddenly the aircraft shattered into pieces in midair.", "vocab": [{"ko": "갑자기", "en": "suddenly; abruptly"}, {"ko": "공중", "en": "midair; air"}, {"ko": "산산조각", "en": "pieces; fragments"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "산산조각(이) 나다 (to break into pieces)", "exp": "An expression for something breaking into tiny pieces. 비행기가 산산조각이 났어요 = the plane broke into pieces.", "example_in_sentence": "산산조각이 났어요"}]}, {"text": "위버는 비행기 없이 우주 가장자리에서 땅으로 떨어졌습니다.", "translation": "Without an aircraft, Weaver fell from the edge of space to the ground.", "vocab": [{"ko": "없이", "en": "without"}, {"ko": "떨어지다", "en": "to fall; to drop"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~ 없이 (without ~)", "exp": "Comes after a noun to mean ''without'' it. 비행기 없이 = without the aircraft.", "example_in_sentence": "비행기 없이"}]}, {"text": "보통이라면 죽을 수밖에 없는 상황이었어요.", "translation": "Normally, it would have been a situation where one could only die.", "vocab": [{"ko": "보통", "en": "normally; usually; ordinary"}, {"ko": "죽다", "en": "to die"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수밖에 없다 (have no choice but to)", "exp": "Says there is only one possible outcome. 죽다 → 죽을 수밖에 없는 상황 = a situation where (he) could only die.", "example_in_sentence": "죽을 수밖에 없는"}]}, {"text": "하지만 그는 기적적으로 살아남았습니다.", "translation": "However, miraculously, he survived.", "vocab": [{"ko": "기적적으로", "en": "miraculously"}, {"ko": "살아남다", "en": "to survive"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이 사건은 항공 역사상 가장 놀라운 생존 기록 중 하나예요.", "translation": "This incident is one of the most remarkable survival records in aviation history.", "vocab": [{"ko": "사건", "en": "incident; event"}, {"ko": "역사상", "en": "in the history of"}, {"ko": "놀랍다", "en": "to be surprising; to be remarkable"}, {"ko": "생존 기록", "en": "survival record"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~ 중 하나 (one of ~)", "exp": "Picks one item out of a group. 가장 놀라운 생존 기록 중 하나 = one of the most remarkable survival records.", "example_in_sentence": "생존 기록 중 하나"}]}, {"text": "위버의 생존은 오늘날까지도 많은 사람들에게 회자되고 있습니다.", "translation": "Weaver''s survival continues to be spoken of by many people until today.", "vocab": [{"ko": "오늘날", "en": "today; nowadays"}, {"ko": "회자되다", "en": "to be mentioned; to be talked about"}, {"ko": "사람들", "en": "people"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~까지도", "exp": "Extended/inclusive scope marker. 오늘날 (today) + 까지도 (even until/through). Emphasizes continuation from past to present.", "example_in_sentence": "오늘날까지도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다", "exp": "Progressive aspect. 회자되다 + 고 있습니다 (is being mentioned/continues to be spoken of). Indicates ongoing action.", "example_in_sentence": "회자되고 있습니다"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "시험 조종사", "en": "test pilot", "note": ""}, {"ko": "겪다", "en": "to experience; to go through", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가장자리", "en": "edge; margin", "note": ""}, {"ko": "떨어지다", "en": "to fall; to drop", "note": ""}, {"ko": "살아남다", "en": "to survive", "note": ""}, {"ko": "당시", "en": "at that time; then", "note": ""}, {"ko": "조종하다", "en": "to pilot; to operate", "note": ""}, {"ko": "특수", "en": "special; specific", "note": ""}, {"ko": "음속", "en": "speed of sound", "note": ""}, {"ko": "배", "en": "times; fold (multiplier)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "정찰기", "en": "reconnaissance aircraft", "note": ""}, {"ko": "날아가다", "en": "to fly", "note": ""}, {"ko": "갑자기", "en": "suddenly; abruptly", "note": ""}, {"ko": "공중", "en": "midair; air", "note": ""}, {"ko": "산산조각", "en": "pieces; fragments", "note": ""}, {"ko": "없이", "en": "without", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보통", "en": "normally; usually; ordinary", "note": ""}, {"ko": "죽다", "en": "to die", "note": ""}, {"ko": "기적적으로", "en": "miraculously", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사건", "en": "incident; event", "note": ""}, {"ko": "역사상", "en": "in the history of", "note": ""}, {"ko": "놀랍다", "en": "to be surprising; to be remarkable", "note": ""}, {"ko": "생존 기록", "en": "survival record", "note": ""}, {"ko": "오늘날", "en": "today; nowadays", "note": ""}, {"ko": "회자되다", "en": "to be mentioned; to be talked about", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사람들", "en": "people", "note": ""}, {"word": "우주 가장자리", "reading": "uju gajangjari", "meaning": "edge of space; the boundary between atmosphere and space", "context": "우주 가장자리에서 떨어져도"}, {"word": "특수 비행기", "reading": "teuksu bihaengggi", "meaning": "special aircraft; an aircraft with specialized purpose", "context": "SR-71이라는 특수 비행기를"}, {"word": "기적", "reading": "gijeok", "meaning": "miracle; an extraordinary and welcome event", "context": "그는 기적적으로 살아남았습니다"}, {"word": "항공 역사", "reading": "hanggong yeoksa", "meaning": "aviation history; the historical record of aircraft and flight", "context": "항공 역사상 가장 놀라운"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수 없다 (cannot)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Says something is impossible. 믿다 → 믿을 수 없는 일 = something (you) cannot believe.", "ex_ko": "1966년 1월 25일, 미국의 시험 조종사 빌 위버는 믿을 수 없는 일을 겪었어요.", "ex_en": "On January 25, 1966, Bill Weaver, an American test pilot, experienced something unbelievable."}, {"name": "~아/어도 (even though, even if)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Shows that the result happens despite the first part. 떨어지다 → 떨어져도 = even though (he) fell.", "ex_ko": "그는 우주 가장자리에서 떨어져도 살아남았습니다.", "ex_en": "He survived despite falling from the edge of space."}, {"name": "~(이)라는 (called ~)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Comes after a name to describe the noun that follows. SR-71이라는 특수 비행기 = a special aircraft called the SR-71.", "ex_ko": "당시 위버는 SR-71이라는 특수 비행기를 조종하고 있었어요.", "ex_en": "At that time, Weaver was piloting a special aircraft called the SR-71."}, {"name": "~고 있다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Progressive aspect. 회자되다 + 고 있습니다 (is being mentioned/continues to be spoken of). Indicates ongoing action.", "ex_ko": "당시 위버는 SR-71이라는 특수 비행기를 조종하고 있었어요.", "ex_en": "At that time, Weaver was piloting a special aircraft called the SR-71."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Capability/possibility pattern. 날아가다 + ㄹ 수 있는 (can; is able to). Modifies the noun 정찰기.", "ex_ko": "이 비행기는 음속의 3배(마하 3) 속도로 날아갈 수 있는 정찰기입니다.", "ex_en": "This aircraft is a reconnaissance jet that can fly at three times the speed of sound (Mach 3)."}, {"name": "산산조각(이) 나다 (to break into pieces)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "An expression for something breaking into tiny pieces. 비행기가 산산조각이 났어요 = the plane broke into pieces.", "ex_ko": "하지만 갑자기 비행기가 공중에서 산산조각이 났어요.", "ex_en": "However, suddenly the aircraft shattered into pieces in midair."}, {"name": "~ 없이 (without ~)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Comes after a noun to mean ''without'' it. 비행기 없이 = without the aircraft.", "ex_ko": "위버는 비행기 없이 우주 가장자리에서 땅으로 떨어졌습니다.", "ex_en": "Without an aircraft, Weaver fell from the edge of space to the ground."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수밖에 없다 (have no choice but to)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Says there is only one possible outcome. 죽다 → 죽을 수밖에 없는 상황 = a situation where (he) could only die.", "ex_ko": "보통이라면 죽을 수밖에 없는 상황이었어요.", "ex_en": "Normally, it would have been a situation where one could only die."}, {"name": "~까지도", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Extended/inclusive scope marker. 오늘날 (today) + 까지도 (even until/through). Emphasizes continuation from past to present.", "ex_ko": "위버의 생존은 오늘날까지도 많은 사람들에게 회자되고 있습니다.", "ex_en": "Weaver''s survival continues to be spoken of by many people until today."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'moi5ka4oq7cz' and md5(translation) = 'fd8ecea5b211c42d0b67bc04ef17cff5';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["In 1945, there was a Japanese man named Yamaguchi Tsutomu. He experienced a nuclear bomb explosion in Hiroshima. However, he survived. He took shelter in an air raid shelter (a place to escape air raids). He spent the night there. The next morning, he took a train. He was trying to get to work on time. His workplace was in Nagasaki. But a nuclear bomb also exploded in Nagasaki. Surprisingly, he survived the second nuclear bomb as well. He is a person who had a very unique experience in the world. This kind of thing is truly rare.", "Korean Teacher Shortage Becomes Serious, School Classes Disrupted", "What is an \"anxiety bag\"? A Popular Trend", "The United States and China Resume Talks Over Trade Issues", "\"Talking Pig\" Becomes SNS Star", "Apple Greatly Improves iPhone Speed with New AI Chip"], "sentences": [{"text": "1945년 야마구치 츠토무라는 일본 사람이 있었어요.", "translation": "In 1945, there was a Japanese person named Yamaguchi Tsutomu.", "vocab": [{"ko": "야마구치", "en": "Yamaguchi (surname)"}, {"ko": "일본 사람", "en": "Japanese person"}, {"ko": "있다", "en": "to exist; to be"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(이)라는 (named ~, called ~)", "exp": "Comes after a name to describe the noun that follows. 야마구치 츠토무라는 일본 사람 = a Japanese man named Yamaguchi Tsutomu.", "example_in_sentence": "야마구치 츠토무라는 일본 사람"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense suffix. Indicates the action or state occurred in the past. 있다 → 있었어요.", "example_in_sentence": "있었어요"}]}, {"text": "그는 히로시마에서 핵폭탄(원자폭탄) 폭발을 당했어요.", "translation": "He experienced a nuclear bomb (atomic bomb) explosion in Hiroshima.", "vocab": [{"ko": "히로시마", "en": "Hiroshima"}, {"ko": "핵폭탄", "en": "nuclear bomb"}, {"ko": "폭발", "en": "explosion"}, {"ko": "당하다", "en": "to experience; to suffer; to undergo"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서", "exp": "Locative particle indicating the location where an action takes place.", "example_in_sentence": "히로시마에서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를", "exp": "Object particle marking the direct object of the verb. 폭발 is what is experienced.", "example_in_sentence": "폭발을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense suffix. 당하다 → 당했어요.", "example_in_sentence": "당했어요"}]}, {"text": "하지만 살아남았어요.", "translation": "However, he survived.", "vocab": [{"ko": "하지만", "en": "however; but"}, {"ko": "살아남다", "en": "to survive"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense suffix. 살아남다 → 살아남았어요.", "example_in_sentence": "살아남았어요"}]}, {"text": "그는 방공호(공습을 피하는 곳)로 피했어요.", "translation": "He fled to a bunker (a place to avoid air raids).", "vocab": [{"ko": "방공호", "en": "bunker; air-raid shelter"}, {"ko": "공습", "en": "air raid"}, {"ko": "피하다", "en": "to escape; to flee; to avoid"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로", "exp": "Particle indicating direction or destination of movement. Where he fled to.", "example_in_sentence": "방공호(공습을 피하는 곳)로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense suffix. 피하다 → 피했어요.", "example_in_sentence": "피했어요"}]}, {"text": "하룻밤을 그곳에서 보냈어요.", "translation": "He spent one night there.", "vocab": [{"ko": "하룻밤", "en": "one night"}, {"ko": "보내다", "en": "to spend (time); to pass"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를", "exp": "Object particle marking the direct object. 하룻밤 is the time period being spent.", "example_in_sentence": "하룻밤을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서", "exp": "Locative particle indicating where the action takes place.", "example_in_sentence": "그곳에서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense suffix. 보내다 → 보냈어요.", "example_in_sentence": "보냈어요"}]}, {"text": "다음 날 아침 기차를 탔어요.", "translation": "The next morning, he boarded a train.", "vocab": [{"ko": "다음", "en": "next; following"}, {"ko": "기차", "en": "train"}, {"ko": "타다", "en": "to ride; to board"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를", "exp": "Object particle marking the direct object of the verb. 기차 is what is boarded.", "example_in_sentence": "기차를"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense suffix. 타다 → 탔어요.", "example_in_sentence": "탔어요"}]}, {"text": "그는 시간에 맞춰 직장에 가려고 했어요.", "translation": "He intended to go to work on time.", "vocab": [{"ko": "시간", "en": "time"}, {"ko": "맞추다", "en": "to match; to fit (a time)"}, {"ko": "직장", "en": "workplace; job"}, {"ko": "가다", "en": "to go"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에 맞춰 (on time for, in line with)", "exp": "Means doing something so it fits a time or standard. 시간에 맞춰 = on time.", "example_in_sentence": "시간에 맞춰"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)려고 하다", "exp": "Auxiliary construction expressing intention or plan. 가다 → 가려고 했어요 (intended to go).", "example_in_sentence": "가려고 했어요"}]}, {"text": "그의 직장은 나가사키에 있었어요.", "translation": "His workplace was in Nagasaki.", "vocab": [{"ko": "나가사키", "en": "Nagasaki"}, {"ko": "있다", "en": "to be; to exist"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는", "exp": "Topic particle marking the subject of the sentence.", "example_in_sentence": "그의 직장은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에", "exp": "Locative particle indicating where something is located.", "example_in_sentence": "나가사키에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense suffix. 있다 → 있었어요.", "example_in_sentence": "있었어요"}]}, {"text": "그런데 나가사키에서도 핵폭탄이 터졌어요.", "translation": "However, a nuclear bomb also exploded in Nagasaki.", "vocab": [{"ko": "그런데", "en": "however; but; nevertheless"}, {"ko": "터지다", "en": "to burst; to explode"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~도", "exp": "Particle meaning ''also'' or ''too,'' adding emphasis to the location where the action occurs.", "example_in_sentence": "나가사키에서도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense suffix. 터지다 → 터졌어요.", "example_in_sentence": "터졌어요"}]}, {"text": "놀랍게도 그는 두 번째 핵폭탄에서도 살아남았어요.", "translation": "Surprisingly, he also survived the second nuclear bomb.", "vocab": [{"ko": "놀랍다", "en": "to be surprising; to be amazing"}, {"ko": "두 번째", "en": "second (time); second"}, {"ko": "살아남다", "en": "to survive"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~게도 (to one''s ~)", "exp": "Turns a feeling word into a comment on the whole sentence. 놀랍다 → 놀랍게도 = surprisingly.", "example_in_sentence": "놀랍게도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~도 (also, too)", "exp": "Adds ''also'' to the word before it. 두 번째 핵폭탄에서도 = from the second nuclear bomb too.", "example_in_sentence": "두 번째 핵폭탄에서도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense suffix. 살아남다 → 살아남았어요.", "example_in_sentence": "살아남았어요"}]}, {"text": "그는 세계에서 매우 특별한 경험을 한 사람이에요.", "translation": "He is a person who has had a very special experience in the world.", "vocab": [{"ko": "세계", "en": "world"}, {"ko": "매우", "en": "very; extremely"}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "special; exceptional; unique"}, {"ko": "경험", "en": "experience"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서", "exp": "Locative particle indicating the scope or range within which something is remarkable.", "example_in_sentence": "세계에서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "exp": "Turns a describing word into a noun modifier. 특별하다 → 특별한 경험 = a special experience.", "example_in_sentence": "특별한 경험"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를", "exp": "Object particle marking the direct object of the verb 하다.", "example_in_sentence": "경험을"}]}, {"text": "이런 일은 정말 드문 일이에요.", "translation": "Such an occurrence is truly rare.", "vocab": [{"ko": "이런", "en": "such; like this"}, {"ko": "드물다", "en": "rare; uncommon; scarce"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는", "exp": "Topic particle marking the subject of the sentence.", "example_in_sentence": "이런 일은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "exp": "Turns a describing word into a noun modifier. ㄹ drops before ㄴ: 드물다 → 드문 일 = a rare thing.", "example_in_sentence": "드문 일"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "야마구치", "en": "Yamaguchi (surname)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "일본 사람", "en": "Japanese person", "note": ""}, {"ko": "있다", "en": "to exist; to be", "note": ""}, {"ko": "히로시마", "en": "Hiroshima", "note": ""}, {"ko": "핵폭탄", "en": "nuclear bomb", "note": ""}, {"ko": "폭발", "en": "explosion", "note": ""}, {"ko": "당하다", "en": "to experience; to suffer; to undergo", "note": ""}, {"ko": "하지만", "en": "however; but", "note": ""}, {"ko": "살아남다", "en": "to survive", "note": ""}, {"ko": "방공호", "en": "bunker; air-raid shelter", "note": ""}, {"ko": "공습", "en": "air raid", "note": ""}, {"ko": "피하다", "en": "to escape; to flee; to avoid", "note": ""}, {"ko": "하룻밤", "en": "one night", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보내다", "en": "to spend (time); to pass", "note": ""}, {"ko": "다음", "en": "next; following", "note": ""}, {"ko": "기차", "en": "train", "note": ""}, {"ko": "타다", "en": "to ride; to board", "note": ""}, {"ko": "시간", "en": "time", "note": ""}, {"ko": "맞추다", "en": "to match; to fit (a time)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "직장", "en": "workplace; job", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가다", "en": "to go", "note": ""}, {"ko": "나가사키", "en": "Nagasaki", "note": ""}, {"ko": "그런데", "en": "however; but; nevertheless", "note": ""}, {"ko": "터지다", "en": "to burst; to explode", "note": ""}, {"ko": "놀랍다", "en": "to be surprising; to be amazing", "note": ""}, {"ko": "두 번째", "en": "second (time); second", "note": ""}, {"ko": "세계", "en": "world", "note": ""}, {"ko": "매우", "en": "very; extremely", "note": ""}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "special; exceptional; unique", "note": ""}, {"ko": "경험", "en": "experience", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이런", "en": "such; like this", "note": ""}, {"ko": "드물다", "en": "rare; uncommon; scarce", "note": ""}, {"word": "놀랍게도", "reading": "nol-rab-ge-do", "meaning": "surprisingly; astonishingly", "context": "놀랍게도 그는 두 번째 핵폭탄에서도 살아남았어요"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~(이)라는 (named ~, called ~)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Comes after a name to describe the noun that follows. 야마구치 츠토무라는 일본 사람 = a Japanese man named Yamaguchi Tsutomu.", "ex_ko": "1945년 야마구치 츠토무라는 일본 사람이 있었어요.", "ex_en": "In 1945, there was a Japanese person named Yamaguchi Tsutomu."}, {"name": "~았/었어요", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Past tense suffix. Indicates the action or state occurred in the past. 있다 → 있었어요.", "ex_ko": "1945년 야마구치 츠토무라는 일본 사람이 있었어요.", "ex_en": "In 1945, there was a Japanese person named Yamaguchi Tsutomu."}, {"name": "~에서", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Locative particle indicating the scope or range within which something is remarkable.", "ex_ko": "그는 히로시마에서 핵폭탄(원자폭탄) 폭발을 당했어요.", "ex_en": "He experienced a nuclear bomb (atomic bomb) explosion in Hiroshima."}, {"name": "~을/를", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Object particle marking the direct object of the verb. 폭발 is what is experienced.", "ex_ko": "그는 히로시마에서 핵폭탄(원자폭탄) 폭발을 당했어요.", "ex_en": "He experienced a nuclear bomb (atomic bomb) explosion in Hiroshima."}, {"name": "~(으)로", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Particle indicating direction or destination of movement. Where he fled to.", "ex_ko": "그는 방공호(공습을 피하는 곳)로 피했어요.", "ex_en": "He fled to a bunker (a place to avoid air raids)."}, {"name": "~에 맞춰 (on time for, in line with)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Means doing something so it fits a time or standard. 시간에 맞춰 = on time.", "ex_ko": "그는 시간에 맞춰 직장에 가려고 했어요.", "ex_en": "He intended to go to work on time."}, {"name": "~(으)려고 하다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Auxiliary construction expressing intention or plan. 가다 → 가려고 했어요 (intended to go).", "ex_ko": "그는 시간에 맞춰 직장에 가려고 했어요.", "ex_en": "He intended to go to work on time."}, {"name": "~은/는", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Topic particle marking the subject of the sentence.", "ex_ko": "그의 직장은 나가사키에 있었어요.", "ex_en": "His workplace was in Nagasaki."}, {"name": "~도 (also, too)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Particle meaning ''also'' or ''too,'' adding emphasis to the location where the action occurs.", "ex_ko": "그런데 나가사키에서도 핵폭탄이 터졌어요.", "ex_en": "However, a nuclear bomb also exploded in Nagasaki."}, {"name": "~게도 (to one''s ~)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Turns a feeling word into a comment on the whole sentence. 놀랍다 → 놀랍게도 = surprisingly.", "ex_ko": "놀랍게도 그는 두 번째 핵폭탄에서도 살아남았어요.", "ex_en": "Surprisingly, he also survived the second nuclear bomb."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Turns a describing word into a noun modifier. ㄹ drops before ㄴ: 드물다 → 드문 일 = a rare thing.", "ex_ko": "그는 세계에서 매우 특별한 경험을 한 사람이에요.", "ex_en": "He is a person who has had a very special experience in the world."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'moi5kzqf9w90' and md5(translation) = 'afee119e802c2d3a6b21f956011e90b8';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["The first Pride Parade was held in the United States in 1973. A Pride Parade is an event that supports the rights of sexual minorities.", "Something special happened at this event. Parents who had LGBTQ+ children participated together. At that time, this kind of thing was very rare.", "The parents sent a message of support for their children. Their participation moved many people.", "This photograph still has historical significance today. It is an example that shows how important family love and support are. Currently in Korea, understanding of sexual minorities is gradually expanding."], "sentences": [{"text": "1973년 미국에서 첫 번째 프라이드 퍼레이드(Pride Parade)가 열렸어요.", "translation": "The first Pride Parade was held in the United States in 1973.", "vocab": [{"ko": "열리다", "en": "to be held; to open"}, {"ko": "첫 번째", "en": "first"}, {"ko": "미국", "en": "United States"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense marker for declarative sentences in polite/informal register. 열리다 (to be held) → 열렸어요 (was held).", "example_in_sentence": "열렸어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서", "exp": "Locative particle indicating the location/place where an action occurs.", "example_in_sentence": "미국에서"}]}, {"text": "프라이드 퍼레이드는 성소수자들의 권리를 지지하는 행사예요.", "translation": "A Pride Parade is an event that supports the rights of sexual minorities.", "vocab": [{"ko": "성소수자", "en": "sexual minority"}, {"ko": "권리", "en": "right"}, {"ko": "지지하다", "en": "to support"}, {"ko": "행사", "en": "event"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는", "exp": "Present participle/attributive form modifying a noun. 지지하다 (to support) → 지지하는 (supporting/that supports).", "example_in_sentence": "지지하는 행사"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~예요/이에요", "exp": "Copula in polite/informal register for definition or classification. Equivalent to ''is''.", "example_in_sentence": "행사예요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~의", "exp": "Possessive/genitive particle connecting noun + noun. Marks possession or relationship.", "example_in_sentence": "성소수자들의 권리"}]}, {"text": "이 행사에서 특별한 일이 있었어요.", "translation": "Something special happened at this event.", "vocab": [{"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special"}, {"ko": "일", "en": "thing; matter"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense marker. 있다 (to be/exist) → 있었어요 (there was).", "example_in_sentence": "있었어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서", "exp": "Locative particle marking the place where an event or action occurs.", "example_in_sentence": "행사에서"}]}, {"text": "성소수자 자녀를 둔 부모들이 함께 참여했어요.", "translation": "Parents who have LGBTQ+ children participated together.", "vocab": [{"ko": "자녀", "en": "child(ren)"}, {"ko": "두다", "en": "to have (a child)"}, {"ko": "부모", "en": "parent"}, {"ko": "참여하다", "en": "to participate"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past noun modifier)", "exp": "Describes the noun that follows. 두다 → 둔 부모들 = parents who have (LGBTQ+ children).", "example_in_sentence": "둔 부모들"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense marker. 참여하다 (to participate) → 참여했어요 (participated).", "example_in_sentence": "참여했어요"}]}, {"text": "당시에는 이런 일이 매우 드물었어요.", "translation": "At that time, such things were very rare.", "vocab": [{"ko": "당시", "en": "that time; then"}, {"ko": "드물다", "en": "to be rare"}, {"ko": "매우", "en": "very"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense marker. 드물다 (to be rare) → 드물었어요 (was rare).", "example_in_sentence": "드물었어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에는", "exp": "Temporal particle 에 + contrastive/emphatic particle 는. Marks a specific time point.", "example_in_sentence": "당시에는"}]}, {"text": "부모들은 자녀를 지지한다는 메시지를 보냈어요.", "translation": "Parents sent a message saying they support their children.", "vocab": [{"ko": "지지하다", "en": "to support"}, {"ko": "메시지", "en": "message"}, {"ko": "보내다", "en": "to send"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/는다는 + noun (the ~ that ...)", "exp": "Turns a statement into the content of the noun that follows. 지지하다 → 지지한다 → 지지한다는 메시지 = a message that (they) support (their children).", "example_in_sentence": "지지한다는 메시지"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense marker. 보내다 (to send) → 보냈어요 (sent).", "example_in_sentence": "보냈어요"}]}, {"text": "이들의 참여는 많은 사람들에게 감동을 주었어요.", "translation": "Their participation moved many people.", "vocab": [{"ko": "참여", "en": "participation"}, {"ko": "감동", "en": "emotion; being moved"}, {"ko": "주다", "en": "to give"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense marker. 주다 (to give) → 주었어요 (gave).", "example_in_sentence": "주었어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에게", "exp": "Dative particle marking the recipient or target of an action or emotion.", "example_in_sentence": "사람들에게"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "감동을 주다", "exp": "Verbal expression meaning ''to move (emotionally); to inspire.'' Literally ''to give emotion.''", "example_in_sentence": "감동을 주었어요"}]}, {"text": "이 사진은 지금도 역사적으로 중요한 의미가 있어요.", "translation": "This photograph still has historically important significance.", "vocab": [{"ko": "사진", "en": "photograph"}, {"ko": "역사적", "en": "historical"}, {"ko": "중요하다", "en": "to be important"}, {"ko": "의미", "en": "meaning; significance"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~도", "exp": "Emphatic/inclusive particle meaning ''also; still; even.'' Conveys that the state persists.", "example_in_sentence": "지금도"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "의미가 있다", "exp": "Verbal expression meaning ''to have meaning; to be significant.'' Literally ''meaning exists.''", "example_in_sentence": "의미가 있어요"}]}, {"text": "가족의 사랑과 지지가 얼마나 중요한지 보여주는 사례예요.", "translation": "It is an example that shows how important family love and support are.", "vocab": [{"ko": "가족", "en": "family"}, {"ko": "사랑", "en": "love"}, {"ko": "중요하다", "en": "to be important"}, {"ko": "사례", "en": "example; case"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는", "exp": "Present participle/attributive form modifying a noun. 보여주다 (to show) → 보여주는 (that shows).", "example_in_sentence": "보여주는 사례"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ지 (how / whether ~)", "exp": "Turns a question into part of the sentence. 얼마나 중요하다 → 얼마나 중요한지 보여주다 = to show how important (it) is.", "example_in_sentence": "얼마나 중요한지"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~예요/이에요", "exp": "Copula in polite/informal register for classification or definition.", "example_in_sentence": "사례예요"}]}, {"text": "현재 한국에서도 성소수자에 대한 이해가 점점 넓어지고 있어요.", "translation": "Currently, understanding of sexual minorities in Korea is gradually broadening.", "vocab": [{"ko": "현재", "en": "currently; at present"}, {"ko": "한국", "en": "Korea"}, {"ko": "이해", "en": "understanding"}, {"ko": "넓어지다", "en": "to broaden; to widen"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~도", "exp": "Inclusive particle meaning ''also; too.'' Indicates Korea is included in the broader scope.", "example_in_sentence": "한국에서도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에 대한", "exp": "Relational construction 에 대하다 meaning ''regarding; concerning; about/toward.'' 에 대하다 → 에 대한 (attributive form).", "example_in_sentence": "성소수자에 대한 이해"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다", "exp": "Progressive aspect marker indicating an ongoing or continuous action/state. 넓어지다 → 넓어지고 있다 (is broadening).", "example_in_sentence": "넓어지고 있어요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "열리다", "en": "to be held; to open", "note": ""}, {"ko": "첫 번째", "en": "first", "note": ""}, {"ko": "미국", "en": "United States", "note": ""}, {"ko": "성소수자", "en": "sexual minority", "note": ""}, {"ko": "권리", "en": "right", "note": ""}, {"ko": "지지하다", "en": "to support", "note": ""}, {"ko": "행사", "en": "event", "note": ""}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special", "note": ""}, {"ko": "일", "en": "thing; matter", "note": ""}, {"ko": "자녀", "en": "child(ren)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "두다", "en": "to have (a child)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "부모", "en": "parent", "note": "