exual minorities."}, {"name": "~예요/이에요", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Copula in polite/informal register for definition or classification. Equivalent to ''is''.", "ex_ko": "프라이드 퍼레이드는 성소수자들의 권리를 지지하는 행사예요.", "ex_en": "A Pride Parade is an event that supports the rights of sexual minorities."}, {"name": "~의", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Possessive/genitive particle connecting noun + noun. Marks possession or relationship.", "ex_ko": "프라이드 퍼레이드는 성소수자들의 권리를 지지하는 행사예요.", "ex_en": "A Pride Parade is an event that supports the rights of sexual minorities."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ (past noun modifier)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Describes the noun that follows. 두다 → 둔 부모들 = parents who have (LGBTQ+ children).", "ex_ko": "성소수자 자녀를 둔 부모들이 함께 참여했어요.", "ex_en": "Parents who have LGBTQ+ children participated together."}, {"name": "~에는", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Temporal particle 에 + contrastive/emphatic particle 는. Marks a specific time point.", "ex_ko": "당시에는 이런 일이 매우 드물었어요.", "ex_en": "At that time, such things were very rare."}, {"name": "~ㄴ/는다는 + noun (the ~ that ...)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Turns a statement into the content of the noun that follows. 지지하다 → 지지한다 → 지지한다는 메시지 = a message that (they) support (their children).", "ex_ko": "부모들은 자녀를 지지한다는 메시지를 보냈어요.", "ex_en": "Parents sent a message saying they support their children."}, {"name": "~에게", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Dative particle marking the recipient or target of an action or emotion.", "ex_ko": "이들의 참여는 많은 사람들에게 감동을 주었어요.", "ex_en": "Their participation moved many people."}, {"name": "~도", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Emphatic/inclusive particle meaning ''also; still; even.'' Conveys that the state persists.", "ex_ko": "이 사진은 지금도 역사적으로 중요한 의미가 있어요.", "ex_en": "This photograph still has historically important significance."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ지 (how / whether ~)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Turns a question into part of the sentence. 얼마나 중요하다 → 얼마나 중요한지 보여주다 = to show how important (it) is.", "ex_ko": "가족의 사랑과 지지가 얼마나 중요한지 보여주는 사례예요.", "ex_en": "It is an example that shows how important family love and support are."}, {"name": "~에 대한", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Relational construction 에 대하다 meaning ''regarding; concerning; about/toward.'' 에 대하다 → 에 대한 (attributive form).", "ex_ko": "현재 한국에서도 성소수자에 대한 이해가 점점 넓어지고 있어요.", "ex_en": "Currently, understanding of sexual minorities in Korea is gradually broadening."}, {"name": "~고 있다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Progressive aspect marker indicating an ongoing or continuous action/state. 넓어지다 → 넓어지고 있다 (is broadening).", "ex_ko": "현재 한국에서도 성소수자에 대한 이해가 점점 넓어지고 있어요.", "ex_en": "Currently, understanding of sexual minorities in Korea is gradually broadening."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'moi5lkxte05t' and md5(translation) = 'c13a881c52e5166e142cbf5acbad2293';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["These days, a new ingredient is becoming popular in K-beauty (Korean cosmetics). The name of that ingredient is azulene.", "Azulene is a good ingredient for sensitive skin. It helps when your face becomes red or your skin hurts.", "When you use this ingredient, your skin calms down quickly. Skin troubles improve in just a few seconds.", "Many people with sensitive skin are looking for it. Korean cosmetic companies are also making azulene products."], "sentences": [{"text": "요즘 K-뷰티(한국 화장품)에서 새로운 성분이 인기예요.", "translation": "These days, a new ingredient is popular in K-beauty (Korean cosmetics).", "vocab": [{"ko": "요즘", "en": "these days, recently"}, {"ko": "새롭다", "en": "to be new"}, {"ko": "성분", "en": "ingredient, component"}, {"ko": "인기", "en": "popularity, fame"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서", "exp": "Particle indicating location or source where an action/state occurs.", "example_in_sentence": "K-뷰티(한국 화장품)에서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~예요/이에요 (is)", "exp": "The polite form of 이다 (to be). After a vowel use 예요: 인기 → 인기예요 = is popular.", "example_in_sentence": "인기예요"}]}, {"text": "그 성분의 이름은 아줄렌(azulene)이에요.", "translation": "The name of that ingredient is azulene.", "vocab": [{"ko": "성분", "en": "ingredient, component"}, {"ko": "이름", "en": "name"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~의", "exp": "Possessive particle indicating attribution or belonging.", "example_in_sentence": "성분의"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는", "exp": "Topic marker particle; identifies the subject of the predicate.", "example_in_sentence": "이름은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이에요", "exp": "Present copula for noun predicate; polite/informal ending. 이다 + 어요 → 이에요.", "example_in_sentence": "이에요"}]}, {"text": "아줄렌은 민감한 피부에 좋은 성분이에요.", "translation": "Azulene is a good ingredient for sensitive skin.", "vocab": [{"ko": "민감하다", "en": "to be sensitive"}, {"ko": "피부", "en": "skin"}, {"ko": "좋다", "en": "to be good"}, {"ko": "성분", "en": "ingredient, component"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "exp": "Describing words take ~(으)ㄴ before a noun. 민감하다 → 민감한 피부 = sensitive skin.", "example_in_sentence": "민감한"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에", "exp": "Particle indicating target/beneficiary or location of benefit.", "example_in_sentence": "피부에"}]}, {"text": "얼굴이 빨갛게 되거나 피부가 아플 때 도움이 돼요.", "translation": "It helps when the face becomes red or the skin hurts.", "vocab": [{"ko": "얼굴", "en": "face"}, {"ko": "빨갛다", "en": "to be red"}, {"ko": "피부", "en": "skin"}, {"ko": "아프다", "en": "to hurt, to ache"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~게 되다 (to become ~)", "exp": "Shows a change into a new state. 빨갛다 → 빨갛게 되다 = to become red.", "example_in_sentence": "빨갛게 되거나"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~거나", "exp": "Conjunctive ending joining two predicates as alternatives; ''or''.", "example_in_sentence": "되거나"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 때 (when)", "exp": "Marks the time when something happens. 아프다 → 아플 때 = when (it) hurts.", "example_in_sentence": "아플 때"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "도움이 되다", "exp": "Verbal collocation meaning ''to be helpful; to help''.", "example_in_sentence": "도움이 돼요"}]}, {"text": "이 성분을 사용하면 피부가 빠르게 진정돼요.", "translation": "If you use this ingredient, the skin calms down quickly.", "vocab": [{"ko": "성분", "en": "ingredient, component"}, {"ko": "사용하다", "en": "to use"}, {"ko": "빠르다", "en": "to be fast"}, {"ko": "진정되다", "en": "to calm down; to be soothed"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를", "exp": "Object marker particle indicating direct object of a transitive verb.", "example_in_sentence": "성분을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면 (if, when)", "exp": "Sets up a condition. 사용하다 → 사용하면 = if you use (it).", "example_in_sentence": "사용하면"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~게", "exp": "Adverbial ending converting adjective to adverb. 빠르다 → 빠르 + 게.", "example_in_sentence": "빠르게"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~되다", "exp": "Passive/middle voice suffix; shows state change. 진정 (soothing) + 되다.", "example_in_sentence": "진정돼요"}]}, {"text": "몇 초 만에 피부 트러블이 나아져요.", "translation": "In just a few seconds, skin trouble improves.", "vocab": [{"ko": "몇", "en": "how many, a few"}, {"ko": "초", "en": "second (time unit)"}, {"ko": "피부", "en": "skin"}, {"ko": "나아지다", "en": "to improve, to get better"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~ 만에", "exp": "Phrase meaning ''in just ~ time'' or ''within ~''; expresses quickness.", "example_in_sentence": "몇 초 만에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이", "exp": "Nominative subject marker particle.", "example_in_sentence": "트러블이"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어지다 (to become ~)", "exp": "Shows a change of state. 낫다 (to be better; ㅅ drops) → 나아지다 = to get better → 나아져요.", "example_in_sentence": "나아져요"}]}, {"text": "민감한 피부를 가진 사람들이 많이 찾고 있어요.", "translation": "Many people who have sensitive skin are looking for it.", "vocab": [{"ko": "민감하다", "en": "to be sensitive"}, {"ko": "피부", "en": "skin"}, {"ko": "가지다", "en": "to have, to possess"}, {"ko": "사람", "en": "person"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를", "exp": "Object marker particle indicating direct object.", "example_in_sentence": "피부를"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past noun modifier)", "exp": "Describes the noun that follows. 가지다 → 가진 사람들 = people who have (sensitive skin).", "example_in_sentence": "가진"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이", "exp": "Nominative subject marker particle.", "example_in_sentence": "사람들이"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다", "exp": "Progressive aspect; shows ongoing action. 찾 + 고 있어요.", "example_in_sentence": "찾고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "한국 화장품 회사들도 아줄렌 제품을 만들고 있어요.", "translation": "Korean cosmetic companies are also making azulene products.", "vocab": [{"ko": "한국", "en": "Korea"}, {"ko": "화장품", "en": "cosmetics"}, {"ko": "회사", "en": "company"}, {"ko": "제품", "en": "product"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label":