cation or source where an action/state occurs.", "ex_ko": "요즘 K-뷰티(한국 화장품)에서 새로운 성분이 인기예요.", "ex_en": "These days, a new ingredient is popular in K-beauty (Korean cosmetics)."}, {"name": "~예요/이에요 (is)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "The polite form of 이다 (to be). After a vowel use 예요: 인기 → 인기예요 = is popular.", "ex_ko": "요즘 K-뷰티(한국 화장품)에서 새로운 성분이 인기예요.", "ex_en": "These days, a new ingredient is popular in K-beauty (Korean cosmetics)."}, {"name": "~의", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Possessive particle indicating attribution or belonging.", "ex_ko": "그 성분의 이름은 아줄렌(azulene)이에요.", "ex_en": "The name of that ingredient is azulene."}, {"name": "~은/는", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Topic marker particle; identifies the subject of the predicate.", "ex_ko": "그 성분의 이름은 아줄렌(azulene)이에요.", "ex_en": "The name of that ingredient is azulene."}, {"name": "~이에요", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Present copula for noun predicate; polite/informal ending. 이다 + 어요 → 이에요.", "ex_ko": "그 성분의 이름은 아줄렌(azulene)이에요.", "ex_en": "The name of that ingredient is azulene."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Describes the noun that follows. 가지다 → 가진 사람들 = people who have (sensitive skin).", "ex_ko": "아줄렌은 민감한 피부에 좋은 성분이에요.", "ex_en": "Azulene is a good ingredient for sensitive skin."}, {"name": "~게 되다 (to become ~)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Shows a change into a new state. 빨갛다 → 빨갛게 되다 = to become red.", "ex_ko": "얼굴이 빨갛게 되거나 피부가 아플 때 도움이 돼요.", "ex_en": "It helps when the face becomes red or the skin hurts."}, {"name": "~거나", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Conjunctive ending joining two predicates as alternatives; ''or''.", "ex_ko": "얼굴이 빨갛게 되거나 피부가 아플 때 도움이 돼요.", "ex_en": "It helps when the face becomes red or the skin hurts."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 때 (when)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Marks the time when something happens. 아프다 → 아플 때 = when (it) hurts.", "ex_ko": "얼굴이 빨갛게 되거나 피부가 아플 때 도움이 돼요.", "ex_en": "It helps when the face becomes red or the skin hurts."}, {"name": "~을/를", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Object marker particle indicating direct object of a transitive verb.", "ex_ko": "이 성분을 사용하면 피부가 빠르게 진정돼요.", "ex_en": "If you use this ingredient, the skin calms down quickly."}, {"name": "~(으)면 (if, when)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Sets up a condition. 사용하다 → 사용하면 = if you use (it).", "ex_ko": "이 성분을 사용하면 피부가 빠르게 진정돼요.", "ex_en": "If you use this ingredient, the skin calms down quickly."}, {"name": "~게", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Adverbial ending converting adjective to adverb. 빠르다 → 빠르 + 게.", "ex_ko": "이 성분을 사용하면 피부가 빠르게 진정돼요.", "ex_en": "If you use this ingredient, the skin calms down quickly."}, {"name": "~되다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Passive/middle voice suffix; shows state change. 진정 (soothing) + 되다.", "ex_ko": "이 성분을 사용하면 피부가 빠르게 진정돼요.", "ex_en": "If you use this ingredient, the skin calms down quickly."}, {"name": "~이", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Nominative subject marker particle.", "ex_ko": "몇 초 만에 피부 트러블이 나아져요.", "ex_en": "In just a few seconds, skin trouble improves."}, {"name": "~아/어지다 (to become ~)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Shows a change of state. 낫다 (to be better; ㅅ drops) → 나아지다 = to get better → 나아져요.", "ex_ko": "몇 초 만에 피부 트러블이 나아져요.", "ex_en": "In just a few seconds, skin trouble improves."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'moifgh8h4cr3' and md5(translation) = '7816e0676858fb879d17922cc9df8c12';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["A scam warning about Botox has appeared on the internet. There are allegations that some practitioners are diluting Botox with water.", "Botox is a popular procedure for removing wrinkles. However, some hospitals or clinics may dilute Botox to make more money.", "Diluted Botox has reduced effectiveness. Patients may not get good results even though they pay the same amount of money.", "Experts advise getting the procedure at a trustworthy hospital. It is important to check the Botox product and dosage before the procedure."], "sentences": [{"text": "인터넷에서 보톡스(Botox) 관련 사기 경고가 나왔어요.", "translation": "A warning about Botox-related fraud has appeared on the Internet.", "vocab": [{"ko": "인터넷", "en": "internet"}, {"ko": "사기", "en": "fraud; scam"}, {"ko": "경고", "en": "warning"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서", "exp": "Locative particle marking the location/source where an action occurs or originates.", "example_in_sentence": "인터넷에서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense conversational ending indicating a completed past action. 나오다(come out) → 나왔어요.", "example_in_sentence": "나왔어요"}]}, {"text": "일부 시술자들이 보톡스를 물로 희석한다는 의혹이 제기되고 있어요.", "translation": "Suspicions are being raised that some practitioners are diluting Botox with water.", "vocab": [{"ko": "일부", "en": "some; part"}, {"ko": "시술자", "en": "practitioner; technician"}, {"ko": "희석하다", "en": "to dilute"}, {"ko": "의혹", "en": "suspicion; allegation"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로", "exp": "Instrumental particle indicating the means or material used for an action. 물(water) + ~(으)로.", "example_in_sentence": "물로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/는다는 + noun (the ~ that ...)", "exp": "Turns a statement into the content of the noun that follows. 희석하다 → 희석한다는 의혹 = a suspicion that (they) dilute (it).", "example_in_sentence": "희석한다는 의혹"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있어요", "exp": "Progressive/continuous aspect in conversational style; indicates ongoing state. 제기되다(be raised) + ~고 있어요.", "example_in_sentence": "제기되고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "보톡스는 주름을 없애는 인기 시술이에요.", "translation": "Botox is a popular procedure that removes wrinkles.", "vocab": [{"ko": "주름", "en": "wrinkle"}, {"ko": "없애다", "en": "to remove; to eliminate"}, {"ko": "인기", "en": "popularity; being popular"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (present noun modifier)", "exp": "Describes the noun that follows. 없애다 → 없애는 시술 = a procedure that removes (wrinkles).", "example_in_sentence": "주름을 없애는 인기 시술"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이에요", "exp": "Present copular ending in conversational style. Identifies/classifies the subject.", "example_in_sentence": "이에요"}]}, {"text": "하지만 일부 병원이나 시술소에서 더 많은 돈을 벌기 위해 보톡스를 희석할 수 있다고 해요.", "translation": "However, it is said that some hospitals or clinics may dilute Botox in order to earn more money.", "vocab": [{"ko": "하지만", "en": "however; but"}, {"ko": "병원", "en": "hospital"}, {"ko": "시술소", "en": "clinic; treatment facility"}, {"ko": "벌다", "en": "to earn; to make (money)"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~이나", "exp": "Conjunction/particle indicating alternatives or multiple options. 병원(hospital) 이나 시술소(clinic).", "example_in_sentence": "병원이나 시술소"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~기 위해", "exp": "Purposive connective; expresses intent/goal of an action. 벌다(earn) + ~기 위해(in order to).", "example_in_sentence": "벌기 위해"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다고 하다", "exp": "Reported speech indicating hearsay or indirect statement. Combines possibility and quotative.", "example_in_sentence": "희석할 수 있다고 해요"}]}, {"text": "희석된 보톡스는 효과가 떨어져요.", "translation": "Diluted Botox has reduced effectiveness.", "vocab": [{"ko": "희석되다", "en": "to be diluted"}, {"ko": "효과", "en": "effect; effectiveness"}, {"ko": "떨어지다", "en": "to drop; to decrease"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ", "exp": "Past participle/adjectival ending modifying the subject noun. 희석되다(be diluted) + ~ㄴ.", "example_in_sentence": "희석된"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가", "exp": "Nominative particle marking the subject of the sentence.", "example_in_sentence": "효과가"}]}, {"text": "환자들은 같은 돈을 내고도 좋은 결과를 얻지 못할 수 있어요.", "translation": "Patients may pay the same amount of money and still not get good results.", "vocab": [{"ko": "환자", "en": "patient"}, {"ko": "같다", "en": "to be same; to be equal"}, {"ko": "결과", "en": "result; outcome"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "exp": "Describing words take ~(으)ㄴ before a noun. 같다 → 같은 돈 = the same money.", "example_in_sentence": "같은 돈"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고도", "exp": "Concessive connective combining two contrasting situations; ''even while/though''. 내다(pay) + ~고도.", "example_in_sentence": "내고도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~지 못하다", "exp": "Negative potential expressing inability/failure. 얻다(obtain) + ~지 못하다.", "example_in_sentence": "얻지 못할"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다 (may, might)", "exp": "Here it expresses possibility. 못하다 → 못할 수 있어요 = (they) might not be able to.", "example_in_sentence": "못할 수 있어요"}]}, {"text": "전문가들은 믿을 만한 병원에서 시술받으라고 조언해요.", "translation": "Experts advise people to receive treatment at trustworthy hospitals.", "vocab": [{"ko": "전문가", "en": "expert; specialist"}, {"ko": "믿다", "en": "to trust; to believe"}, {"ko": "조언하다", "en": "to advise; to counsel"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 만하다 (worth ~ing)", "exp": "Says something is worth doing. 믿다 → 믿을 만한 병원 = a hospital you can trust.", "example_in_sentence": "믿을 만한"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)라고 (quoting advice or a command)", "exp": "Quotes what someone tells others to do. 시술받다 → 시술받으라고 조언하다 = to advise (people) to get the procedure.", "example_in_sentence": "시술받으라고 조언해요"}]}, {"text": "시술 전에 보톡스 제품과 용량을 확인하는 것이 중요해요.", "translation": "It is important to confirm the Botox product and dosage before treatment.", "vocab": [{"ko": "전", "en": "before"}, {"ko": "제품", "en": "product"}, {"ko": "용량", "en": "dosage; amount"}, {"ko": "확인하다", "en": "to confirm; to check"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 것이 중요하다 (it is important to ~)", "exp": "~는 것 turns a verb into a noun. 확인하다 → 확인하는 것이 중요해요 = it is important to check.", "example_in_sentence": "확인하는 것이 중요해요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "인터넷", "en": "internet", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사기", "en": "fraud; scam", "note": ""}, {"ko": "경고", "en": "warning", "note": ""}, {"ko": "일부", "en": "some; part", "note": ""}, {"ko": "시술자", "en": "practitioner; technician", "note": ""}, {"ko": "희석하다", "en": "to dilute", "note": ""}, {"ko": "의혹", "en": "suspicion; allegation", "note": ""}, {"ko": "주름", "en": "wrinkle", "note": ""}, {"ko": "없애다", "en": "to remove; to eliminate", "note": ""}, {"ko": "인기", "en": "popularity; being popular", "note": ""}, {"ko": "하지만", "en": "however; but", "note": ""}, {"ko": "병원", "en": "hospital", "note": ""}, {"ko": "시술소", "en": "clinic; treatment facility", "note": ""}, {"ko": "벌다", "en": "to earn; to make (money)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "희석되다", "en": "to be diluted", "note": ""}, {"ko": "효과", "en": "effect; effectiveness", "note": ""}, {"ko": "떨어지다", "en": "to drop; to decrease", "note": ""}, {"ko": "환자", "en": "patient", "note": ""}, {"ko": "같다", "en": "to be same; to be equal", "note": ""}, {"ko": "결과", "en": "result; outcome", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전문가", "en": "expert; specialist", "note": ""}, {"ko": "믿다", "en": "to trust; to believe", "note": ""}, {"ko": "조언하다", "en": "to advise; to counsel", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전", "en": "before", "note": ""}, {"ko": "제품", "en": "product", "note": ""}, {"ko": "용량", "en": "dosage; amount", "note": ""}, {"ko": "확인하다", "en": "to confirm; to check", "note": ""}, {"word": "시술", "reading": "siseul", "meaning": "medical procedure / treatment / operation", "context": "보톡스는 주름을 없애는 인기 시술이에요"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~에서", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Locative particle marking the location/source where an action occurs or originates.", "ex_ko": "인터넷에서 보톡스(Botox) 관련 사기 경고가 나왔어요.", "ex_en": "A warning about Botox-related fraud has appeared on the Internet."}, {"name": "~았/었어요", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Past tense conversational ending indicating a completed past action. 나오다(come out) → 나왔어요.", "ex_ko": "인터넷에서 보톡스(Botox) 관련 사기 경고가 나왔어요.", "ex_en": "A warning about Botox-related fraud has appeared on the Internet."}, {"name": "~(으)로", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Instrumental particle indicating the means or material used for an action. 물(water) + ~(으)로.", "ex_ko": "일부 시술자들이 보톡스를 물로 희석한다는 의혹이 제기되고 있어요.", "ex_en": "Suspicions are being raised that some practitioners are diluting Botox with water."}, {"name": "~ㄴ/는다는 + noun (the ~ that ...)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Turns a statement into the content of the noun that follows. 희석하다 → 희석한다는 의혹 = a suspicion that (they) dilute (it).", "ex_ko": "일부 시술자들이 보톡스를 물로 희석한다는 의혹이 제기되고 있어요.", "ex_en": "Suspicions are being raised that some practitioners are diluting Botox with water."}, {"name": "~고 있어요", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Progressive/continuous aspect in conversational style; indicates ongoing state. 제기되다(be raised) + ~고 있어요.", "ex_ko": "일부 시술자들이 보톡스를 물로 희석한다는 의혹이 제기되고 있어요.", "ex_en": "Suspicions are being raised that some practitioners are diluting Botox with water."}, {"name": "~는 (present noun modifier)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Describes the noun that follows. 없애다 → 없애는 시술 = a procedure that removes (wrinkles).", "ex_ko": "보톡스는 주름을 없애는 인기 시술이에요.", "ex_en": "Botox is a popular procedure that removes wrinkles."}, {"name": "~이에요", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Present copular ending in conversational style. Identifies/classifies the subject.", "ex_ko": "보톡스는 주름을 없애는 인기 시술이에요.", "ex_en": "Botox is a popular procedure that removes wrinkles."}, {"name": "~이나", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Conjunction/particle indicating alternatives or multiple options. 병원(hospital) 이나 시술소(clinic).", "ex_ko": "하지만 일부 병원이나 시술소에서 더 많은 돈을 벌기 위해 보톡스를 희석할 수 있다고 해요.", "ex_en": "However, it is said that some hospitals or clinics may dilute Botox in order to earn more money."}, {"name": "~기 위해", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Purposive connective; expresses intent/goal of an action. 벌다(earn) + ~기 위해(in order to).", "ex_ko": "하지만 일부 병원이나 시술소에서 더 많은 돈을 벌기 위해 보톡스를 희석할 수 있다고 해요.", "ex_en": "However, it is said that some hospitals or clinics may dilute Botox in order to earn more money."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다고 하다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Reported speech indicating hearsay or indirect statement. Combines possibility and quotative.", "ex_ko": "하지만 일부 병원이나 시술소에서 더 많은 돈을 벌기 위해 보톡스를 희석할 수 있다고 해요.", "ex_en": "However, it is said that some hospitals or clinics may dilute Botox in order to earn more money."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Past participle/adjectival ending modifying the subject noun. 희석되다(be diluted) + ~ㄴ.", "ex_ko": "희석된 보톡스는 효과가 떨어져요.", "ex_en": "Diluted Botox has reduced effectiveness."}, {"name": "~이/가", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Nominative particle marking the subject of the sentence.", "ex_ko": "희석된 보톡스는 효과가 떨어져요.", "ex_en": "Diluted Botox has reduced effectiveness."}, {"name": "~고도", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Concessive connective combining two contrasting situations; ''even while/though''. 내다(pay) + ~고도.", "ex_ko": "환자들은 같은 돈을 내고도 좋은 결과를 얻지 못할 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "Patients may pay the same amount of money and still not get good results."}, {"name": "~지 못하다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Negative potential expressing inability/failure. 얻다(obtain) + ~지 못하다.", "ex_ko": "환자들은 같은 돈을 내고도 좋은 결과를 얻지 못할 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "Patients may pay the same amount of money and still not get good results."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다 (may, might)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Here it expresses possibility. 못하다 → 못할 수 있어요 = (they) might not be able to.", "ex_ko": "환자들은 같은 돈을 내고도 좋은 결과를 얻지 못할 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "Patients may pay the same amount of money and still not get good results."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'moifi31gy61g' and md5(translation) = 'ab3fd20ad033cd7dffa52145a7b96bdb';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["These days, people who like clean and natural makeup are using shiny cosmetics. This is called ''sparkle revival.''", "Previously, many women preferred simple and clean makeup. But now they apply glitter or shiny products on their faces.", "This trend is also popular in Korea. Young people use a lot of sparkly products in eyeshadow or lip gloss. Especially, it''s popular at parties or special occasions.", "Beauty experts say this trend will continue. Sparkly makeup makes people look brighter and more beautiful."], "sentences": [{"text": "요즘 깨끗하고 자연스러운 메이크업을 좋아하는 사람들이 반짝이는 화장품을 사용하고 있어요.", "translation": "These days, people who like clean and natural makeup are using shiny cosmetics.", "vocab": [{"ko": "요즘", "en": "these days, lately"}, {"ko": "깨끗하다", "en": "to be clean"}, {"ko": "자연스럽다", "en": "to be natural"}, {"ko": "반짝이다", "en": "to sparkle, to shine"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있어요", "exp": "Progressive aspect marker indicating an ongoing or continuous action. Verb stem + ~고 있어요 = ''is/are currently doing''.", "example_in_sentence": "사용하고 있어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고", "exp": "Coordinate conjunction connecting two adjectives with equal emphasis. Both describe the noun 메이크업.", "example_in_sentence": "깨끗하고 자연스러운"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 사람들이", "exp": "Present participle relative clause modifying the noun 사람들. Verb stem + ~는 describes people who habitually like that style.", "example_in_sentence": "좋아하는 사람들이"}]}, {"text": "이것을 ''반짝이 부활(sparkle revival)''이라고 해요.", "translation": "This is called ''sparkle revival.''", "vocab": [{"ko": "이것", "en": "this"}, {"ko": "부활", "en": "revival, resurrection"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(이)라고 하다 (to be called ~)", "exp": "Gives the name of something. Noun + (이)라고 해요 = it is called ~.", "example_in_sentence": "''반짝이 부활(sparkle revival)''이라고 해요"}]}, {"text": "전에는 많은 여성들이 단순하고 깨끗한 메이크업을 선호했어요.", "translation": "Previously, many women preferred simple and clean makeup.", "vocab": [{"ko": "전에", "en": "before, previously"}, {"ko": "많다", "en": "many, much"}, {"ko": "단순하다", "en": "simple"}, {"ko": "선호하다", "en": "to prefer"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense marker. Verb stem + ~았어요 (for ㅏ/ㅗ vowels) or ~었어요 (for others) indicates completed action.", "example_in_sentence": "선호했어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "exp": "Describing words take ~(으)ㄴ before a noun. 깨끗하다 → 깨끗한 메이크업 = clean makeup.", "example_in_sentence": "단순하고 깨끗한 메이크업"}]}, {"text": "하지만 지금은 글리터(glitter)나 반짝이는 제품을 얼굴에 발라요.", "translation": "But now they apply glitter or shiny products on their face.", "vocab": [{"ko": "하지만", "en": "but, however"}, {"ko": "지금", "en": "now"}, {"ko": "바르다", "en": "to apply (on skin)"}, {"ko": "제품", "en": "product"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~나", "exp": "Listing particle meaning ''or'' used when giving examples. Connects 글리터 and 반짝이는 제품.", "example_in_sentence": "글리터나 반짝이는 제품"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에", "exp": "Locative particle indicating location or target. Here shows the place where action occurs: ''(on) the face''.", "example_in_sentence": "얼굴에 발라요"}]}, {"text": "한국에서도 이런 트렌드가 인기예요.", "translation": "This trend is also popular in Korea.", "vocab": [{"ko": "한국", "en": "Korea"}, {"ko": "이런", "en": "this kind of, such"}, {"ko": "트렌드", "en": "trend"}, {"ko": "인기", "en": "popularity"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~도", "exp": "Additive particle meaning ''also, too.'' 한국에서도 = ''in Korea as well / Korea too''.", "example_in_sentence": "한국에서도"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "인기이다 (to be popular)", "exp": "인기 (popularity) + 이다 (to be). After a vowel, 이에요 becomes 예요: 인기예요 = is popular.", "example_in_sentence": "인기예요"}]}, {"text": "젊은 사람들이 아이섀도우나 립글로스에 반짝이는 것을 많이 써요.", "translation": "Young people use a lot of shiny eyeshadow or lip gloss.", "vocab": [{"ko": "젊다", "en": "to be young"}, {"ko": "아이섀도우", "en": "eyeshadow"}, {"ko": "립글로스", "en": "lip gloss"}, {"ko": "쓰다", "en": "to use, to wear"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~나", "exp": "Listing particle ''or'' connecting examples: 아이섀도우 and 립글로스.", "example_in_sentence": "아이섀도우나 립글로스에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 것을", "exp": "Nominalization converting the clause into an object. 반짝이다 + ~는 것 = ''the thing that sparkles / shiny stuff''.", "example_in_sentence": "반짝이는 것을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에", "exp": "Target/recipient particle showing the makeup products where shiny elements are applied.", "example_in_sentence": "아이섀도우나 립글로스에"}]}, {"text": "특히 파티나 특별한 날에 인기가 많아요.", "translation": "It is especially popular at parties or on special days.", "vocab": [{"ko": "특히", "en": "especially, particularly"}, {"ko": "파티", "en": "party"}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "special"}, {"ko": "많다", "en": "much, many"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~나", "exp": "Listing particle ''or'' connecting examples: 파티 and 특별한 날.", "example_in_sentence": "파티나 특별한 날에"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "인기가 많다", "exp": "Collocation meaning ''to be very popular.'' 인기 (popularity, noun) + 많다 (to be many/much).", "example_in_sentence": "인기가 많아요"}]}, {"text": "뷰티 전문가들은 이 트렌드가 계속 이어질 것이라고 말해요.", "translation": "Beauty experts say that this trend will continue.", "vocab": [{"ko": "뷰티", "en": "beauty"}, {"ko": "전문가", "en": "expert, specialist"}, {"ko": "계속", "en": "continuously; still"}, {"ko": "이어지다", "en": "to continue, to be connected"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 것이다 (will)", "exp": "Talks about the future or a prediction. 이어지다 → 이어질 것이다 = will continue.", "example_in_sentence": "이어질 것이라고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(이)라고 말하다 (to say that ~)", "exp": "Reports what someone says. 것이다 → 것이라고 말해요 = say that (it) will ...", "example_in_sentence": "이어질 것이라고 말해요"}]}, {"text": "반짝이 메이크업은 사람들을 더 밝고 예쁘게 보이게 해줘요.", "translation": "Sparkly makeup makes people look brighter and prettier.", "vocab": [{"ko": "반짝이", "en": "sparkle, glitter"}, {"ko": "밝다", "en": "bright, light"}, {"ko": "예쁘다", "en": "pretty, beautiful"}, {"ko": "보이다", "en": "to look, to appear"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~게 하다 (to make someone/something ~)", "exp": "Means to cause someone or something to do or be. 보이다 → 보이게 하다 = to make (people) look (bright and pretty).", "example_in_sentence": "보이게 해줘요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고", "exp": "Coordinate conjunction connecting two adjectives with equal emphasis: 밝고 예쁘게 both describe how people appear.", "example_in_sentence": "밝고 예쁘게"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어 주다 (to do for someone)", "exp": "Shows that an action benefits someone. 하다 → 해 주다 → 해줘요 = does (it) for (them).", "example_in_sentence": "해줘요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "요즘", "en": "these days, lately", "note": ""}, {"ko": "깨끗하다", "en": "to be clean", "note": ""}, {"ko": "자연스럽다", "en": "to be natural", "note": ""}, {"ko": "반짝이다", "en": "to sparkle, to shine", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이것", "en": "this", "note": ""}, {"ko": "부활", "en": "revival, resurrection", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전에", "en": "before, previously", "note": ""}, {"ko": "많다", "en": "many, much", "note": ""}, {"ko": "단순하다", "en": "simple", "note": ""}, {"ko": "선호하다", "en": "to prefer", "note": ""}, {"ko": "하지만", "en": "but, however", "note": ""}, {"ko": "지금", "en": "now", "note": ""}, {"ko": "바르다", "en": "to apply (on skin)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "제품", "en": "product", "note": ""}, {"ko": "한국", "en": "Korea", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이런", "en": "this kind of, such", "note": ""}, {"ko": "트렌드", "en": "trend", "note": ""}, {"ko": "인기", "en": "popularity", "note": ""}, {"ko": "젊다", "en": "to be young", "note": ""}, {"ko": "아이섀도우", "en": "eyeshadow", "note": ""}, {"ko": "립글로스", "en": "lip gloss", "note": ""}, {"ko": "쓰다", "en": "to use, to wear", "note": ""}, {"ko": "특히", "en": "especially, particularly", "note": ""}, {"ko": "파티", "en": "party", "note": ""}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "special", "note": ""}, {"ko": "뷰티", "en": "beauty", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전문가", "en": "expert, specialist", "note": ""}, {"ko": "계속", "en": "continuously; still", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이어지다", "en": "to continue, to be connected", "note": ""}, {"ko": "반짝이", "en": "sparkle, glitter", "note": ""}, {"ko": "밝다", "en": "bright, light", "note": ""}, {"ko": "예쁘다", "en": "pretty, beautiful", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보이다", "en": "to look, to appear", "note": ""}, {"word": "메이크업", "reading": "meikeuap", "meaning": "makeup", "context": "깨끗하고 자연스러운 메이크업을 좋아하는"}, {"word": "화장품", "reading": "hwajangpum", "meaning": "cosmetic product", "context": "반짝이는 화장품을 사용하고 있어요"}, {"word": "글리터", "reading": "geulliteo", "meaning": "glitter", "context": "글리터(glitter)나 반짝이는 제품을 얼굴에 발라요"}, {"word": "발라다", "reading": "ballada", "meaning": "to apply; to spread (on a surface)", "context": "반짝이는 제품을 얼굴에 발라요"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~고 있어요", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Progressive aspect marker indicating an ongoing or continuous action. Verb stem + ~고 있어요 = ''is/are currently doing''.", "ex_ko": "요즘 깨끗하고 자연스러운 메이크업을 좋아하는 사람들이 반짝이는 화장품을 사용하고 있어요.", "ex_en": "These days, people who like clean and natural makeup are using shiny cosmetics."}, {"name": "~고", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Coordinate conjunction connecting two adjectives with equal emphasis: 밝고 예쁘게 both describe how people appear.", "ex_ko": "요즘 깨끗하고 자연스러운 메이크업을 좋아하는 사람들이 반짝이는 화장품을 사용하고 있어요.", "ex_en": "These days, people who like clean and natural makeup are using shiny cosmetics."}, {"name": "~는 사람들이", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Present participle relative clause modifying the noun 사람들. Verb stem + ~는 describes people who habitually like that style.", "ex_ko": "요즘 깨끗하고 자연스러운 메이크업을 좋아하는 사람들이 반짝이는 화장품을 사용하고 있어요.", "ex_en": "These days, people who like clean and natural makeup are using shiny cosmetics."}, {"name": "~(이)라고 하다 (to be called ~)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Gives the name of something. Noun + (이)라고 해요 = it is called ~.", "ex_ko": "이것을 ''반짝이 부활(sparkle revival)''이라고 해요.", "ex_en": "This is called ''sparkle revival.''"}, {"name": "~았/었어요", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Past tense marker. Verb stem + ~았어요 (for ㅏ/ㅗ vowels) or ~었어요 (for others) indicates completed action.", "ex_ko": "전에는 많은 여성들이 단순하고 깨끗한 메이크업을 선호했어요.", "ex_en": "Previously, many women preferred simple and clean makeup."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Describing words take ~(으)ㄴ before a noun. 깨끗하다 → 깨끗한 메이크업 = clean makeup.", "ex_ko": "전에는 많은 여성들이 단순하고 깨끗한 메이크업을 선호했어요.", "ex_en": "Previously, many women preferred simple and clean makeup."}, {"name": "~나", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Listing particle meaning ''or'' used when giving examples. Connects 글리터 and 반짝이는 제품.", "ex_ko": "하지만 지금은 글리터(glitter)나 반짝이는 제품을 얼굴에 발라요.", "ex_en": "But now they apply glitter or shiny products on their face."}, {"name": "~에", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Locative particle indicating location or target. Here shows the place where action occurs: ''(on) the face''.", "ex_ko": "하지만 지금은 글리터(glitter)나 반짝이는 제품을 얼굴에 발라요.", "ex_en": "But now they apply glitter or shiny products on their face."}, {"name": "~도", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Additive particle meaning ''also, too.'' 한국에서도 = ''in Korea as well / Korea too''.", "ex_ko": "한국에서도 이런 트렌드가 인기예요.", "ex_en": "This trend is also popular in Korea."}, {"name": "~는 것을", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Nominalization converting the clause into an object. 반짝이다 + ~는 것 = ''the thing that sparkles / shiny stuff''.", "ex_ko": "젊은 사람들이 아이섀도우나 립글로스에 반짝이는 것을 많이 써요.", "ex_en": "Young people use a lot of shiny eyeshadow or lip gloss."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 것이다 (will)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Talks about the future or a prediction. 이어지다 → 이어질 것이다 = will continue.", "ex_ko": "뷰티 전문가들은 이 트렌드가 계속 이어질 것이라고 말해요.", "ex_en": "Beauty experts say that this trend will continue."}, {"name": "~(이)라고 말하다 (to say that ~)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Reports what someone says. 것이다 → 것이라고 말해요 = say that (it) will ...", "ex_ko": "뷰티 전문가들은 이 트렌드가 계속 이어질 것이라고 말해요.", "ex_en": "Beauty experts say that this trend will continue."}, {"name": "~게 하다 (to make someone/something ~)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Means to cause someone or something to do or be. 보이다 → 보이게 하다 = to make (people) look (bright and pretty).", "ex_ko": "반짝이 메이크업은 사람들을 더 밝고 예쁘게 보이게 해줘요.", "ex_en": "Sparkly makeup makes people look brighter and prettier."}, {"name": "~아/어 주다 (to do for someone)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Shows that an action benefits someone. 하다 → 해 주다 → 해줘요 = does (it) for (them).", "ex_ko": "반짝이 메이크업은 사람들을 더 밝고 예쁘게 보이게 해줘요.", "ex_en": "Sparkly makeup makes people look brighter and prettier."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'moifiwou7p6a' and md5(translation) = '271b56093ed005a1c8ce726cd20ecff0';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["In July 1976, something special happened in Philadelphia, USA. An American Legion convention was held at the Bellevue-Stratford Hotel.", "However, people who attended the convention suddenly got pneumonia. Many people got sick with the same symptoms. Doctors worked hard to find the cause of this disease.", "Later, scientists discovered a new bacterium. People got sick because of this bacterium. So this disease came to be called ''Legionnaires'' disease''.", "Legionnaires'' disease still occurs occasionally today. Bacteria can grow in air conditioners or hot water facilities. That''s why building management is very important."], "sentences": [{"text": "1976년 7월, 미국 필라델피아에서 특별한 일이 일어났어요.", "translation": "In July 1976, something special happened in Philadelphia, United States.", "vocab": [{"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special"}, {"ko": "일", "en": "event; thing"}, {"ko": "일어나다", "en": "to happen; to occur"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past tense)", "exp": "Marks a completed past action. 일어나다 → 일어났어요 = happened.", "example_in_sentence": "일어났어요"}]}, {"text": "벨뷰-스트래트포드 호텔에서 재향군인회(American Legion) 대회가 열렸어요.", "translation": "An American Legion conference was held at the Bellevue-Stratford Hotel.", "vocab": [{"ko": "호텔", "en": "hotel"}, {"ko": "대회", "en": "conference; convention"}, {"ko": "열리다", "en": "to be held; to open"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past tense)", "exp": "Marks a completed past action. 열리다 → 열렸어요 = was held.", "example_in_sentence": "열렸어요"}]}, {"text": "그런데 대회에 참석한 사람들이 갑자기 폐렴에 걸렸어요.", "translation": "However, people who attended the conference suddenly got pneumonia.", "vocab": [{"ko": "참석하다", "en": "to attend"}, {"ko": "갑자기", "en": "suddenly"}, {"ko": "폐렴", "en": "pneumonia"}, {"ko": "걸리다", "en": "to catch; to contract (a disease)"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past noun modifier)", "exp": "Describes the noun with a past action. 참석하다 → 참석한 사람들 = people who attended.", "example_in_sentence": "참석한"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past tense)", "exp": "Marks a completed past action. 걸리다 → 걸렸어요 = caught (an illness).", "example_in_sentence": "걸렸어요"}]}, {"text": "많은 사람들이 같은 증상으로 아팠어요.", "translation": "Many people were sick with the same symptoms.", "vocab": [{"ko": "많다", "en": "to be many; to be a lot"}, {"ko": "같다", "en": "to be the same"}, {"ko": "증상", "en": "symptom"}, {"ko": "아프다", "en": "to be sick; to be ill"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "exp": "Describing words take ~(으)ㄴ before a noun. 같다 → 같은 증상 = the same symptoms.", "example_in_sentence": "같은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로 (because of, with)", "exp": "Here (으)로 marks the cause. 같은 증상으로 아팠어요 = were sick with the same symptoms.", "example_in_sentence": "증상으로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past tense)", "exp": "Marks a past state. 아프다 → 아팠어요 = were sick (the 으 drops).", "example_in_sentence": "아팠어요"}]}, {"text": "의사들은 이 병의 원인을 찾기 위해 노력했어요.", "translation": "Doctors tried to find the cause of this disease.", "vocab": [{"ko": "의사", "en": "doctor"}, {"ko": "병", "en": "disease; illness"}, {"ko": "원인", "en": "cause"}, {"ko": "찾다", "en": "to find; to search"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~기 위해 (in order to)", "exp": "Shows purpose. 찾다 → 찾기 위해 = in order to find.", "example_in_sentence": "찾기 위해"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past tense)", "exp": "Marks a completed past action. 노력하다 → 노력했어요 = tried hard.", "example_in_sentence": "노력했어요"}]}, {"text": "나중에 과학자들이 새로운 세균을 발견했어요.", "translation": "Later, scientists discovered a new bacterium.", "vocab": [{"ko": "나중에", "en": "later"}, {"ko": "과학자", "en": "scientist"}, {"ko": "새롭다", "en": "to be new"}, {"ko": "세균", "en": "bacterium; germ"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "exp": "Describing words take ~(으)ㄴ before a noun. 새롭다 (ㅂ irregular) → 새로운 세균 = a new bacterium.", "example_in_sentence": "새로운"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past tense)", "exp": "Marks a completed past action. 발견하다 → 발견했어요 = discovered.", "example_in_sentence": "발견했어요"}]}, {"text": "이 세균 때문에 사람들이 아팠던 거예요.", "translation": "It was because of this bacterium that people got sick.", "vocab": [{"ko": "세균", "en": "bacterium; germ"}, {"ko": "때문에", "en": "because of; due to"}, {"ko": "아프다", "en": "to be sick; to be ill"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었던 거예요 (that''s why ~ was)", "exp": "Explains the real reason behind a past situation. 아프다 → 아팠던 거예요 = (that''s why) people were sick.", "example_in_sentence": "아팠던 거예요"}]}, {"text": "그래서 이 병을 ''레지오넬라병(Legionnaires'' disease)''이라고 부르게 되었어요.", "translation": "So this disease came to be called ''Legionnaires'' disease.''", "vocab": [{"ko": "그래서", "en": "so; therefore"}, {"ko": "병", "en": "disease; illness"}, {"ko": "부르다", "en": "to call; to name"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(이)라고 부르다 (to call it ~)", "exp": "Gives the name people use for something. 레지오넬라병이라고 부르다 = to call it Legionnaires'' disease.", "example_in_sentence": "이라고 부르게"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~게 되다", "exp": "Auxiliary construction indicating ''come to; begin to''. Verb stem 부르 + ~게 되다 → 부르게 되었어요.", "example_in_sentence": "부르게 되었어요"}]}, {"text": "레지오넬라병은 지금도 가끔 발생해요.", "translation": "Legionnaires'' disease still occurs occasionally even now.", "vocab": [{"ko": "지금", "en": "now"}, {"ko": "가끔", "en": "occasionally; sometimes"}, {"ko": "발생하다", "en": "to occur; to happen"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~도", "exp": "Additive particle meaning ''also; even''. Attaches to 지금.", "example_in_sentence": "지금도"}]}, {"text": "에어컨이나 온수 시설에서 세균이 자랄 수 있어요.", "translation": "Bacteria can grow in air conditioning or hot water facilities.", "vocab": [{"ko": "에어컨", "en": "air conditioner"}, {"ko": "온수", "en": "hot water"}, {"ko": "시설", "en": "facility"}, {"ko": "세균", "en": "bacterium; germ"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~이나", "exp": "Alternative particle meaning ''or; or else''. Connects 에어컨 and 온수 시설.", "example_in_sentence": "에어컨이나"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다 (can)", "exp": "Expresses possibility. 자라다 → 자랄 수 있어요 = can grow.", "example_in_sentence": "자랄 수 있어요"}]}, {"text": "그래서 건물 관리가 매우 중요해요.", "translation": "Therefore, building management is very important.", "vocab": [{"ko": "그래서", "en": "so; therefore"}, {"ko": "건물", "en": "building"}, {"ko": "관리", "en": "management"}, {"ko": "매우", "en": "very; greatly"}], "analysis": []}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special", "note": ""}, {"ko": "일", "en": "event; thing", "note": ""}, {"ko": "일어나다", "en": "to happen; to occur", "note": ""}, {"ko": "호텔", "en": "hotel", "note": ""}, {"ko": "대회", "en": "conference; convention", "note": ""}, {"ko": "열리다", "en": "to be held; to open", "note": ""}, {"ko": "참석하다", "en": "to attend", "note": ""}, {"ko": "갑자기", "en": "suddenly", "note": ""}, {"ko": "폐렴", "en": "pneumonia", "note": ""}, {"ko": "걸리다", "en": "to catch; to contract (a disease)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "많다", "en": "to be many; to be a lot", "note": ""}, {"ko": "같다", "en": "to be the same", "note": ""}, {"ko": "증상", "en": "symptom", "note": ""}, {"ko": "아프다", "en": "to be sick; to be ill", "note": ""}, {"ko": "의사", "en": "doctor", "note": ""}, {"ko": "병", "en": "disease; illness", "note": ""}, {"ko": "원인", "en": "cause", "note": ""}, {"ko": "찾다", "en": "to find; to search", "note": ""}, {"ko": "나중에", "en": "later", "note": ""}, {"ko": "과학자", "en": "scientist", "note": ""}, {"ko": "새롭다", "en": "to be new", "note": ""}, {"ko": "세균", "en": "bacterium; germ", "note": ""}, {"ko": "때문에", "en": "because of; due to", "note": ""}, {"ko": "그래서", "en": "so; therefore", "note": ""}, {"ko": "부르다", "en": "to call; to name", "note": ""}, {"ko": "지금", "en": "now", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가끔", "en": "occasionally; sometimes", "note": ""}, {"ko": "발생하다", "en": "to occur; to happen", "no