": "to request; to ask for", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사실", "en": "fact; (사실은) actually", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이용하다", "en": "to use; to take advantage of", "note": ""}, {"ko": "깨닫다", "en": "to realize; to understand; to grasp", "note": ""}, {"ko": "관계", "en": "relationship; connection", "note": ""}, {"ko": "정리하다", "en": "to end (a relationship); to sort out", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이제", "en": "now; from now on; henceforth", "note": ""}, {"ko": "인생", "en": "life; lifetime", "note": ""}, {"ko": "살아가다", "en": "to live; to go on living", "note": ""}, {"ko": "진정하다", "en": "to be true; to be genuine", "note": ""}, {"ko": "우정", "en": "friendship", "note": ""}, {"ko": "서로", "en": "each other; mutually; one another", "note": ""}, {"ko": "존중하다", "en": "to respect; to honor", "note": ""}, {"ko": "한쪽", "en": "one side; one party", "note": ""}, {"ko": "건강하다", "en": "to be healthy", "note": ""}, {"word": "도우다", "reading": "doudda", "meaning": "to help; to assist", "context": "어려운 상황에 있는 친구를 도우려고 했어요"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~(으)려고 하다 (to try to, intend to)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Shows an intention or attempt. 돕다 (ㅂ irregular) → 도우려고 했어요 = tried to help.", "ex_ko": "한 여성이 어려운 상황에 있는 친구를 도우려고 했어요.", "ex_en": "A woman tried to help a friend who was in a difficult situation."}, {"name": "~게 되다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Indicates a change of state or realization that occurs naturally. 알다 (to know) + 게 되다 (come to) = came to know.", "ex_ko": "하지만 친구의 진짜 목적을 알게 되었어요.", "ex_en": "However, she came to know the friend''s real purpose."}, {"name": "~지만", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Conjunctive ending expressing contrast between two clauses. Shows contradiction or unexpected turn.", "ex_ko": "친구는 도움을 요청했지만, 사실은 다른 목적이 있었어요.", "ex_en": "The friend asked for help, but in fact had a different purpose."}, {"name": "~았/었어요", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Past tense in polite register.", "ex_ko": "친구는 도움을 요청했지만, 사실은 다른 목적이 있었어요.", "ex_en": "The friend asked for help, but in fact had a different purpose."}, {"name": "~ㄴ/는다는 것 (the fact that ~)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Turns a statement into a noun phrase. 이용하려고 한다 → 이용하려고 한다는 것을 깨닫다 = to realize that (she) was trying to use (her).", "ex_ko": "여성은 친구가 자신을 이용하려고 한다는 것을 깨달았어요.", "ex_en": "The woman realized that the friend was trying to use her."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ 후 (after ~ing)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Shows that one action comes after another. 알게 되다 → 알게 된 후 = after (she) found out.", "ex_ko": "이 일을 알게 된 후, 여성은 친구와의 관계를 정리하기로 했어요.", "ex_en": "After coming to know about this matter, the woman decided to end the relationship with the friend."}, {"name": "~기로 하다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Expresses decision or resolution to do something. ~기로 (decide to) + 하다 = decided to.", "ex_ko": "이 일을 알게 된 후, 여성은 친구와의 관계를 정리하기로 했어요.", "ex_en": "After coming to know about this matter, the woman decided to end the relationship with the friend."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 거예요 (will)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Talks about a future plan. 살아가다 → 살아갈 거예요 = will live.", "ex_ko": "그녀는 \"이제 내 인생을 살아갈 거예요\"라고 말했어요.", "ex_en": "She said, \"Now I will live my own life.\""}, {"name": "~(이)라고 말하다 (direct quote)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Comes right after a direct quote. \"...\"라고 말했어요 = said, \"...\".", "ex_ko": "그녀는 \"이제 내 인생을 살아갈 거예요\"라고 말했어요.", "ex_en": "She said, \"Now I will live my own life.\""}, {"name": "~는 관계", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Present participle attributive form. ~는 (which; that does) describes the noun 관계 (relationship).", "ex_ko": "진정한 우정은 서로를 존중하는 관계예요.", "ex_en": "True friendship is a relationship in which both people respect each other."}, {"name": "~예요", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Polite present tense copula. ~예요 is informal polite form of 이다 (to be).", "ex_ko": "진정한 우정은 서로를 존중하는 관계예요.", "ex_en": "True friendship is a relationship in which both people respect each other."}, {"name": "~(으)면 (if)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Sets up a condition. 하다 → 하면 = if (one) does.", "ex_ko": "한쪽이 다른 쪽을 이용하려고 하면 건강한 관계가 아니에요.", "ex_en": "If one side tries to use the other, it is not a healthy relationship."}, {"name": "~이/가 아니에요 (is not)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "The polite form of 아니다 (to not be). 건강한 관계가 아니에요 = it is not a healthy relationship.", "ex_ko": "한쪽이 다른 쪽을 이용하려고 하면 건강한 관계가 아니에요.", "ex_en": "If one side tries to use the other, it is not a healthy relationship."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mok10lk4tady' and md5(translation) = '22baae1b7780768ed445c787067d6665';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["During China''s Han Dynasty, there was a prince named Liu He. He was removed from the throne just 27 days after becoming emperor. The reason Liu He stepped down from the imperial throne is surprising. It''s because he committed 1,127 mistakes in just 27 days. On average, he caused more than 40 problems per day. At the time, court officials meticulously recorded his actions. It is said that he drank too much alcohol and neglected state affairs. Additionally, he disregarded the etiquette and propriety that he should have maintained as emperor. Ultimately, the court removed him from the imperial throne. Liu He is one of the shortest-reigning emperors in Chinese history. This incident became a historical lesson demonstrating the weight of power.", "Korean Teacher Shortage Becomes Serious, School Classes Disrupted", "What is an \"anxiety bag\"? A Popular Trend", "The United States and China Resume Talks Over Trade Issues", "\"Talking Pig\" Becomes SNS Star", "Apple Greatly Improves iPhone Speed with New AI Chip"], "sentences": [{"text": "중국 한나라 시대에 류허(劉賀)라는 왕자가 있었어요.", "translation": "There was a prince named Liu He during the Han Dynasty of China.", "vocab": [{"ko": "한나라", "en": "Han Dynasty"}, {"ko": "왕자", "en": "prince"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(이)라는", "exp": "Attributive form marking apposition or naming; connects a name/identity to the noun it modifies. 류허 (name) + 라는 → describing 왕자.", "example_in_sentence": "류허(劉賀)라는 왕자"}]}, {"text": "그는 황제가 된 지 27일 만에 왕좌에서 쫓겨났습니다.", "translation": "He was driven from the throne only 27 days after becoming emperor.", "vocab": [{"ko": "황제", "en": "emperor"}, {"ko": "왕좌", "en": "throne"}, {"ko": "쫓겨나다", "en": "to be driven out; to be expelled"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~(으)ㄴ 지 ~ 만에 (only ~ after doing)", "exp": "Shows how soon something happened after an event. 되다 → 된 지 27일 만에 = 27 days after becoming (emperor).", "example_in_sentence": "황제가 된 지 27일 만에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서 (ablative location)", "exp": "Marks the location/source from which movement occurs. 왕좌 + 에서 (expelled from).", "example_in_sentence": "왕좌에서 쫓겨났습니다"}]}, {"text": "류허가 황제 자리에서 물러난 이유는 놀라워요.", "translation": "The reason Liu He stepped down from the emperor''s position is surprising.", "vocab": [{"ko": "물러나다", "en": "to step down; to withdraw"}, {"ko": "이유", "en": "reason"}, {"ko": "놀랍다", "en": "to be surprising; to be astonishing"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past noun modifier)", "exp": "Describes the noun with a past action. 물러나다 → 물러난 이유 = the reason (he) stepped down.", "example_in_sentence": "물러난 이유"}]}, {"text": "단 27일 동안 1,127가지의 잘못을 저질렀기 때문이에요.", "translation": "It is because he committed 1,127 kinds of wrongdoings in just 27 days.", "vocab": [{"ko": "잘못", "en": "wrongdoing; mistake"}, {"ko": "저지르다", "en": "to commit (a crime/mistake)"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~ 동안", "exp": "Marks duration or time span during which an action occurs. 27일 (27 days) + 동안.", "example_in_sentence": "27일 동안"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었기 때문이다 (it is because ~)", "exp": "Gives the reason for the previous sentence. 저지르다 → 저질렀기 때문이에요 = it is because (he) committed.", "example_in_sentence": "저질렀기 때문이에요"}]}, {"text": "하루에 평균 40개가 넘는 문제를 일으킨 셈입니다.", "translation": "This amounts to causing over 40 problems per day on average.", "vocab": [{"ko": "평균", "en": "average"}, {"ko": "넘다", "en": "to exceed; to go over"}, {"ko": "일으키다", "en": "to cause; to bring about"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (present noun modifier)", "exp": "Describes the noun that follows. 넘다 → 40개가 넘는 문제 = more than 40 problems.", "example_in_sentence": "넘는 문제"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ 셈이다 (it amounts to ~)", "exp": "Used when a calculation shows what something comes to. 일으키다 → 일으킨 셈입니다 = it amounts to having caused.", "example_in_sentence": "일으킨 셈입니다"}]}, {"text": "당시 조정 신하들은 그의 행동을 자세히 기록했어요.", "translation": "At that time, court officials recorded his actions in detail.", "vocab": [{"ko": "당시", "en": "at that time; then"}, {"ko": "조정", "en": "court (imperial)"}, {"ko": "신하", "en": "official; courtier"}, {"ko": "행동", "en": "action; conduct"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "술을 너무 많이 마시고 국정을 소홀히 했다고 전해집니다.", "translation": "It is said that he drank too much alcohol and neglected state affairs.", "vocab": [{"ko": "술", "en": "alcohol"}, {"ko": "국정", "en": "state affairs; national politics"}, {"ko": "소홀히 하다", "en": "to neglect; to be careless"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 (and)", "exp": "Joins two actions. 마시다 → 마시고 = drank and (neglected ...).", "example_in_sentence": "마시고 국정을 소홀히 했다"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~다고 전해지다", "exp": "Passive-voice hearsay construction: ''it is said/reported that...''. Past form + 다고 전해집니다.", "example_in_sentence": "했다고 전해집니다"}]}, {"text": "또한 황제로서 지켜야 할 예의(禮儀)도 무시했어요.", "translation": "Also, he disregarded the etiquette that should be observed as an emperor.", "vocab": [{"ko": "지키다", "en": "to observe; to keep"}, {"ko": "예의", "en": "etiquette; courtesy; propriety"}, {"ko": "무시하다", "en": "to disregard; to ignore"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어야 할 + noun (that should be ~)", "exp": "Describes a noun with an obligation. 지키다 → 지켜야 할 예의 = etiquette that should be observed.", "example_in_sentence": "지켜야 할 예의"}]}, {"text": "결국 조정에서는 그를 황제 자리에서 내쫓았습니다.", "translation": "In the end, the court drove him out from the emperor''s position.", "vocab": [{"ko": "결국", "en": "in the end; after all; ultimately"}, {"ko": "조정", "en": "court (imperial)"}, {"ko": "내쫓다", "en": "to drive out; to expel"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서 (organization as subject)", "exp": "With an organization or group, 에서 can mark who does the action. 조정에서는 그를 내쫓았습니다 = the court drove him out.", "example_in_sentence": "조정에서는"}]}, {"text": "류허는 중국 역사상 가장 짧은 기간 동안 황제를 한 인물 중 하나예요.", "translation": "Liu He is one of the historical figures who served as emperor for the shortest period in Chinese history.", "vocab": [{"ko": "역사상", "en": "in history; throughout history"}, {"ko": "기간", "en": "period; duration"}, {"ko": "인물", "en": "figure; person (of note)"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "exp": "Describing words take ~(으)ㄴ before a noun. 짧다 → 가장 짧은 기간 = the shortest period.", "example_in_sentence": "짧은 기간"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~ 중 하나", "exp": "Idiomatic expression meaning ''one of...''. 인물 + 중 하나.", "example_in_sentence": "인물 중 하나"}]}, {"text": "이 사건은 권력의 무거움을 보여주는 역사적 교훈이 되었습니다.", "translation": "This event became a historical lesson demonstrating the weight of power.", "vocab": [{"ko": "사건", "en": "event; incident"}, {"ko": "권력", "en": "power; authority"}, {"ko": "무거움", "en": "heaviness; gravity; weight (metaphorical)"}, {"ko": "교훈", "en": "lesson; moral; instruction"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (attributive present)", "exp": "Present tense attributive ending on verbs; modifies following noun. 보여주 + 는 → qualifying 교훈.", "example_in_sentence": "보여주는 역사적 교훈"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 되다 (to become ~)", "exp": "Noun + 이/가 되다 = to become something. 교훈이 되었습니다 = became a lesson.", "example_in_sentence": "역사적 교훈이 되었습니다"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "한나라", "en": "Han Dynasty", "note": ""}, {"ko": "왕자", "en": "prince", "note": ""}, {"ko": "황제", "en": "emperor", "note": ""}, {"ko": "왕좌", "en": "throne", "note": ""}, {"ko": "쫓겨나다", "en": "to be driven out; to be expelled", "note": ""}, {"ko": "물러나다", "en": "to step down; to withdraw", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이유", "en": "reason", "note": ""}, {"ko": "놀랍다", "en": "to be surprising; to be astonishing", "note": ""}, {"ko": "잘못", "en": "wrongdoing; mistake", "note": ""}, {"ko": "저지르다", "en": "to commit (a crime/mistake)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "평균", "en": "average", "note": ""}, {"ko": "넘다", "en": "to exceed; to go over", "note": ""}, {"ko": "일으키다", "en": "to cause; to bring about", "note": ""}, {"ko": "당시", "en": "at that time; then", "note": ""}, {"ko": "조정", "en": "court (imperial)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "신하", "en": "official; courtier", "note": ""}, {"ko": "행동", "en": "action; conduct", "note": ""}, {"ko": "술", "en": "alcohol", "note": ""}, {"ko": "국정", "en": "state affairs; national politics", "note": ""}, {"ko": "소홀히 하다", "en": "to neglect; to be careless", "note": ""}, {"ko": "지키다", "en": "to observe; to keep", "note": ""}, {"ko": "예의", "en": "etiquette; courtesy; propriety", "note": ""}, {"ko": "무시하다", "en": "to disregard; to ignore", "note": ""}, {"ko": "결국", "en": "in the end; after all; ultimately", "note": ""}, {"ko": "내쫓다", "en": "to drive out; to expel", "note": ""}, {"ko": "역사상", "en": "in history; throughout history", "note": ""}, {"ko": "기간", "en": "period; duration", "note": ""}, {"ko": "인물", "en": "figure; person (of note)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사건", "en": "event; incident", "note": ""}, {"ko": "권력", "en": "power; authority", "note": ""}, {"ko": "무거움", "en": "heaviness; gravity; weight (metaphorical)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "교훈", "en": "lesson; moral; instruction", "note": ""}, {"word": "저질렀다", "reading": "jeojilreotda", "meaning": "to commit; to perpetrate (past tense of 저지르다)", "context": "1,127가지의 잘못을 저질렀기"}, {"word": "소홀히", "reading": "sohorhi", "meaning": "carelessly; negligently; in a neglectful manner", "context": "국정을 소홀히 했다고"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~(이)라는", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Attributive form marking apposition or naming; connects a name/identity to the noun it modifies. 류허 (name) + 라는 → describing 왕자.", "ex_ko": "중국 한나라 시대에 류허(劉賀)라는 왕자가 있었어요.", "ex_en": "There was a prince named Liu He during the Han Dynasty of China."}, {"name": "~에서 (organization as subject)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "With an organization or group, 에서 can mark who does the action. 조정에서는 그를 내쫓았습니다 = the court drove him out.", "ex_ko": "그는 황제가 된 지 27일 만에 왕좌에서 쫓겨났습니다.", "ex_en": "He was driven from the throne only 27 days after becoming emperor."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ (past noun modifier)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Describes the noun with a past action. 물러나다 → 물러난 이유 = the reason (he) stepped down.", "ex_ko": "류허가 황제 자리에서 물러난 이유는 놀라워요.", "ex_en": "The reason Liu He stepped down from the emperor''s position is surprising."}, {"name": "~았/었기 때문이다 (it is because ~)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Gives the reason for the previous sentence. 저지르다 → 저질렀기 때문이에요 = it is because (he) committed.", "ex_ko": "단 27일 동안 1,127가지의 잘못을 저질렀기 때문이에요.", "ex_en": "It is because he committed 1,127 kinds of wrongdoings in just 27 days."}, {"name": "~는 (present noun modifier)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Present tense attributive ending on verbs; modifies following noun. 보여주 + 는 → qualifying 교훈.", "ex_ko": "하루에 평균 40개가 넘는 문제를 일으킨 셈입니다.", "ex_en": "This amounts to causing over 40 problems per day on average."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ 셈이다 (it amounts to ~)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Used when a calculation shows what something comes to. 일으키다 → 일으킨 셈입니다 = it amounts to having caused.", "ex_ko": "하루에 평균 40개가 넘는 문제를 일으킨 셈입니다.", "ex_en": "This amounts to causing over 40 problems per day on average."}, {"name": "~고 (and)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Joins two actions. 마시다 → 마시고 = drank and (neglected ...).", "ex_ko": "술을 너무 많이 마시고 국정을 소홀히 했다고 전해집니다.", "ex_en": "It is said that he drank too much alcohol and neglected state affairs."}, {"name": "~다고 전해지다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Passive-voice hearsay construction: ''it is said/reported that...''. Past form + 다고 전해집니다.", "ex_ko": "술을 너무 많이 마시고 국정을 소홀히 했다고 전해집니다.", "ex_en": "It is said that he drank too much alcohol and neglected state affairs."}, {"name": "~아/어야 할 + noun (that should be ~)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Describes a noun with an obligation. 지키다 → 지켜야 할 예의 = etiquette that should be observed.", "ex_ko": "또한 황제로서 지켜야 할 예의(禮儀)도 무시했어요.", "ex_en": "Also, he disregarded the etiquette that should be observed as an emperor."}, {"name": "~이/가 되다 (to become ~)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Noun + 이/가 되다 = to become something. 교훈이 되었습니다 = became a lesson.", "ex_ko": "이 사건은 권력의 무거움을 보여주는 역사적 교훈이 되었습니다.", "ex_en": "This event became a historical lesson demonstrating the weight of power."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mok119we0y93' and md5(translation) = '1c951a4a1136cd5f5727916f85c1ba90';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["An Italian woman is facing opposition from her fiancé''s family due to her blood type. The woman was preparing to marry a local man.", "The fiancé''s family opposed the marriage, saying the woman''s blood type was not good. In some cultures, people believe that blood type influences personality and destiny.", "This incident shows that even in modern society, traditional beliefs can have a significant impact on people''s lives. Many people are showing critical reactions to such discrimination.", "In Korea, blood type personality theory was also popular in the past. However, recently, individual character and values are being considered more important than such beliefs."], "sentences": [{"text": "이탈리아의 한 여성이 혈액형을 이유로 약혼자 가족의 반대를 받고 있어요.", "translation": "A woman from Italy is facing opposition from her fiancé''s family because of her blood type.", "vocab": [{"ko": "혈액형", "en": "blood type"}, {"ko": "약혼자", "en": "fiancé(e)"}, {"ko": "반대를 받다", "en": "to face opposition; to be opposed"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 이유로 (on the grounds of ~)", "exp": "Gives the reason for an action. 혈액형을 이유로 = because of (her) blood type.", "example_in_sentence": "혈액형을 이유로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있어요", "exp": "Progressive aspect indicating an ongoing action or state. Formed with ~고 있- + ~어요.", "example_in_sentence": "반대를 받고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "이 여성은 현지 남성과 결혼을 준비하고 있었습니다.", "translation": "This woman was preparing for marriage with a local man.", "vocab": [{"ko": "현지", "en": "local; native"}, {"ko": "결혼을 준비하다", "en": "to prepare for marriage"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있었습니다", "exp": "Past progressive aspect. ~고 있- (ongoing action) + ~었- (past) + ~습니다 (formal past).", "example_in_sentence": "준비하고 있었습니다"}]}, {"text": "약혼자의 가족은 여성의 혈액형이 좋지 않다며 결혼을 반대했어요.", "translation": "The fiancé''s family opposed the marriage, saying that the woman''s blood type was not good.", "vocab": [{"ko": "반대하다", "en": "to oppose"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~다며 (saying that ~)", "exp": "Reports what someone said while doing the main action. 좋지 않다 → 좋지 않다며 반대했어요 = opposed (it), saying it was not good.", "example_in_sentence": "좋지 않다며"}]}, {"text": "일부 문화권에서는 혈액형이 성격이나 운명에 영향을 준다고 믿습니다.", "translation": "In some cultures, people believe that blood type influences personality and destiny.", "vocab": [{"ko": "일부", "en": "some; a part of"}, {"ko": "문화권", "en": "cultural sphere; culture"}, {"ko": "운명", "en": "destiny; fate"}, {"ko": "영향을 주다", "en": "to influence; to have an effect on"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~에 영향을 주다", "exp": "Collocation meaning ''to have an influence/effect on''. 영향 (influence) + 을 (object particle) + 주다 (give).", "example_in_sentence": "영향을 준다"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~다고 믿다", "exp": "Quotative construction. ~다고 marks reported speech/belief, and 믿다 means ''to believe''. Full pattern: V + ~다고 믿다.", "example_in_sentence": "영향을 준다고 믿습니다"}]}, {"text": "이 사건은 현대 사회에서도 전통적인 믿음이 개인의 삶에 큰 영향을 미칠 수 있음을 보여줘요.", "translation": "This case shows that even in modern society, traditional beliefs can have a significant impact on individuals'' lives.", "vocab": [{"ko": "사건", "en": "incident; case; event"}, {"ko": "현대", "en": "modern times; modernity"}, {"ko": "전통적", "en": "traditional"}, {"ko": "미치다", "en": "to have (an effect); to exert"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~에 영향을 미치다", "exp": "Collocation meaning ''to have an influence/effect on''. Similar to 영향을 주다 but with 미치다 (reach/exert).", "example_in_sentence": "영향을 미칠"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다 (can, may)", "exp": "Expresses possibility. 미치다 → 미칠 수 있다 = can have (an effect).", "example_in_sentence": "미칠 수 있음"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㅁ을 보여주다 (to show that ~)", "exp": "~(으)ㅁ turns a clause into a noun, often in formal writing. 있다 → 있음을 보여줘요 = shows that (it) can ...", "example_in_sentence": "미칠 수 있음을 보여줘요"}]}, {"text": "많은 사람들이 이런 차별에 대해 비판적인 반응을 보이고 있습니다.", "translation": "Many people are showing critical reactions to such discrimination.", "vocab": [{"ko": "차별", "en": "discrimination"}, {"ko": "비판적", "en": "critical"}, {"ko": "반응", "en": "reaction; response"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있습니다", "exp": "Progressive aspect in formal polite form. ~고 있- (ongoing) + ~습니다 (formal present).", "example_in_sentence": "보이고 있습니다"}]}, {"text": "한국에서도 과거 혈액형 성격론이 인기를 끌었던 적이 있어요.", "translation": "In Korea too, there was a time when blood type personality theory was popular in the past.", "vocab": [{"ko": "혈액형 성격론", "en": "blood type personality theory"}, {"ko": "인기를 끌다", "en": "to become popular; to gain popularity"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "인기를 끌다", "exp": "Collocation meaning ''to become/gain popularity'' or ''to attract attention''. 인기 (popularity) + 를 (object) + 끌다 (draw/attract).", "example_in_sentence": "인기를 끌었던"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었던 적이 있다 (there was a time when ~)", "exp": "Talks about a past experience or period. 끌다 → 끌었던 적이 있어요 = there was a time when (it) was popular.", "example_in_sentence": "끌었던 적이 있어요"}]}, {"text": "하지만 최근에는 이런 믿음보다 개인의 인격과 가치관이 더 중요하게 여겨지고 있습니다.", "translation": "However, recently, individual character and values are being considered more important than such beliefs.", "vocab": [{"ko": "인격", "en": "character; personality"}, {"ko": "가치관", "en": "values; value system"}, {"ko": "여겨지다", "en": "to be considered; to be regarded"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~게 여겨지다", "exp": "Passive construction with adverbial modifier. ~게 (manner adverbializer) + 여겨지다 (passive of 여기다, to regard). Shows how something is regarded.", "example_in_sentence": "중요하게 여겨지고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있습니다", "exp": "Progressive aspect in formal form indicating an ongoing state or trend. ~고 있- + ~습니다.", "example_in_sentence": "여겨지고 있습니다"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "혈액형", "en": "blood type", "note": ""}, {"ko": "약혼자", "en": "fiancé(e)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "반대를 받다", "en": "to face opposition; to be opposed", "note": ""}, {"ko": "현지", "en": "local; native", "note": ""}, {"ko": "결혼을 준비하다", "en": "to prepare for marriage", "note": ""}, {"ko": "반대하다", "en": "to oppose", "note": ""}, {"ko": "일부", "en": "some; a part of", "note": ""}, {"ko": "문화권", "en": "cultural sphere; culture", "note": ""}, {"ko": "운명", "en": "destiny; fate", "note": ""}, {"ko": "영향을 주다", "en": "to influence; to have an effect on", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사건", "en": "incident; case; event", "note": ""}, {"ko": "현대", "en": "modern times; modernity", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전통적", "en": "traditional", "note": ""}, {"ko": "미치다", "en": "to have (an effect); to exert", "note": ""}, {"ko": "차별", "en": "discrimination", "note": ""}, {"ko": "비판적", "en": "critical", "note": ""}, {"ko": "반응", "en": "reaction; response", "note": ""}, {"ko": "혈액형 성격론", "en": "blood type personality theory", "note": ""}, {"ko": "인기를 끌다", "en": "to become popular; to gain popularity", "note": ""}, {"ko": "인격", "en": "character; personality", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가치관", "en": "values; value system", "note": ""}, {"ko": "여겨지다", "en": "to be considered; to be regarded", "note": ""}, {"word": "성격", "reading": "seong-gyeok", "meaning": "personality; character", "context": "혈액형이 성격이나 운명에 영향을"}, {"word": "성격론", "reading": "seong-gyeok-non", "meaning": "theory of personality; personality typology", "context": "한국에서도 과거 혈액형 성격론이 인기를"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~을/를 이유로 (on the grounds of ~)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Gives the reason for an action. 혈액형을 이유로 = because of (her) blood type.", "ex_ko": "이탈리아의 한 여성이 혈액형을 이유로 약혼자 가족의 반대를 받고 있어요.", "ex_en": "A woman from Italy is facing opposition from her fiancé''s family because of her blood type."}, {"name": "~고 있어요", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Progressive aspect indicating an ongoing action or state. Formed with ~고 있- + ~어요.", "ex_ko": "이탈리아의 한 여성이 혈액형을 이유로 약혼자 가족의 반대를 받고 있어요.", "ex_en": "A woman from Italy is facing opposition from her fiancé''s family because of her blood type."}, {"name": "~고 있었습니다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Past progressive aspect. ~고 있- (ongoing action) + ~었- (past) + ~습니다 (formal past).", "ex_ko": "이 여성은 현지 남성과 결혼을 준비하고 있었습니다.", "ex_en": "This woman was preparing for marriage with a local man."}, {"name": "~다며 (saying that ~)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Reports what someone said while doing the main action. 좋지 않다 → 좋지 않다며 반대했어요 = opposed (it), saying it was not good.", "ex_ko": "약혼자의 가족은 여성의 혈액형이 좋지 않다며 결혼을 반대했어요.", "ex_en": "The fiancé''s family opposed the marriage, saying that the woman''s blood type was not good."}, {"name": "~다고 믿다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Quotative construction. ~다고 marks reported speech/belief, and 믿다 means ''to believe''. Full pattern: V + ~다고 믿다.", "ex_ko": "일부 문화권에서는 혈액형이 성격이나 운명에 영향을 준다고 믿습니다.", "ex_en": "In some cultures, people believe that blood type influences personality and destiny."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다 (can, may)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Expresses possibility. 미치다 → 미칠 수 있다 = can have (an effect).", "ex_ko": "이 사건은 현대 사회에서도 전통적인 믿음이 개인의 삶에 큰 영향을 미칠 수 있음을 보여줘요.", "ex_en": "This case shows that even in modern society, traditional beliefs can have a significant impact on individuals'' lives."}, {"name": "~(으)ㅁ을 보여주다 (to show that ~)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "~(으)ㅁ turns a clause into a noun, often in formal writing. 있다 → 있음을 보여줘요 = shows that (it) can ...", "ex_ko": "이 사건은 현대 사회에서도 전통적인 믿음이 개인의 삶에 큰 영향을 미칠 수 있음을 보여줘요.", "ex_en": "This case shows that even in modern society, traditional beliefs can have a significant impact on individuals'' lives."}, {"name": "~고 있습니다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Progressive aspect in formal form indicating an ongoing state or trend. ~고 있- + ~습니다.", "ex_ko": "많은 사람들이 이런 차별에 대해 비판적인 반응을 보이고 있습니다.", "ex_en": "Many people are showing critical reactions to such discrimination."}, {"name": "~았/었던 적이 있다 (there was a time when ~)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Talks about a past experience or period. 끌다 → 끌었던 적이 있어요 = there was a time when (it) was popular.", "ex_ko": "한국에서도 과거 혈액형 성격론이 인기를 끌었던 적이 있어요.", "ex_en": "In Korea too, there was a time when blood type personality theory was popular in the past."}, {"name": "~게 여겨지다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Passive construction with adverbial modifier. ~게 (manner adverbializer) + 여겨지다 (passive of 여기다, to regard). Shows how something is regarded.", "ex_ko": "하지만 최근에는 이런 믿음보다 개인의 인격과 가치관이 더 중요하게 여겨지고 있습니다.", "ex_en": "However, recently, individual character and values are being considered more important than such beliefs."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mok11yba0nrd' and md5(translation) = '7dce004eb2db33e9fef2979b4af6ea64';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["Until before 1961, people reported that they mostly had friendly experiences when encountering UFOs (unidentified flying objects) and aliens. Aliens were regarded as beings that did not harm people.", "However, when the alien abduction case of the couple Betty Hill and Barney Hill was reported in 1961, the situation changed completely. They claimed to have been abducted by aliens with gray skin, large heads, and black eyes.", "The Hill couple also said that they had lost memories of a period of time. They added new details that the aliens had forcibly conducted medical examinations.", "After this incident, people''s perception of UFOs and aliens changed greatly. The image of the aliens, which had been friendly, became a scary existence. Until now, the characteristics first mentioned by the Hill couple frequently appear in stories of alien abductions."], "sentences": [{"text": "1961년 이전까지 사람들은 UFO(미확인 비행물체)와 외계인을 만나면 대부분 친근한 경험을 했다고 보고했습니다.", "translation": "Before 1961, people who encountered UFOs (unidentified flying objects) and aliens mostly reported having friendly experiences.", "vocab": [{"ko": "미확인", "en": "unidentified; unconfirmed"}, {"ko": "비행물체", "en": "flying object"}, {"ko": "친근하다", "en": "to be friendly; to be familiar"}, {"ko": "보고하다", "en": "to report"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면 (when, if)", "exp": "Sets up a condition or time. 만나다 → 만나면 = when (they) met.", "example_in_sentence": "외계인을 만나면"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었다고 보고하다", "exp": "Past tense ~았/었다 + quotative particle 고 + verb. Marks reported speech of past experience.", "example_in_sentence": "했다고 보고했습니다"}]}, {"text": "외계인들은 사람들에게 해를 끼치지 않는 존재로 여겨졌어요.", "translation": "Extraterrestrials were regarded as beings that did not cause harm to people.", "vocab": [{"ko": "외계인", "en": "extraterrestrial; alien"}, {"ko": "해를 끼치다", "en": "to cause harm; to hurt"}, {"ko": "존재", "en": "existence; being"}, {"ko": "여겨지다", "en": "to be regarded; to be considered"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~지 않는", "exp": "Negative participle form: ~지 않다 in attributive position. Negates an action or property modifying a noun.", "example_in_sentence": "끼치지 않는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로 여겨지다", "exp": "Particle ~(으)로 marking a role/classification + passive verb 여겨지다. Indicates how something is perceived or classified.", "example_in_sentence": "존재로 여겨졌어요"}]}, {"text": "그런데 1961년 베티 힐과 바니 힐 부부의 외계인 납치 사건이 보고되면서 상황이 완전히 바뀌었습니다.", "translation": "However, as the extraterrestrial abduction case involving Betty Hill and Barney Hill was reported in 1961, the situation changed completely.", "vocab": [{"ko": "납치", "en": "abduction; kidnapping"}, {"ko": "사건", "en": "incident; case; event"}, {"ko": "보고되다", "en": "to be reported"}, {"ko": "바뀌다", "en": "to change"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면서 (as, while)", "exp": "Shows that a change happened as another event took place. 보고되다 → 보고되면서 = as (it) was reported.", "example_in_sentence": "보고되면서"}]}, {"text": "이들은 회색 피부에 큰 머리, 검은 눈을 가진 외계인에게 납치당했다고 주장했어요.", "translation": "They claimed that they had been abducted by extraterrestrials with grayish skin, a large head, and black eyes.", "vocab": [{"ko": "회색", "en": "gray; grey"}, {"ko": "피부", "en": "skin"}, {"ko": "납치당하다", "en": "to be abducted; to be kidnapped"}, {"ko": "주장하다", "en": "to claim; to assert"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past noun modifier)", "exp": "Describes the noun that follows. 가지다 → 가진 외계인 = aliens that had (gray skin, a big head and black eyes).", "example_in_sentence": "회색 피부에 큰 머리, 검은 눈을 가진 외계인"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~당하다", "exp": "Passive morpheme suffix. Converts transitive verb 납치하다 into passive 납치당하다 (to be abducted).", "example_in_sentence": "납치당했다고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었다고 주장하다", "exp": "Past tense marker ~았/었다 + quotative 고 + verb. Reports a past claim or assertion.", "example_in_sentence": "납치당했다고 주장했어요"}]}, {"text": "힐 부부는 또한 기억을 잃어버린 시간이 있었다고 말했습니다.", "translation": "The Hill couple also said there was a period of time during which they had lost their memory.", "vocab": [{"ko": "기억", "en": "memory"}, {"ko": "잃어버리다", "en": "to lose; to misplace"}, {"ko": "시간", "en": "time; period"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ 시간 (a time when ~)", "exp": "Describes the time with what happened in it. 잃어버리다 → 잃어버린 시간 = a time when (they) had lost (their memory).", "example_in_sentence": "기억을 잃어버린 시간이 있었다"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었다고 말하다 (said that ~)", "exp": "Reports what someone said about the past. 있다 → 있었다고 말했습니다 = said that there was.", "example_in_sentence": "있었다고 말했습니다"}]}, {"text": "외계인들이 강제로 의학적 검사를 했다는 새로운 내용도 추가했어요.", "translation": "They also added a new detail: that the aliens had forcibly carried out medical examinations.", "vocab": [{"ko": "강제로", "en": "forcibly; by force"}, {"ko": "의학적", "en": "medical"}, {"ko": "검사", "en": "examination; inspection"}, {"ko": "내용", "en": "content; details"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었다는 + noun (the ~ that ...)", "exp": "Turns a past statement into the content of the noun that follows. 하다 → 했다는 새로운 내용 = a new detail that (they) did (it).", "example_in_sentence": "했다는 새로운 내용"}]}, {"text": "이 사건 이후 UFO와 외계인에 대한 사람들의 인식이 크게 달라졌습니다.", "translation": "After this incident, people''s perception of UFOs and extraterrestrials changed significantly.", "vocab": [{"ko": "사건", "en": "incident; case"}, {"ko": "이후", "en": "after; afterwards"}, {"ko": "인식", "en": "perception; awareness"}, {"ko": "달라지다", "en": "to change; to differ"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~에 대한", "exp": "Particle ~에 + postposition 대해 in attributive form. Marks the target or object of an attitude/perception.", "example_in_sentence": "외계인에 대한"}]}, {"text": "친근했던 외계인의 이미지가 무서운 존재로 바뀌게 되었어요.", "translation": "The once-friendly image of aliens came to change into that of frightening beings.", "vocab": [{"ko": "친근하다", "en": "to be friendly; to be familiar"}, {"ko": "이미지", "en": "image"}, {"ko": "무섭다", "en": "to be frightening; to be scary"}, {"ko": "바뀌다", "en": "to change"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었던 (that used to be)", "exp": "Describes a past state that is no longer true. 친근하다 → 친근했던 = (the image) that used to be friendly.", "example_in_sentence": "친근했던"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~게 되다", "exp": "Auxiliary construction indicating a resultant or achieved state. Shows transition or coming-to-be of a condition.", "example_in_sentence": "바뀌게 되었어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로", "exp": "Particle marking role/transformation. Indicates what something becomes or transforms into.", "example_in_sentence": "존재로"}]}, {"text": "현재까지도 외계인 납치 이야기에는 힐 부부가 처음 언급한 특징들이 자주 등장합니다.", "translation": "Even to the present, the characteristics first mentioned by the Hill couple often appear in stories of extraterrestrial abduction.", "vocab": [{"ko": "현재", "en": "the present; now"}, {"ko": "언급하다", "en": "to mention"}, {"ko": "특징", "en": "characteristic; feature"}, {"ko": "등장하다", "en": "to appear; to make an appearance"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past noun modifier)", "exp": "Describes the noun with a past action. 언급하다 → 처음 언급한 특징들 = the features (they) first mentioned.", "example_in_sentence": "처음 언급한 특징들"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "미확인", "en": "unidentified; unconfirmed", "note": ""}, {"ko": "비행물체", "en": "flying object", "note": ""}, {"ko": "친근하다", "en": "to be friendly; to be familiar", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보고하다", "en": "to report", "note": ""}, {"ko": "외계인", "en": "extraterrestrial; alien", "note": ""}, {"ko": "해를 끼치다", "en": "to cause harm; to hurt", "note": ""}, {"ko": "존재", "en": "existence; being", "note": ""}, {"ko": "여겨지다", "en": "to be regarded; to be considered", "note": ""}, {"ko": "납치", "en": "abduction; kidnapping", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사건", "en": "incident; case; event", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보고되다", "en": "to be reported", "note": ""}, {"ko": "바뀌다", "en": "to change", "note": ""}, {"ko": "회색", "en": "gray; grey", "note": ""}, {"ko": "피부", "en": "skin", "note": ""}, {"ko": "납치당하다", "en": "to be abducted; to be kidnapped", "note": ""}, {"ko": "주장하다", "en": "to claim; to assert", "note": ""}, {"ko": "기억", "en": "memory", "note": ""}, {"ko": "잃어버리다", "en": "to lose; to misplace", "note": ""}, {"ko": "시간", "en": "time; period", "note": ""}, {"ko": "강제로", "en": "forcibly; by force", "note": ""}, {"ko": "의학적", "en": "medical", "note": ""}, {"ko": "검사", "en": "examination; inspection", "note": ""}, {"ko": "내용", "en": "content; details", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이후", "en": "after; afterwards", "note": ""}, {"ko": "인식", "en": "perception; awareness", "note": ""}, {"ko": "달라지다", "en": "to change; to differ", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이미지", "en": "image", "note": ""}, {"ko": "무섭다", "en": "to be frightening; to be scary", "note": ""}, {"ko": "현재", "en": "the present; now", "note": ""}, {"ko": "언급하다", "en": "to mention", "note": ""}, {"ko": "특징", "en": "characteristic; feature", "note": ""}, {"ko": "등장하다", "en": "to appear; to make an appearance", "note": ""}, {"word": "미확인 비행물체", "reading": "mihewagin bihaengmulche", "meaning": "unidentified flying object; UFO", "context": "UFO(미확인 비행물체)와 외계인을 만나면"}, {"word": "무서운", "reading": "museoun", "meaning": "scary; frightening; fearful", "context": "외계인의 이미지가 무서운 존재로 바뀌게"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~(으)면서 (as, while)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Shows that a change happened as another event took place. 보고되다 → 보고되면서 = as (it) was reported.", "ex_ko": "1961년 이전까지 사람들은 UFO(미확인 비행물체)와 외계인을 만나면 대부분 친근한 경험을 했다고 보고했습니다.", "ex_en": "Before 1961, people who encountered UFOs (unidentified flying objects) and aliens mostly reported having friendly experiences."}, {"name": "~았/었다고 보고하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Past tense ~았/었다 + quotative particle 고 + verb. Marks reported speech of past experience.", "ex_ko": "1961년 이전까지 사람들은 UFO(미확인 비행물체)와 외계인을 만나면 대부분 친근한 경험을 했다고 보고했습니다.", "ex_en": "Before 1961, people who encountered UFOs (unidentified flying objects) and aliens mostly reported having friendly experiences."}, {"name": "~지 않는", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Negative participle form: ~지 않다 in attributive position. Negates an action or property modifying a noun.", "ex_ko": "외계인들은 사람들에게 해를 끼치지 않는 존재로 여겨졌어요.", "ex_en": "Extraterrestrials were regarded as beings that did not cause harm to people."}, {"name": "~(으)로 여겨지다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Particle ~(으)로 marking a role/classification + passive verb 여겨지다. Indicates how something is perceived or classified.", "ex_ko": "외계인들은 사람들에게 해를 끼치지 않는 존재로 여겨졌어요.", "ex_en": "Extraterrestrials were regarded as beings that did not cause harm to people."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ (past noun modifier)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Describes the noun that follows. 가지다 → 가진 외계인 = aliens that had (gray skin, a big head and black eyes).", "ex_ko": "이들은 회색 피부에 큰 머리, 검은 눈을 가진 외계인에게 납치당했다고 주장했어요.", "ex_en": "They claimed that they had been abducted by extraterrestrials with grayish skin, a large head, and black eyes."}, {"name": "~당하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Passive morpheme suffix. Converts transitive verb 납치하다 into passive 납치당하다 (to be abducted).", "ex_ko": "이들은 회색 피부에 큰 머리, 검은 눈을 가진 외계인에게 납치당했다고 주장했어요.", "ex_en": "They claimed that they had been abducted by extraterrestrials with grayish skin, a large head, and black eyes."}, {"name": "~았/었다고 주장하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Past tense marker ~았/었다 + quotative 고 + verb. Reports a past claim or assertion.", "ex_ko": "이들은 회색 피부에 큰 머리, 검은 눈을 가진 외계인에게 납치당했다고 주장했어요.", "ex_en": "They claimed that they had been abducted by extraterrestrials with grayish skin, a large head, and black eyes."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ 시간 (a time when ~)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Describes the time with what happened in it. 잃어버리다 → 잃어버린 시간 = a time when (they) had lost (their memory).", "ex_ko": "힐 부부는 또한 기억을 잃어버린 시간이 있었다고 말했습니다.", "ex_en": "The Hill couple also said there was a period of time during which they had lost their memory."}, {"name": "~았/었다고 말하다 (said that ~)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Reports what someone said about the past. 있다 → 있었다고 말했습니다 = said that there was.", "ex_ko": "힐 부부는 또한 기억을 잃어버린 시간이 있었다고 말했습니다.", "ex_en": "The Hill couple also said there was a period of time during which they had lost their memory."}, {"name": "~았/었다는 + noun (the ~ that ...)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Turns a past statement into the content of the noun that follows. 하다 → 했다는 새로운 내용 = a new detail that (they) did (it).", "ex_ko": "외계인들이 강제로 의학적 검사를 했다는 새로운 내용도 추가했어요.", "ex_en": "They also added a new detail: that the aliens had forcibly carried out medical examinations."}, {"name": "~았/었던 (that used to be)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Describes a past state that is no longer true. 친근하다 → 친근했던 = (the image) that used to be friendly.", "ex_ko": "친근했던 외계인의 이미지가 무서운 존재로 바뀌게 되었어요.", "ex_en": "The once-friendly image of aliens came to change into that of frightening beings."}, {"name": "~게 되다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Auxiliary construction indicating a resultant or achieved state. Shows transition or coming-to-be of a condition.", "ex_ko": "친근했던 외계인의 이미지가 무서운 존재로 바뀌게 되었어요.", "ex_en": "The once-friendly image of aliens came to change into that of frightening beings."}, {"name": "~(으)로", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Particle marking role/transformation. Indicates what something becomes or transforms into.", "ex_ko": "친근했던 외계인의 이미지가 무서운 존재로 바뀌게 되었어요.", "ex_en": "The once-friendly image of aliens came to change into that of frightening beings."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mok12n4q500s' and md5(translation) = '5b1a485c4a2e9a6b6b175ca4e2744d4a';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["A liger is an animal born between a male lion and a female tiger. They have special genetic characteristics.", "Ligers receive growth-promoting genes from their father, the lion. However, their mother, the tiger, does not have the growth-inhibiting gene that female lions possess.", "Because of these genetic traits, ligers continue to grow. This is called genetic gigantism. A liger''s body weight can reach a maximum of 500 kilograms (approximately 1,100 pounds).", "This is a much larger size than typical lions or tigers. This is a unique phenomenon that appears when the two species are mixed."], "sentences": [{"text": "라이거(Liger)는 수사자와 암호랑이 사이에서 태어난 동물입니다.", "translation": "A liger is an animal born from a male lion and a female tiger.", "vocab": [{"ko": "수사자", "en": "male lion"}, {"ko": "암호랑이", "en": "female tiger"}, {"ko": "태어나다", "en": "to be born"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~ 사이에서", "exp": "Indicates a location or context between two entities. Used with nouns to show the space/relationship in which an action occurs.", "example_in_sentence": "수사자와 암호랑이 사이에서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past noun modifier)", "exp": "Describes the noun with a past event. 태어나다 → 태어난 동물 = an animal that was born.", "example_in_sentence": "태어난 동물"}]}, {"text": "이들은 특별한 유전적 특징을 가지고 있어요.", "translation": "They have special genetic characteristics.", "vocab": [{"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special"}, {"ko": "유전적", "en": "genetic"}, {"ko": "특징", "en": "characteristic"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~을/를 가지고 있다", "exp": "Expresses possession or having a quality. Object particle ~을/를 marks what is possessed, and 있다 indicates the state of possession.", "example_in_sentence": "특별한 유전적 특징을 가지고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "라이거는 아버지인 사자로부터 성장을 촉진하는 유전자를 받습니다.", "translation": "Ligers receive genes that promote growth from their father, the lion.", "vocab": [{"ko": "아버지", "en": "father"}, {"ko": "성장", "en": "growth"}, {"ko": "촉진하다", "en": "to promote; to accelerate"}, {"ko": "유전자", "en": "gene"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~인 (attributive copula)", "exp": "The copula ~인 functions as an attributive marker connecting 아버지 to 사자, meaning ''father who is a lion''. Shows apposition or identification.", "example_in_sentence": "아버지인 사자"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (present noun modifier)", "exp": "Describes what the noun does. 촉진하다 → 성장을 촉진하는 유전자 = genes that promote growth.", "example_in_sentence": "성장을 촉진하는 유전자"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~로부터 (source particle)", "exp": "Marks the source or origin of an action. Indicates where something comes from or originates.", "example_in_sentence": "아버지인 사자로부터"}]}, {"text": "하지만 어머니인 호랑이에게는 암사자가 가진 성장 억제 유전자가 없어요.", "translation": "However, the mother, the tiger, does not have the growth-suppressing genes that female lions have.", "vocab": [{"ko": "어머니", "en": "mother"}, {"ko": "암사자", "en": "female lion"}, {"ko": "억제", "en": "suppression; inhibition"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (noun modifier)", "exp": "Describes the noun that follows. 가지다 → 암사자가 가진 유전자 = the genes that female lions have.", "example_in_sentence": "암사자가 가진 성장 억제 유전자"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에게는 (as for ~, has)", "exp": "With 있다/없다, 에게 marks who has something; 는 adds contrast. 호랑이에게는 ... 없어요 = the tiger does not have ...", "example_in_sentence": "어머니인 호랑이에게는"}]}, {"text": "이런 유전적 특성 때문에 라이거는 계속해서 자랍니다.", "translation": "Because of these genetic characteristics, ligers continue to grow.", "vocab": [{"ko": "특성", "en": "characteristic; trait"}, {"ko": "계속하다", "en": "to continue"}, {"ko": "자라다", "en": "to grow"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~때문에 (causal particle)", "exp": "Marks the reason or cause of an action. Connects cause to consequence: ''because of; due to''.", "example_in_sentence": "이런 유전적 특성 때문에"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "계속해서 (continuously)", "exp": "계속하다 → 계속해서 works like an adverb meaning ''on and on, continuously''. 계속해서 자랍니다 = keep on growing.", "example_in_sentence": "계속해서"}]}, {"text": "이를 유전적 거대증이라고 불러요.", "translation": "This is called genetic gigantism.", "vocab": [{"ko": "거대증", "en": "gigantism"}, {"ko": "부르다", "en": "to call; to name"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~이라고 부르다", "exp": "Expression meaning ''to call something ~'' or ''to name something ~''. The ~이라고 construction marks the label/name being applied.", "example_in_sentence": "유전적 거대증이라고 불러요"}]}, {"text": "라이거의 몸무게는 최대 500킬로그램(약 1100파운드)까지 나갈 수 있습니다.", "translation": "A liger''s weight can reach up to 500 kilograms (approximately 1100 pounds).", "vocab": [{"ko": "몸무게", "en": "body weight"}, {"ko": "최대", "en": "maximum; at most"}, {"ko": "나가다", "en": "to weigh (an amount)"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~까지", "exp": "Marks the limit or extent of an action/state. ''up to; as far as; to the extent of''.", "example_in_sentence": "500킬로그램까지"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄹ 수 있다 (possibility)", "exp": "Expresses capability or possibility. Combines the future/potential suffix ~ㄹ with the noun 수 (ability) and 있다. 나가다 → 나갈 수 있다.", "example_in_sentence": "나갈 수 있습니다"}]}, {"text": "일반적인 사자나 호랑이보다 훨씬 큰 크기예요.", "translation": "It is a size much larger than ordinary lions or tigers.", "vocab": [{"ko": "일반적", "en": "general; ordinary; typical"}, {"ko": "훨씬", "en": "much; far; significantly"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~적인 (noun modifier from ~적)", "exp": "Words ending in 적 take 인 before a noun. 일반적 → 일반적인 사자 = an ordinary lion.", "example_in_sentence": "일반적인 사자나 호랑이"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~보다 (comparative particle)", "exp": "Marks the standard of comparison. ''more than; compared to; -er than''.", "example_in_sentence": "사자나 호랑이보다"}]}, {"text": "이는 두 종이 섞이면서 나타나는 독특한 현상입니다.", "translation": "This is a unique phenomenon that appears when two species mix.", "vocab": [{"ko": "종", "en": "species"}, {"ko": "섞이다", "en": "to mix; to blend"}, {"ko": "나타나다", "en": "to appear; to manifest"}, {"ko": "독특하다", "en": "to be unique; to be distinctive"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면서 (as, while)", "exp": "Shows something happening as another action takes place. 섞이다 → 섞이면서 = as (the two species) mix.", "example_in_sentence": "섞이면서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (present noun modifier)", "exp": "Describes the noun that follows. 나타나다 → 나타나는 현상 = a phenomenon that appears.", "example_in_sentence": "나타나는 독특한 현상"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "수사자", "en": "male lion", "note": ""}, {"ko": "암호랑이", "en": "female tiger", "note": ""}, {"ko": "태어나다", "en": "to be born", "note": ""}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special", "note": ""}, {"ko": "유전적", "en": "genetic", "note": ""}, {"ko": "특징", "en": "characteristic", "note": ""}, {"ko": "아버지", "en": "father", "note": ""}, {"ko": "성장", "en": "growth", "note": ""}, {"ko": "촉진하다", "en": "to promote; to accelerate", "note": ""}, {"ko": "유전자", "en": "gene", "note": ""}, {"ko": "어머니", "en": "mother", "note": ""}, {"ko": "암사자", "en": "female lion", "note": ""}, {"ko": "억제", "en": "suppression; inhibition", "note": ""}, {"ko": "특성", "en": "characteristic; trait", "note": ""}, {"ko": "계속하다", "en": "to continue", "note": ""}, {"ko": "자라다", "en": "to grow", "note": ""}, {"ko": "거대증", "en": "gigantism", "note": ""}, {"ko": "부르다", "en": "to call; to name", "note": ""}, {"ko": "몸무게", "en": "body weight", "note": ""}, {"ko": "최대", "en": "maximum; at most", "note": ""}, {"ko": "나가다", "en": "to weigh (an amount)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "일반적", "en": "general; ordinary; typical", "note": ""}, {"ko": "훨씬", "en": "much; far; significantly", "note": ""}, {"ko": "종", "en": "species", "note": ""}, {"ko": "섞이다", "en": "to mix; to blend", "note": ""}, {"ko": "나타나다", "en": "to appear; to manifest", "note": ""}, {"ko": "독특하다", "en": "to be unique; to be distinctive", "note": ""}, {"word": "라이거", "reading": "laigeó", "meaning": "liger; offspring of a male lion and female tiger", "context": "라이거(Liger)는 수사자와 암호랑이 사이에서 태어난"}, {"word": "현상", "reading": "hyeonsang", "meaning": "phenomenon; occurrence; event", "context": "두 종이 섞이면서 나타나는 독특한 현상"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~(으)ㄴ (past noun modifier)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Describes the noun that follows. 가지다 → 암사자가 가진 유전자 = the genes that female lions have.", "ex_ko": "라이거(Liger)는 수사자와 암호랑이 사이에서 태어난 동물입니다.", "ex_en": "A liger is an animal born from a male lion and a female tiger."}, {"name": "~인 (attributive copula)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "The copula ~인 functions as an attributive marker connecting 아버지 to 사자, meaning ''father who is a lion''. Shows apposition or identification.", "ex_ko": "라이거는 아버지인 사자로부터 성장을 촉진하는 유전자를 받습니다.", "ex_en": "Ligers receive genes that promote growth from their father, the lion."}, {"name": "~는 (present noun modifier)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Describes what the noun does. 촉진하다 → 성장을 촉진하는 유전자 = genes that promote growth.", "ex_ko": "라이거는 아버지인 사자로부터 성장을 촉진하는 유전자를 받습니다.", "ex_en": "Ligers receive genes that promote growth from their father, the lion."}, {"name": "~로부터 (source particle)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Marks the source or origin of an action. Indicates where something comes from or originates.", "ex_ko": "라이거는 아버지인 사자로부터 성장을 촉진하는 유전자를 받습니다.", "ex_en": "Ligers receive genes that promote growth from their father, the lion."}, {"name": "~에게는 (as for ~, has)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "With 있다/없다, 에게 marks who has something; 는 adds contrast. 호랑이에게는 ... 없어요 = the tiger does not have ...", "ex_ko": "하지만 어머니인 호랑이에게는 암사자가 가진 성장 억제 유전자가 없어요.", "ex_en": "However, the mother, the tiger, does not have the growth-suppressing genes that female lions have."}, {"name": "~때문에 (causal particle)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Marks the reason or cause of an action. Connects cause to consequence: ''because of; due to''.", "ex_ko": "이런 유전적 특성 때문에 라이거는 계속해서 자랍니다.", "ex_en": "Because of these geneti